    notes: "WY added 2026-08-21. Citation: W.S. 1-21-1209. Source: law.justia.com/codes/wyoming/title-1/chapter-21/article-12/section-1-21-1209/. Parallel to CO's edu-identity-change-notice-co, though the WY version is narrower — only binds the successor to the deposit-related duties (1207/1208), not a broader notice-to-tenant duty the way CO's identity-change rule works. | WY: RETRO 2026-10-04 (SOP 1.56, rule 79). BASIS: section-open, official Wyoming Legislature NXT gateway, 2026 Wyoming Statutes, read 2026-10-04 (Art. 12 at /1/53/65, Art. 13 at /1/53/66). Both articles' live text is character-identical to the 2026-09-30 read, so no amendment intervened and no history-line discrepancy arises. VERDICT: confirmed, including the narrowing qualifier. W.S. 1-21-1209 binds the holder of the owner's interest to 'the provisions of W.S. 1-21-1207 and 1-21-1208' only -- the deposit duties -- which is exactly what the row says and why it is narrower than CO's equivalent. Was a host copy; now primary.",
