    notes: "Confirmed absent. Same pattern as Wyoming's edu-no-alt-housing-requirement-wy. | KS CHANGED 2026-10-02, SOP 1.26 retro, targeted fix 18 (SOP rule 78): repointed the dangling coverage pointer from fire-casualty-termination-ks, which the 2026-09-29 three-bucket scrub switched off, to its live successor edu-casualty-termination-ks. CORRECTION TO THE PROMPT'S PREMISE: the prompt said 'Notes only', but this pointer is in bodyText, not notes — the notes field here reads only 'Confirmed absent. Same pattern as Wyoming's edu-no-alt-housing-requirement-wy.' A notes-only sweep would have reported this row clean and left a landlord-facing pointer to a switched-off row. No other text changed. | RULE 79 BASIS UPGRADE: the absence is no longer secondary-source-only. 'alternate housing', 'alternative housing', 'relocation', 'comparable housing' and 'temporary housing' return 26 hits across the corpus and none is in Article 25; the Chapter 58 hits are the relocation-assistance and real-estate-licensing articles. Read section-open 2026-10-02 from a full-text corpus built in the built-in browser from ksrevisor.gov: every section of K.S.A. chapters 12, 16, 16a, 31, 44, 50, 58, 60 and 61 (5,906 sections, 16,345,503 characters, 0 fetch failures), control term 'zqxvbnmwt' 0 hits. Boundary: chapters outside that list were not loaded, and the Kansas Legislature's own statute search indexes section titles and a leading snippet only, so its clean negatives prove nothing about body text (verified: 'periodic rent-paying date' returns 0 results though it is verbatim in K.S.A. 58-2570(b)).",
