    bodyText:
      "If you withhold security deposit money without reasonable justification, North Dakota law makes you liable for treble (triple) damages.",
    notes: "N.D.C.C. § 47-16-07.1(4). | BASIS RECORDED 2026-10-02 (retro, RULE 79). This row's notes carried a citation with no evidentiary basis, so the rule 79 screen could not read it. Basis: the complete text of N.D.C.C. ch. 47-16, read from the official compilation (ndlegis.gov/cencode/t47c16.pdf); §§ 47-16-19, 47-16-20 and 47-16-20.1 were transcribed verbatim from that source on 2026-09-27 and match the chapter text this project has relied on since § 27 of this log, and the chapter was re-read against it on 2026-10-02. Citation and subdivision confirmed; no content change.",
