    topicKey: "dv-confidentiality",
    bodyText:
      "If a tenant terminates under South Dakota's domestic-abuse/stalking early-termination provision and provides the landlord a forwarding address or other contact information, the landlord may not disclose that information to any person except with the tenant's consent or as required by law.",
    notes: "SD session 1. SDCL 43-32-19.2. Same confidentiality-obligation pattern already present for CO (edu-dv-confidentiality-co); confirmed as its own distinct code section for SD rather than folded into 19.1. TITLE NORMALISED 2026-09-19: 'Domestic Abuse Contact Information Confidentiality (South Dakota)' -> 'Domestic Abuse Contact Information Confidentiality' (state name in the title was a per-session convention used only by SD, OH, ND and CO). | Retro checks (SOP 1.24) 2026-10-02 - BASIS RECORDED (rule 79 provenance repair, no substantive change). This row's notes recorded no verification basis, so it could not be screened by keyword. Controlling text read section-open this pass from the official sdlegislature.gov API, whole South Dakota code loaded and ch. 43-32 proved complete against the site's own chapter index (43 of 43): SDCL 43-32-19.2. Confirmed: where a tenant terminating under 43-32-19.1 gives the landlord a forwarding address or other contact information, the landlord may not disclose it except with the tenant's consent or as required by law. Note this section was initially missed by the section parser used this pass because its number and period are separated by a line break; the parser was fixed and the chapter then proved complete at 43 of 43.",
