    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "landlord-entry",
    bodyText:
      "Except in an emergency or where it is impracticable, a South Dakota landlord must give the tenant reasonable notice of intent to enter and may enter only at reasonable times. Twenty-four hours' written notice is presumed reasonable unless the lease sets a different method or timing by mutual agreement. The notice must specify the date(s) of entry, a time period during normal business hours for the entry, the purpose of the entry, and a means by which the tenant may request to reschedule.",
    notes: "SD session 1. SDCL 43-32-32. Structurally close to ND's entry-notice statute (24-hour presumed-reasonable notice, specific content requirements) but SD adds a tenant right to request rescheduling that ND's text (as read in that session) did not explicitly carry - worth a side-by-side note on the checklist rather than treating the two as identical. No fixed 'reasonable hours' window given (unlike MN's 8am-8pm) - SD leaves 'reasonable times' undefined by statute. TITLE NORMALISED 2026-09-19: 'Entry Notice Requirements (South Dakota)' -> 'Entry Notice Requirements' (state name in the title was a per-session convention used only by SD, OH, ND and CO). | Retro checks (SOP 1.24) 2026-10-02 - BASIS RECORDED (rule 79 provenance repair, no substantive change). This row's notes recorded no verification basis, so it could not be screened by keyword. Controlling text read section-open this pass from the official sdlegislature.gov API, whole South Dakota code loaded and ch. 43-32 proved complete against the site's own chapter index (43 of 43): SDCL 43-32-32. Confirmed: reasonable notice and entry at reasonable times except in an emergency or where impracticable; twenty-four hours' written notice is PRESUMED reasonable unless alternate methods or times are mutually agreed in the lease; and the notice must specify the date or dates of entry, a period during normal business hours, the purpose, and a means for the tenant to request rescheduling.",
