    topicKey: "foreclosure",
    bodyText:
      "Federal law (the Protecting Tenants at Foreclosure Act) protects tenants when a rental is foreclosed, and Florida has copied the same rules into a state statute that takes effect only if the federal act is ever repealed. Under these rules, a person who acquires a rental through foreclosure takes it subject to the rights of any bona fide tenant. The new owner must give a bona fide tenant at least 90 days' notice to vacate. A tenant with a bona fide lease made before the notice of foreclosure may stay until the lease ends, unless the new owner sells to a buyer who will live in the unit, and even then the tenant gets the 90-day notice. A tenant without a lease or with an at-will lease also gets the 90-day notice. A tenancy is bona fide only if the tenant is not the former owner or the former owner's child, spouse or parent, the lease was an arm's-length transaction, and the rent is not substantially below market (unless reduced by a subsidy).",
    notes: "FL: Primary text read section-open 2026-09-26 from the official 2026 Florida Statutes (flsenate.gov / leg.state.fl.us), with per-section history lines. Controlling text: Fla. Stat. §83.5615 (s. 2, ch. 2020-99), mirroring the federal PTFA. Longer state or local protections and subsidized-tenancy rules are preserved (§83.5615(2)). Notice-of-foreclosure date defined in (3)(c). No Florida pre-lease foreclosure disclosure to tenants located in Part II (contrast MN, NV). | FL retro 2026-10-03 (SOP 1.30) - TARGETED FIX (found while re-reading ch. 83 for rule 79): the official 2026 text prints a note under §83.5615: 'Section 2, ch. 2020-99, created s. 83.5615 “[e]ffective upon the repeal of the federal Protecting Tenants at Foreclosure Act, Pub. L. No. 111-22.”' Pub. L. 115-174, §304 (read on govinfo.gov) repealed the federal act's sunset and restored §§701-703 effective 30 days after enactment (May 24, 2018). So §83.5615 is not in force; the federal act is. The body now says so. The 90-day notice, lease-survival and bona fide rules are stated as Florida's mirror text gives them; PTFA §§701-703 themselves not read (non-state citation, rule 21). Read section-open 2026-10-03 on the official Online Sunshine text (leg.state.fl.us, 2026 Florida Statutes) in the desktop browser pane; excerpts and page hashes in the FL retro sources (lease-clause-decision-log-FL.md, Retro checks (SOP 1.30)).",
