      "Florida statutes do not provide for sealing or expunging eviction court records. Florida's court rules have no eviction-specific sealing rule either; a party may ask the court to make specific information confidential under the general court-records rule. Eviction filings remain public records that tenant-screening companies may report, subject to federal credit-reporting law.",
