      "New Jersey requires the owner of a rental unit to carry liability insurance of at least $500,000 for combined property damage and bodily injury, or at least $300,000 for an owner-occupied multifamily home of four or fewer units. Owners must register the certificate of insurance with the municipality each year. A municipality can fine a noncompliant owner $500 to $5,000.",
