      "Ohio has no statewide domestic violence lease-termination right, no DV anti-termination protection, and no DV lock-change duty. A survivor who leaves early remains liable on the lease under ordinary contract principles, and a landlord may pursue the remaining rent, subject only to the common-law duty to mitigate. Seven other states in this library give the survivor a statutory release; Ohio does not. Tenants in federally subsidised housing are covered by the federal Violence Against Women Act instead, which is a separate regime.",
