      "North Carolina has no statute or court rule allowing summary ejectment records to be sealed or expunged. Court records are open to public inspection unless a law closes them, and the court system licenses remote and bulk access to civil case data, which includes eviction cases. A party may ask the court to seal a particular document under the general court rules, but nothing provides for sealing an eviction case as a whole.",
