    bodyText:
      "If a landlord is the utility's customer for gas, electric, steam, water or sewer serving tenants, the utility must give the landlord 37 days' written notice before shutting service off for nonpayment and must notify the tenants at least 30 days ahead. The landlord must give the utility the tenants' names and addresses within 7 days of a request unless it pays or arranges to pay; failing to do so costs $500 to $1,000 a day in liquidated damages. Tenants may pay the bill for the last month to keep service on, then deduct what they paid from rent or recover it from the landlord. A landlord may not retaliate against them. A landlord who asks the utility to end service must certify that the units are vacant or the tenants consent, have the tenants tell the utility they consent, or give the utility the tenants' names so it can notify them. Owners of rental buildings with units that are not individually metered must tell each utility that the property is rented, and they remain responsible for the bills. A utility two or more months unpaid may ask the court to appoint a receiver to collect rents. Tenants cannot waive these rights. Separately, where a municipal authority or a third class city supplies water or sewer service through a tenant's own account at a unit the owner does not live in, the owner can be made to pay the tenant's unpaid bill if the authority or city notifies both the owner and the tenant within 30 days after the bill first becomes overdue; for water, the owner is not liable for service more than 90 days after it became overdue unless a court order stopped the shutoff.",
    notes: "PA: Read section-open 2026-09-29 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official site (palegis.us) and, for court rules and regulations, the official Pennsylvania Code site (pacodeandbulletin.gov): The Landlord and Tenant Act of 1951 (1951 P.L. 69, No. 20) read whole from the official unconsolidated-statute text with every amendment note (newest: Act 88 of 2024, 2024 P.L. 944); the Pennsylvania Constitution and all 74 titles of the Pennsylvania Consolidated Statutes (75 files) loaded from the official title files (29.28 million characters; revision stamps 2022-03-07 to 2026-09-16) and searched whole; all 262 acts of 2024, 2025 and 2026 screened in full text for landlord-tenant terms; no special-session act in 2024-2026 (PA log §1). P.S. numbers are Purdon's, which the official site does not print; each 1951-Act cite gives the Act section in parentheses (kickoff rule). Controlling text: 66 Pa.C.S. §§ 1521-1533 (Chapter 15 Subchapter B, the Utility Service Tenants Rights Act, as amended by Act 54 of 1993, 1993 P.L. 379; read whole from the official Title 66 text): 66 Pa.C.S. § 1521 definitions ('landlord ratepayer'), 66 Pa.C.S. § 1523 (37 days to the landlord; community agencies 10 days; tenants 30 days; voluntary relinquishment needs vacancy certification or consent), 66 Pa.C.S. § 1524 (tenant list within 7 days), 66 Pa.C.S. § 1525, 66 Pa.C.S. § 1526 (statutory tenant notice in 12-point bold capitals - the utility's duty, not the landlord's), 66 Pa.C.S. § 1527 (continued service), 66 Pa.C.S. § 1528, 66 Pa.C.S. § 1529 (deduct from rent), 66 Pa.C.S. § 1529.1 (owner's duty to notify utilities of rental use where units are not individually metered), 66 Pa.C.S. § 1530 (waiver void), 66 Pa.C.S. § 1531 (retaliation), 66 Pa.C.S. § 1532 (penalties), 66 Pa.C.S. § 1533 (receiver). 66 Pa.C.S. § 1529.1(b) also lists an individually metered unit's account in the owner's name unless the tenant or a representative tells the utility otherwise. Water and sewer owner liability (read section-open): 53 Pa.C.S. § 5607(d)(10) (municipal authority water; 30-day notice to owner and tenant; no owner liability for service 90 or more days after the bill first becomes overdue unless a court order prevented termination), 53 Pa.C.S. § 5607(d)(11) (sewer; owner liable unless the authority fails to give the 30-day notice); 11 Pa.C.S. § 13588(b) (third class cities, water); borough, township and other municipal water systems not read (open item). `rent-payment` ('except as permitted by applicable law') and `utilities-paid-by-landlord` tagged.",
