    bodyText:
      "Pennsylvania's Electronic Transactions Act gives electronic records and signatures legal effect when the parties agree to act electronically. But a paper consumer contract, such as a lease signed on paper, may authorize doing business electronically only if the tenant agrees in a separate and express acknowledgment that says which parts of the transaction will be electronic and how. Using e-payment alone does not show agreement. Federal law separately says electronic delivery cannot replace paper for notices of default or eviction on a primary residence. Pennsylvania's notice-to-quit statute lists its own delivery methods: personal delivery, leaving it at the main building, or conspicuous posting.",
