    bodyText:
      "The Pennsylvania Human Relations Act bars housing discrimination because of race (including hair texture and protective hairstyles), color, familial status, age (40 and over), religious creed, ancestry, sex, national origin, handicap or disability, a known relationship with a person with a disability, or use of a guide or support animal. It adds age to the federal classes. A landlord may not evict before the end of the lease because of pregnancy or the birth of a child, and may not ask questions, keep records or use application forms about protected characteristics. Landlords must allow reasonable modifications at the tenant's expense (with restoration where reasonable) and make reasonable accommodations. Every covered landlord must post the Human Relations Commission's fair practices notice in its place of business. The Act does not cover renting part of an owner-occupied building of no more than two units, a room in a landlord-occupied rooming house with a common entrance, or qualifying housing for older persons. Occupancy limits based on bedrooms and unit size are allowed. Pennsylvania has no statewide source-of-income protection.",
    notes: "PA: Read section-open 2026-09-29 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official site (palegis.us) and, for court rules and regulations, the official Pennsylvania Code site (pacodeandbulletin.gov): The Landlord and Tenant Act of 1951 (1951 P.L. 69, No. 20) read whole from the official unconsolidated-statute text with every amendment note (newest: Act 88 of 2024, 2024 P.L. 944); the Pennsylvania Constitution and all 74 titles of the Pennsylvania Consolidated Statutes (75 files) loaded from the official title files (29.28 million characters; revision stamps 2022-03-07 to 2026-09-16) and searched whole; all 262 acts of 2024, 2025 and 2026 screened in full text for landlord-tenant terms; no special-session act in 2024-2026 (PA log §1). P.S. numbers are Purdon's, which the official site does not print; each 1951-Act cite gives the Act section in parentheses (kickoff rule). Controlling text: 43 P.S. § 954 (Act § 4, definitions: (h) age = 40 or older; (i) 'housing accommodations' excludes a personal residence offered for rent by the owner or lessee; (k) personal residence = no more than two families living independently, used by the owner as a bona fide residence; (t) familial status; (bb) race includes hair texture and protective hairstyles, (cc) protective hairstyle - both added by Act 54 of 2025, 2025 P.L. 331, read in the current text), 43 P.S. § 955(h)(1)-(11) (Act § 5(h): refusal, pregnancy eviction (1.1), terms, modifications (3.1), accommodations (3.2), advertising (5), inquiry and record ban (6), accessibility (7), older-persons and religious exemptions (9)-(10), occupancy standards (11)), 43 P.S. § 955(j) (fair practices notice posting). PHRA read in the official text (1955 P.L. 744, No. 222) for sections 3-5. Sexual orientation and gender identity: PHRC regulations define 'sex' to include them (16 Pa. Code, 2023) - administrative, not read (instruction 16). Source of income: no state class ('source of income' / 'housing choice voucher' searches, PA log §17); Philadelphia and Pittsburgh ordinances out of scope (instruction 20). `permitted-occupants`, `no-alterations` tagged.",
