    topicKey: "security-deposit-return",
    bodyText:
      "Within 30 days after the lease ends and the tenant delivers possession, or after a different starting point North Dakota law sets (such as a domestic-violence termination), return the deposit with any interest the law requires, less lawful deductions, and a written itemization of anything you kept (N.D.C.C. 47-16-07.1). If the deposit goes unclaimed for a year after the lease ends, report and remit it under North Dakota's unclaimed property law (47-30.2-04). See the notes on interest, penalties and domestic-violence timing.",
    notes: "ND: Moved from security-deposit-return-nd by the three-bucket scrub (2026-09-29); content and citation unchanged: N.D.C.C. § 47-16-07.1(1), (3), (4); § 47-16-17.1(8); § 47-30.2-04. | BASIS RECORDED 2026-10-02 (retro, RULE 79 with RULE 78). The 2026-09-29 three-bucket scrub created or moved this row and carried over the content and citation but NOT the evidentiary basis, which stayed behind in the switched-off source row. A row whose notes record no basis cannot be screened, so the scrub quietly removed six ND rows from rule 79's reach. Basis: the complete text of N.D.C.C. ch. 47-16, read from the official compilation (ndlegis.gov/cencode/t47c16.pdf), re-read 2026-10-02; citation and subdivision confirmed, no content change. Reported as a rule 78 defect in this retro's log section: a pass that moves content must move its basis with it.",
