      "If a deposit is more than $50 or one month's rent, whichever is greater, the excess earns interest at 5% a year for any period the tenant stays in possession six months or more. Compute and pay it to the tenant every year. No interest is owed on the part at or below that threshold (R.C. 5321.16(A)).",
    notes: "OH: Moved from security-deposit-interest-oh by the three-bucket scrub (2026-09-29); content and citation unchanged: R.C. 5321.16(A). | 2026-10-02 (SOP 1.23 rules 78 and 79 retro): BASIS CARRIED FORWARD. The 2026-09-29 three-bucket scrub recorded this row's provenance ('moved from'/'created from') and its citation but not its BASIS, so on a rule 79 keyword screen the row read as having none - the same defect rule 78 records for the six rows ND's scrub created. The basis is the source row's and is restated here: R.C. 5321.16(A) was READ SECTION-OPEN on 2026-09-18 and again on 2026-09-27 (effective 1974-11-04, S.B. 103, 110th G.A., never amended); the row's figures - the greater of $50 or one month's periodic rent as the threshold, 5% per annum on the excess only, six months or more in possession, computed and paid annually to the tenant - are read off that text. No content changed; this is a provenance repair, not a re-verification.",
