    notes: "CA: Created by the three-bucket scrub (2026-09-29) from unbundled-parking-ca; content unchanged: Civ. Code s1947.1. | CA: SOP 1.31 retro check 23, 2026-10-03. APPLICABILITY CONFIRMED against Civ. Code s1947.1 as recorded from the original pass's section-open read: s1947.1(e)(2)(A) requires all three of a certificate of occupancy issued on or after 2025-01-01, sixteen or more residential units, and location in one of ten named counties (Alameda, Fresno, Los Angeles, Riverside, Sacramento, San Bernardino, San Joaquin, Santa Clara, Shasta, Ventura); s1947.1(b)(1) parking 'shall not be included in any residential rental agreement' and must sit in an addendum or a separate rental agreement; s1947.1(b)(2) unbundling runs 'for the life of the property', which is what this row's 'permanently' states; s1947.1(c) right of first refusal; s1947.1(d)(1) an unpaid parking fee cannot support an unlawful detainer and (d)(2) allows revocation after 45 days. All four details the prompt asked about are confirmed. ONE WORDING FIX: 'leased separately' now reads so as not to exclude the addendum route the statute expressly allows. CITATION ERROR CORRECTED: the scrub's note cited 'Civ. Code s3485' alongside s1947.1. s3485 is the weapons-nuisance unlawful-detainer section, repealed as of 2024-01-01 by its own subdivision (j), and has nothing to do with parking - a stray citation the scrub carried in. Removed. Found by this retro's citation screen, not by the prompt.",
