      "A tenant who is 60 or older or has a physical or mental disability may end the lease on 30 days' written notice, given within 60 days after relocating, if their condition requires a move for care or treatment that can't be provided in the dwelling; a co-tenant may do the same if also 60 or older or disabled, or if they became a tenant on or after the date the relocating tenant signed (NRS 118A.340). Such a tenant may also end the lease on 60 days' written notice, within three months after the death of their spouse or co-tenant. The notice must set out the facts and, for a relocation, include reasonable verification of the condition and the need to move. A tenant's death does not by itself give you a right to end the lease.",
    notes: "NV: Moved from infirmity-death-termination-nv by the three-bucket scrub (2026-09-29); content and citations unchanged: NRS 118A.340. | NV (retro SOP 1.27, 2026-10-02): Rule 79 provenance repair: basis carried forward from infirmity-death-termination-nv (section-open read of revisor text, leg.state.nv.us, Rev. 4/15/2026, 2026-09-24); the scrub copied the citations but not the basis. Re-read today against the saved text; body unchanged. Read section-open 2026-10-02 in Taylor's built-in browser from leg.state.nv.us (Nevada Revised Statutes 2025/2026 R1; the relied-on chapter pages print Rev. 4/15/2026 and the 36th Special Session (2025) amended none of the sections relied on; whole NRS loaded, 835 chapter pages, 49,746 sections, parser checked complete against every chapter's table of contents); each relied-on section saved with a SHA-256 match to the browser text (NV retro sources).",
