    title: "Disclose Foreclosure Proceedings Before Signing",
    group: "Disclosures",
    states: ["NV"],
    ruleTypes: ["CONDITIONAL"],
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "foreclosure-disclosure",
    bodyText:
      "If the property is the subject of any foreclosure proceedings, you must disclose that in writing to a prospective tenant before they enter into the lease (NRS 118A.275). The law does not require the disclosure to be in the lease or attached to it; give it in writing before the tenant signs, for example in a separate notice. Treat a recorded notice of default as a foreclosure proceeding and disclose it too. A willful failure to disclose is a deceptive trade practice. The lease's optional foreclosure clause records that the disclosure was made, and stating in writing that there are no proceedings is a sensible record, but neither replaces the disclosure before signing.",
    notes: "NV: Created by the three-bucket scrub (2026-09-29) from foreclosure-disclosure-nv; content unchanged: NRS 118A.275; NRS 40.255. | NV (retro SOP 1.27, 2026-10-02): Rule 79 provenance repair: basis carried forward from foreclosure-disclosure-nv (section-open read of revisor text, leg.state.nv.us, Rev. 4/15/2026, 2026-09-24); the scrub copied the citations but not the basis. Re-read today against the saved text; body unchanged. Read section-open 2026-10-02 in Taylor's built-in browser from leg.state.nv.us (Nevada Revised Statutes 2025/2026 R1; the relied-on chapter pages print Rev. 4/15/2026 and the 36th Special Session (2025) amended none of the sections relied on; whole NRS loaded, 835 chapter pages, 49,746 sections, parser checked complete against every chapter's table of contents); each relied-on section saved with a SHA-256 match to the browser text (NV retro sources). | NV (retro SOP 1.47, 2026-10-03): Targeted fix 2: body corrected and completed against NRS 118A.275 read section-open. The old body said 'disclose ... whether' the property is in foreclosure; the statute requires a written disclosure only IF it is ('shall disclose in writing to a prospective tenant if the property ... is the subject of any foreclosure proceedings'). The body now says the disclosure is owed in writing before signing and need not be in or with the lease: the statute has no 'with the rental agreement' or 'in the lease' wording, so the lease is not its vehicle and the clause stays optional. 118A.275(2): a willful violation is a deceptive trade practice under NRS 598.0903-598.0999 (remedies not read, not stated). The open point on whether a recorded notice of default starts a 'foreclosure proceeding' (NRS ch. 107 not read) stands; the body tells landlords to disclose a recorded notice of default too, the safe course. Read section-open 2026-10-03 in Taylor's built-in browser from leg.state.nv.us (ch. 118A page Rev. 4/15/2026, fetched twice with matching SHA-256; wording identical to the copy saved at the 2026-10-02 retro). Section history: 'Added to NRS by 2009, 2791', never amended.",
