    notes: "TX: Created by the three-bucket scrub (2026-09-29) from nsf-fee-limit-tx; content unchanged: Tex. Bus. & Com. Code §3.506. | TX retro 2026-10-03 (SOP 1.29, rule 79 provenance repair): this row was created by the 2026-09-29 scrub and recorded no basis of its own. Basis carried forward from `nsf-fee-limit-tx` (Tex. Bus. & Com. Code §3.506 primary text supplied by Taylor 2026-09-25, read section-open) and re-read section-open 2026-10-03 in the official Business & Commerce Code: §3.506(b) maximum processing fee $30; (c) no fee where a Code Crim. Proc. art. 102.007(e) reimbursement fee was collected, with immediate refund (added to the body; art. 102.007(e) not read); (e) does not affect rights under a written contract (the ambiguity recorded on `nsf-fee-limit-tx` stands). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the official Texas statutes (chapter HTML served by tcss.legis.texas.gov behind statutes.capitol.texas.gov; site current through the 89th Legislature, 2nd Called Session, 2025); the whole Property, Business & Commerce, Civil Practice & Remedies and Finance Codes and the Constitution were loaded, proved complete against the site's chapter lists, saved and hash-matched (TX log, 'Retro checks (SOP 1.29)').",
