    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "surrender-end-of-term",
    bodyText:
      "If a tenant leaves belongings after a warrant for removal is executed, or after giving written notice of voluntarily giving up possession, you may dispose of them only if you reasonably believe the tenant does not intend to claim them, and only as N.J.S.A. 2A:18-72 through 2A:18-84 allow: first send the tenant written notice by certified mail or receipted first-class mail, to the last known address and any other address you know, marked \"Please Forward\"; store the property with reasonable care; and don't sell or dispose of it until the date in the notice, which must be at least 30 days after the notice is delivered or 33 days after mailing, whichever comes first (75 or 78 days for a manufactured or mobile home). The tenant may reclaim it in that time without paying unpaid rent, but must reimburse your reasonable storage and removal costs. If you keep a tenant's property without following these steps, you lose those costs and may owe up to twice the tenant's actual damages.",
    notes: "NJ: Created by the three-bucket scrub (2026-09-29) from surrender-end-of-term-nj; content unchanged: N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.3, 2A:18-72, 2A:18-73, 2A:18-74, 2A:18-75, 2A:18-76, 2A:18-77, 2A:18-78, 2A:18-79, 2A:18-80, 2A:18-81, 2A:18-82, 2A:18-83, 2A:18-84. | NJ: Retro check 2026-10-03 (SOP 1.46), rule 79 (row recorded no basis of its own; created by the scrub). Re-read 2A:18-72 to -84. QUALIFIERS FIXED: 2A:18-72 conditions disposal on the landlord reasonably believing the tenant left with no intention of further claim; 2A:18-74(a) counts \"not less than 30 days after delivery of the notice, or not less than 33 days after the date of mailing, whichever comes first\" (75/78 for manufactured or mobile homes); 2A:18-73 mailing method; 2A:18-82 penalty added. Read section-open 2026-10-03 in the built-in browser on the official NJ Legislature statutes (lis.njleg.state.nj.us, compilation through P.L.2026, c.30); each section fetched twice, heading checked, SHA-256 saved (NJ retro sources, src-1003).",
