    bodyText:
      "If the property's drinking water comes from a private well that no other State law already requires to be tested, have it tested at least once every five years as the Private Well Testing Act requires, give each rental unit a written copy of the results within 30 days of receiving them, and give each new tenant a written copy of the most recent results. For a seasonal rental, you may instead post the results where they are easy to see inside the unit (N.J.S.A. 58:12A-32).",
