      "Any time after rent is due, the landlord may serve a written demand for the rent stating that unless payment is made within a stated time, not less than 5 days after service, the lease will be terminated. If the tenant does not pay within that time, the landlord may treat the lease as ended and file an eviction without further notice or demand, and may join a claim for the rent due. Partial payments of the amount demanded do not invalidate the notice if the notice prominently states: \"Only FULL PAYMENT of the rent demanded in this notice will waive the landlord's right to terminate the lease under this notice, unless the landlord agrees in writing to continue the lease in exchange for receiving partial payment.\" The landlord may agree in writing to continue the lease for a partial payment. Collecting past-due rent after the eviction is filed does not invalidate the suit.",
