      "When a landlord sells, leases, transfers or otherwise disposes of residential property (other than to a lienholder), the new owner becomes liable to the tenant for any security deposit, including statutory interest, and prepaid rent the tenant paid, and the former owner remains jointly and severally liable. When a deposit is actually transferred to the holder of a foreclosure certificate of sale or deed, or to the purchaser at a foreclosure sale, that holder or purchaser is liable for it and must, within 21 days after receiving the deposits and the tenants' names and addresses, post a written notice on the main entrance of each affected unit stating that it has acquired the deposit.",
