      "Illinois has no general statute that sets a residential landlord's repair or habitability duty; Illinois courts recognize an implied warranty of habitability in residential leases (case law, not reviewed here), and local building and housing codes apply. Statutes add specific duties: working smoke and carbon monoxide alarms, heating and cooling standards in 55-and-older housing, paying landlord-paid utilities, rekeying between tenants in Cook County, and a tenant's limited right to repair and deduct. A landlord may not use a lease clause to excuse itself from liability for its own negligence in operating or maintaining the property.",
