    bodyText:
      "If a repair is required by the lease or by a law, rule or local ordinance and its reasonable cost is no more than the lesser of $500 or half a month's rent, the tenant may notify the landlord in writing, by registered or certified mail or other restricted delivery, at the landlord's or agent's address shown in the lease (or the last known address), of the tenant's intention to have the repair made at the landlord's expense. If the landlord does not make the repair within 14 days after notice, or sooner in an emergency, the tenant may have it made in a workmanlike manner by a licensed and insured tradesperson and, after giving the landlord a paid bill from an unrelated tradesperson or supplier, deduct the cost (up to those limits and the customary price) from rent. The right does not apply if the tenant, family or a guest caused the condition. The tenant is responsible for damage caused by its contractor. The Act does not apply to public housing, condominiums, cooperative housing corporations, owner-occupied rental property of 6 or fewer units, or mobile homes. Home rule units may not diminish these rights.",
    notes: "IL: 765 ILCS 742/5, 765 ILCS 742/10, 765 ILCS 742/15, 765 ILCS 742/20, 765 ILCS 742/25, 765 ILCS 742/30 (P.A. 93-891). 765 ILCS 742/25: repairs under the Act are not treated as made with the landlord's authority or permission for mechanics lien purposes (answers construction-liens for IL; the Mechanics Lien Act, 770 ILCS 60, not read). The lease's notice address matters to this remedy; the shared notices clause (tagged IL) provides addresses. Answers repair-notice for IL. Landlord-paid utility nonpayment remedies: edu-landlord-paid-utilities-il. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
