    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "heating",
    bodyText:
      "In residential rental property limited to people 55 or older, where a heating or cooling system serves the whole premises, the landlord must: run the cooling system from June 1 through September 30 whenever the heat index exceeds 80 degrees Fahrenheit; and, from October 1 through May 31, keep heat at no less than 68 degrees between 6 a.m. and 10 p.m. when the outside temperature falls below 55 degrees, and no less than 62 degrees between 10 p.m. and 6 a.m. If there is no premises-wide cooling system, the landlord must provide at least one cooled indoor common gathering space, free to all tenants, when the heat index exceeds 80 degrees (a property with no such space is exempt).",
