    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "utilities-responsibility",
    bodyText:
      "A landlord may not rent a unit where the tenant pays the utility company directly for service that also serves common areas or other units, unless, before offering a lease or renewal, taking a deposit or otherwise agreeing to rent: the landlord gives a written statement of the areas and uses served by the tenant's meter (including foreseeable ones); gives copies of the unit's utility bills for the previous 12 months, unless the tenant waives them in writing; does not ask the tenant to collect from neighbors; and states in writing any rent reduction offered for usage outside the unit. A landlord may not switch from landlord-paid to tenant-paid utilities, or from master-metered to individually metered tenant-paid utilities, during a lease term; it must give at least 30 days' notice, and for tenants under a lease the notice must come at least 30 days before the lease expires, unless both sign a written amendment. Inconsistent lease terms are void.",
    notes: "IL: 765 ILCS 735/1.2 (P.A. 87-178). The statement must precede the lease offer, so no lease clause can supply it (rule 48). The library's utilities clauses (utilities-responsibility, utilities-paid-by-landlord, both tagged IL) do not change utility arrangements mid-term. Answers utility-submetering-disclosure for IL with utility-formula-il (765 ILCS 740/5). Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
