    topicKey: "portfolio-thresholds",
    bodyText:
      "Several Illinois rules turn on the size or type of the property, not the landlord's whole portfolio: the rental-fee law exempts leases in owner-occupied premises of 6 units or fewer; the repair-and-deduct law exempts owner-occupied property of 6 or fewer units, condominiums, cooperatives and public housing; the Human Rights Act's housing exemptions cover an owner-occupied building of 4 or fewer units and rooms in an owner-occupied home (but never discriminatory advertising), and an owner-occupied building of 4 or fewer units may decide on sexual orientation (these exemptions reach only the general prohibitions in Section 3-102, not the disability provisions); the Cook County rekey duty exempts owner-occupied buildings of 4 or fewer units; the posted manager-and-insurer notice applies to buildings of more than 4 units with no resident or on-site owner or manager; deposit interest applies to properties of 25 or more units; the on-site rent-payment rule applies to 100 or more units with an on-site office; the Safe Homes Act excludes public housing except Housing Choice Vouchers; and the radon disclosure excludes units on the third story or higher. Each rule is described in its own row.",
    notes: "IL: 765 ILCS 705/35(e); 765 ILCS 742/10; 775 ILCS 5/3-106(B), (C), (H-1); 765 ILCS 705/15(e); 735 ILCS 5/9-320(a); 765 ILCS 715/1; 735 ILCS 5/9-218(a); 765 ILCS 750/35; 420 ILCS 46/20(9). Each exemption confirmed in current text (rule 32). Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
