    bodyText:
      "Eviction demands and termination notices must be served by one of the methods in the Code of Civil Procedure: personal delivery; leaving a copy with a person 13 or older residing on or in possession of the premises; certified or registered mail with a returned receipt from the addressee; or, if no one is in actual possession, posting on the premises. The statute does not list email. The deposit statement may be emailed to a verified email address the tenant provided. Illinois' Uniform Electronic Transactions Act lists no exclusion for landlord-tenant notices; its other provisions, including when the parties must have agreed to deal electronically, are not covered here. The repair-and-deduct notice goes by registered or certified mail or other restricted delivery.",
