      "An eviction complaint may not name a minor (a person under 18 who has not been emancipated) as a defendant. A complaint that names a minor must be dismissed in its entirety against all defendants and immediately sealed, although the landlord may refile against defendants who can properly be named (the court may not waive the refiling fees). A minor willfully and wantonly named may recover reasonable attorney's fees, actual damages and $1,000 in liquidated damages.",
