      "If a tenant or occupant uses the leased premises, or permits them to be used, for unlawfully possessing, storing, making, growing, delivering, using, selling or giving away controlled substances, the lease becomes void at the landlord's option. The landlord may post a written notice (on circuit clerk forms) requiring the occupants to vacate within 5 days, then file an eviction or assign the right to file to the State's Attorney. If a controlled substance is found or used anywhere in an apartment, there is a rebuttable presumption that a tenant or occupant used or possessed it or permitted its use. The tenant does not forfeit the security deposit solely because of this eviction.",
