      "When a tenant defaults, including by leaving before the lease ends, the landlord must take reasonable measures to mitigate the damages it can recover from the tenant, such as trying to re-rent. No Illinois statute defines when a house or apartment is abandoned.",
    notes: "IL: 735 ILCS 5/9-213.1 (P.A. 84-1043). No abandonment definition located (battery 19). The shared default-by-tenant clause (tagged IL) promises mitigation 'to the extent required by applicable law'. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
