      "Nothing in Illinois' eviction Article prevents law enforcement from enforcing criminal trespass, or from removing persons or property from premises when there is a criminal trespass. Whether a person is a trespasser or an occupant who must be evicted through the courts depends on the facts; a landlord should not remove someone who may be a tenant without a court order.",
