    bodyText:
      "Illinois has no statewide law requiring a landlord to have good cause to end or not renew a residential tenancy. A fixed-term lease ends when the term expires, and a periodic tenancy can be ended with the statutory notice, as long as the landlord's reason is not retaliatory, discriminatory, based on domestic or sexual violence or immigration status, or otherwise unlawful. Some local ordinances may add protections (not covered).",
