      "Illinois has no statute that ends a residential lease when a tenant dies or gives an estate a special right to terminate; the lease continues against the estate under general law, and the landlord's duty to mitigate applies. A tenant's belongings are handled under Illinois estate law.",
    notes: "IL: Confirmed absent: whole-code batteries 60 (death of tenant/lessee) and 96 (death, dies or deceased near tenant/lessee) hit only 755 ILCS 15/1 (safe-deposit boxes), 735 ILCS 5/9-216 and 735 ILCS 5/9-217 (remedies of lessees and representatives of life tenants), mobile-home and unrelated sections (765 ILCS 945/10 Reverse Mortgage Act, 765 ILCS 1005/1c Joint Tenancy Act, 755 ILCS 75/2 Uniform Partition of Heirs Property Act); battery 20 unreliable. Probate law not read. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
