    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "servicemember-rights",
    bodyText:
      "An Illinois resident servicemember (any component of the U.S. Armed Forces or any state's National Guard) who enters military service of more than 29 consecutive days after signing a lease, or who while in service receives orders for a permanent change of station or to deploy for at least 90 days, may terminate a residential lease, as may a family member living with the servicemember, by giving the landlord copies of the orders. Termination takes effect 30 days after notice, or, if rent is paid monthly, 30 days after the next rent due date after the notice; the landlord must refund unearned prepaid rent and the security deposit, less actual damages the lease allows it to deduct. A landlord's refusal to accept a proper termination is a civil rights violation. In a residential eviction, if military service materially affects a servicemember tenant's ability to pay, the court may, and on the tenant's motion must, stay the case for 90 days or adjust the rental obligation. Federal law (the Servicemembers Civil Relief Act) gives additional protections.",
    notes: "IL: 765 ILCS 705/16 (P.A. 97-913); 735 ILCS 5/9-107.10; 330 ILCS 63/35, 330 ILCS 63/50 (Illinois Service Member Civil Relief Act, read in part). Federal SCRA not read (rule 21 flag); no SCRA clause (standing decision). early-termination-ks (tagged IL) preserves military termination rights. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
