    bodyText:
      "It is a civil rights violation to use a rental application form, or to make a record or inquiry in connection with a prospective rental, that indicates any preference, limitation or discrimination based on a protected class under the Illinois Human Rights Act, including familial status, immigration status, source of income and arrest record, or an intention to make one. This applies even to landlords otherwise exempt as owner-occupants of small buildings or renters of rooms. Inquiry into arrest records or immigration status is allowed only where State or federal law authorizes it or it complies with that law.",
    notes: "IL: 775 ILCS 5/3-102(F); 775 ILCS 5/3-106(B), (C), (K), (M). rental-application-accuracy (tagged IL) excludes information Landlord was not permitted by law to request or consider. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
