    id: "edu-radon-tenant-rights-il",
    title: "Radon: Tenant Testing and Termination Rights",
    group: "Disclosures",
    states: ["IL"],
    ruleTypes: ["RECOMMENDED"],
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "radon-disclosure",
    bodyText:
      "For leases entered into on or after January 1, 2024, of units below the third story, a tenant has 90 days from the start of the lease to conduct a radon test and must give the landlord copies of the results within 10 days. If the result exceeds the Illinois Emergency Management Agency's Radon Action Level and the landlord chooses not to mitigate, the tenant may terminate the lease; the landlord may hire a radon contractor to retest within 30 days of learning the results, and a contractor's result may disprove the hazard (results are valid 2 years unless the building is renovated). If the landlord never provided the pamphlet, records and disclosure form, the tenant may test at any time during the lease and, if a hazard is shown and the landlord does not dispute it or mitigate, may within 60 days either have a radon contractor mitigate with the landlord's express consent or terminate the lease. Mitigation must be done by a licensed radon contractor; a tenant who mitigates with the landlord's express consent may deduct the cost from rent in equal parts over the rest of the lease. A landlord may not withhold the deposit for radon testing or mitigation after a tenant terminates for lack of the disclosure, except for an improper installation the tenant made without consent. Neither side is required to test or mitigate.",
    notes: "IL: 420 ILCS 46/26(b)-(e), 420 ILCS 46/30 (P.A. 103-298, eff. 1-1-24); 420 ILCS 46/20(9) (third story and higher excluded). Home rule: 420 ILCS 46/35 (read). Clause: radon-disclosure-il. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
