    bodyText:
      "In addition to the federal lead disclosure, before entering into a residential lease an owner of a residential building with units built before 1978 must give the prospective tenant the Illinois Department of Public Health's lead information brochure. An owner who has received a lead mitigation notice for a unit must, before renewing that unit's lease, give the current tenants a copy of the mitigation notice and inspection report (unless a certificate of compliance has been obtained), and must mitigate the hazard and obtain a certificate of compliance before entering into a new lease of that unit; a buyer of such a unit who received notice of the mitigation order has the same duty.",
