    bodyText:
      "When a condominium unit is leased, the Condominium Property Act, the declaration, bylaws, other condominium instruments and rules that relate to the use of the unit or the common elements apply to the tenant and are deemed incorporated in every lease executed or renewed on or after August 30, 1984. The unit owner must deliver a copy of the signed lease (or a memorandum of an oral lease) to the association board by the date of occupancy or 10 days after signing, whichever is first.",
    notes: "IL: 765 ILCS 605/18(n) (read as an excerpt). Other association powers over leasing (765 ILCS 605/18 other subsections, 765 ILCS 605/9.2 and the Common Interest Community Association Act, 765 ILCS 160) not read. hoa-compliance (tagged IL) requires the tenant to follow association rules. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
