    topicKey: "towing",
    bodyText:
      "Except as provided in the relocation-towing chapter of the Vehicle Code, the owner or lessor of private property, or a person it authorizes, may have a motor vehicle abandoned or left unattended on the property without permission removed by a towing service, without liability for the costs of removal, transportation or storage or for damage caused by them. A tenant's own vehicle parked with permission is not towed under this provision; enforcing lease parking rules against it may require other authority. Local towing ordinances and the Vehicle Code's relocation-towing rules (Chapter 18a) are not covered here.",
