    topicKey: "cannabis",
    bodyText:
      "A landlord may prohibit a tenant from cultivating cannabis, may prohibit smoking cannabis on the premises, and is not required to allow a tenant to use cannabis on the property. A landlord may not refuse to lease to or penalize a person solely for being a registered medical cannabis patient or caregiver, unless required to avoid violating federal law or losing a federal monetary or licensing benefit, and a landlord is not penalized under State law for leasing to a cardholder or a lawful adult user.",
    notes: "IL: 410 ILCS 705/10-5(b)(5), 410 ILCS 705/10-30(b)-(c) (Cannabis Regulation and Tax Act, read as excerpts); 410 ILCS 130/40(a), (c) (Compassionate Use of Medical Cannabis Program Act). Clauses: cannabis-cultivation-il (optional), smoking-policy (tagged IL). Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser on the General Assembly's official ILCS pages (ilga.gov, which print each section's history line and flag text from Public Acts with delayed effective dates): 765 ILCS 705, 710, 715, 721, 730, 735, 740, 742, 750, 752 and 755 and Article IX Parts 2 and 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/9-201 to 5/9-321) read whole; Article IX Part 1 and outside-title sections read in the sections cited; all 3,486 ILCS acts (73,378 section versions) loaded for full-text search, control term 0 hits; the 854 Public Acts of the 104th General Assembly screened in full text for uncompiled changes (IL log §1).",
