    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "attorney-fees",
    bodyText:
      "Illinois has no general statute on attorney's-fee clauses in residential leases; a lease may provide for fees, and the shared default clause awards them to the prevailing party to the extent the law permits. Several tenant-protection statutes award fees to tenants, including those on security deposits, deposit interest, retaliation, the summary of rights, Safe Homes lock changes and confidentiality, immigrant tenant protection, utility violations over $3,000, EV charging, the rental-fee law (for leases it covers) and minors named in evictions. Some local ordinances, including Chicago's, restrict landlord fee clauses (not covered).",
