    bodyText:
      "Pennsylvania state law has no general just-cause or good-cause rule for residential tenancies: when a lease term ends and the landlord gives the required notice to quit, the landlord does not need a reason. A few statutes limit this in specific situations. A landlord may not end or refuse to renew a lease because the tenant or a family member takes part in a tenants' organization. In cities covered by the Rent Withholding Act, a tenant may not be evicted for any reason while rent is paid into escrow for a unit certified unfit. When a building is converted to a condominium, cooperative or planned community, tenants cannot be required to move out during the notice year except for nonpayment, waste or disturbing conduct. Manufactured-home community lots have their own good-cause rules, and some cities, including Philadelphia, have local good-cause rules this library does not cover.",
    notes: "PA: CONFIRMED ABSENT (general rule), found under SOP 1.2 rule 41 retro check 2026-09-30. Pennsylvania Consolidated Statutes (all 74 titles and the Constitution, 75 official title files reloaded 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser from palegis.us, 29,516,464 characters) searched by regular expression, control term 'zqxvbnmwt' 0 hits; the General Assembly's unconsolidated-statute keyword search, control term 'zqxvbnmwt' 0 results; The Landlord and Tenant Act of 1951 read whole (PA log §1). Boundary: administrative rules (Pa. Code), local ordinances and case law not searched unless stated (instruction 16). Battery saved as battery_rule27_2026-09-30.json. Read section-open: 68 P.S. § 250.501 (Act § 501: notice to quit 'upon the termination of a term', no cause required); 68 P.S. § 250.205 (Act § 205: 'No individual unit lease on residential property shall be terminated or nonrenewed on the basis of the participation of any tenant or member of the tenant's family in a tenants' organization or association'); 35 P.S. § 1700-1 (Rent Withholding Act, section 1; `edu-rent-withholding-pa`); 68 Pa.C.S. §§ 3410(a), (f), 4412(a), (f), 5410(a), (f) (`edu-condo-conversion-notice-pa`). Manufactured Home Community Rights Act (1976 P.L. 1176, No. 261) and 68 P.S. § 250.501(c.1)-(c.2) (Act § 501(c.1)-(c.2)) for mobile-home parks deprioritized, not rowed. LOCAL (instruction 20): Philadelphia good-cause provisions flagged, not resolved. No PA-tagged clause needed a change: Pennsylvania is not a just-cause state, so end-of-term wording in `holdover-ca`, `early-termination-ks`, `security-deposit-use`, `no-alterations`, `keys`, `security-deposit-return-pa`, `abandoned-property-pa`, `notice-to-quit-waiver-pa` and `holdover-rate-pa` is consistent with PA law.",
