    bodyText:
      "No Pennsylvania statute states a landlord's covenant of quiet possession or quiet enjoyment for residential leases. Pennsylvania court decisions, rather than a statute, treat leases as carrying an implied promise of quiet enjoyment, so a landlord who substantially interferes with the tenant's use of the home can be liable even if the lease says nothing.",
