      "Virginia has no plain-language or readability law for residential leases and no required statement of waivers. The state's statement of tenant rights and responsibilities, which the landlord must give with the lease, is written in plain language in at least 14-point type by the Department of Housing and Community Development, but that rule governs the Department's form, not the lease.",
