      "Alabama has no just-cause or good-cause eviction rule. A landlord may end a week-to-week or month-to-month tenancy by written notice (at least 7 or 30 days) and may decline to renew a fixed-term lease when it ends, without giving a reason, however long the tenant has lived there. Situational limits still apply: a landlord may not bring or threaten an eviction in retaliation for a tenant's code complaint to a government agency, a repair complaint to the landlord, or organizing or joining a tenants' union; a declarant converting a building to condominiums must give tenants at least 60 days' notice and may not require them to leave sooner except for nonpayment of rent, waste or disturbing other tenants; and in a possession case the tenant may counterclaim, paying rent into court, and wins possession if no rent remains due. Federal rules for subsidized housing are not covered here.",
