    bodyText:
      "Under Alabama's Act, 'rent' means all payments the tenant is to make to or for the landlord under the rental agreement, so late fees and other lease charges count as rent without any special wording. The nonpayment notice may include late fees, and the cost of repairs the landlord makes after the tenant fails to fix a health or safety problem is billed as rent. This library's default clause still says an unpaid late fee alone will not support ending the lease; that is a library choice, not a legal limit.",
