      "South Carolina supplies no statutory lease form. Forms the law does supply: the lease paragraph headed 'IF YOU DO NOT PAY YOUR RENT ON TIME', which, in the statute's words or substantially equivalent ones and in bold, conspicuous type, serves as the nonpayment notice for the whole tenancy; the notice of a dishonored check, sent by certified mail, which must be substantially in the statutory form; and the tenant's affidavit and court order staying an eviction on appeal, which may be substantially in the statutory form. Magistrate court forms (the application for ejectment, the rule to vacate or show cause, the writ of ejectment, the bond to stay execution on appeal, and the 2026 petition and order for removing unlawful occupants) are court forms, not statutes, and are on the Judicial Branch's forms page.",
