    title: "Bad Check Remedies",
    group: "Rent & Payment",
    states: ["IN"],
    ruleTypes: ["RECOMMENDED"],
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "returned-payments",
    bodyText:
      "For a dishonored check you may charge the writer up to $20 plus your bank's actual charge. Separately, a writer found liable under other law who stops payment without valid legal cause, or lets a check be dishonored for lack of funds, no account or a missing signature, is also liable for interest at 18% a year from the check date, court costs, attorney's fees (at least $100 if an outside attorney sues) and other collection costs. A writer whose check was dishonored (not stopped) escapes this chapter by paying the full amount within 10 days after you give notice of nonpayment. If the writer has not paid within 30 days after you send written notice by certified mail, the court must award three times the check (if $250 or less) or the check plus $500 (if more). You must choose between this remedy and a claim under another statute the chapter names, which was not reviewed here.",
    notes: "IN: Ind. Code § 26-1-3.1-502.5(a); Ind. Code ch. 26-2-7 read whole (Ind. Code §§ 26-2-7-1 to 26-2-7-8): notice is given when mailed to the address on the check or the address the writer gave (Ind. Code § 26-2-7-3); a writer whose shortfall came from a dishonored third-party check deposited in the account and who reasonably believed funds were sufficient is excused from the treble award (Ind. Code § 26-2-7-6(a)); liability under Ind. Code § 26-2-7-4 attaches to 'a person found liable under other applicable law'. Ind. Code § 34-24-3-1 (the election alternative) not read. Clause: returned-payments-in. Rule 15: written section-open. Read section-open 2026-09-30 in the built-in browser from iga.in.gov (Indiana General Assembly, 2026 Indiana Code, which prints each section with its history line and any future-dated version): Ind. Code art. 32-31 read whole (chapters 1, 2, 2.9, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 8.5, 9, 10, 11 and 12); the whole 2026 Indiana Code (37 title files, 93,246 sections, checked against the site's title index) and the Indiana Constitution loaded for full-text search, control terms 0 hits (IN log §1, IN log §17).",
