    bodyText:
      "Indiana sales tax applies to renting rooms, lodgings or accommodations for periods of less than 30 days, including transient rentals in a house, condominium or apartment. A residential lease for 30 days or more is outside that rule. Counties and cities may also impose innkeeper's taxes on short stays.",
