    topicKey: "tenant-statutory-duties",
    bodyText:
      "Indiana tenants must follow the health and housing code duties placed on tenants; keep the areas they use reasonably clean; use the electrical, plumbing, sanitary, heating, ventilating and air-conditioning systems, elevators and appliances reasonably; not deface, damage, destroy or remove any part of the premises; follow reasonable rules in force at signing, and amended rules as the lease provides; keep smoke detectors working and replace batteries; and return the unit clean and proper, ordinary wear and tear excepted. Before suing to enforce these duties you must give notice and a reasonable time to fix the problem, unless the tenancy has ended; if you repaired physical damage, your notice must list the repairs and document their cost. A winning landlord may recover actual damages, attorney's fees and court costs, an injunction or other relief. These rules cannot be waived.",
