    bodyText:
      "For property served by a city- or town-owned utility and occupied by someone other than the owner, the occupant applying for service must give the utility the owner's or manager's name and contact information. Charges are payable by the occupant if the utility's records show the property is occupied by a non-owner who is responsible for the bill, and they are not a lien on the property; the city may not require you to cosign or guarantee the occupant's account. This rule does not cover sewage works under the municipal sewer statutes, consolidated-city utilities or a department of public utilities. For those sewage works, a lien for unpaid fees on property occupied by someone other than the owner attaches only if the utility notifies the owner within 20 days after the fees become 60 days delinquent, unless a local ordinance provides otherwise.",
