      "Indiana has no state statute letting a servicemember end a residential lease; the federal Servicemembers Civil Relief Act governs, and Indiana treats a violation of it as a violation of state law. Indiana extends the Act's rights to members of the Indiana National Guard or another state's Guard ordered to active duty, including state active duty, for at least 30 consecutive days; for state active duty, you are not subject to the state remedies until the member or a dependent gives you documentation of Guard status and the orders. A servicemember's dependents, after giving notice to the plaintiff as applicable, have the same rights as the servicemember under the Act's Title II.",
