    topicKey: "nuisance",
    bodyText:
      "Using a leased house, apartment or building to commit a controlled-substance offense is a nuisance under Indiana law. The prosecutor, a city or county attorney, the Attorney General or the property owner may sue to abate it; anyone other than the owner must give each tenant and the owner 45 days' notice first. The court must hold a hearing within 20 days and may grant an injunction, order a tenant who created the nuisance to vacate within 72 hours, and give the owner possession if the tenant disobeys, with the sheriff executing within 5 days. An owner who knew of the nuisance may be ordered to submit a plan to prevent it; other relief needs no proof that a defendant knew.",
