      "Indiana voids a waiver of its security deposit, tenant property, access and possession, tenant duty, landlord duty, retaliation and victim-protection rules. A lease may not define abandonment differently from the statute, and a tenant's attornment to a stranger is void without your consent or a court order. A confession-of-judgment (cognovit) term given before a claim accrues is void, and it is a Class B misdemeanor knowingly to procure the signing of a cognovit note, to keep one as its payee or holder, or to try to enforce in Indiana another jurisdiction's judgment based on one. Small claims venue cannot be waived by contract. No Indiana statute voids exculpatory or indemnity terms in residential leases; that is left to the courts.",
