    bodyText:
      "Arizona has no just-cause eviction rule for houses and apartments. Either party may end a month-to-month tenancy by written notice at least 30 days before the periodic rental date (10 days' notice for a week-to-week tenancy), with no reason required, and a fixed-term lease ends on its expiration date; no length of tenancy changes this. The limits are situational: a landlord may not raise rent, cut services, or bring or threaten an eviction in retaliation for a tenant's code complaint, repair complaint, or joining or organizing a tenants' union or similar organization (a complaint within the prior six months creates a presumption of retaliation); fair housing law applies; and the domestic-violence statute preserves eviction of a victim for actions unrelated to the violence. Arizona has no condominium-conversion notice for apartments and no rule barring eviction while rent is paid into court. Mobile home parks have their own termination rules.",
