    title: "Fees and Rent",
    group: "Rent & Payment",
    states: ["AZ"],
    ruleTypes: ["RECOMMENDED"],
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "fees-as-rent",
    bodyText:
      "Arizona's landlord-tenant act defines rent as the payments made to the landlord in full consideration for the rented premises, so late fees and other charges are not rent unless a statute treats them that way. One does: if a tenant doesn't fix a maintenance problem after the landlord's 14-day notice, the landlord's repair cost can be billed as rent on the next rent due date. The 5-day nonpayment notice covers rent only, but to reinstate before an eviction is filed the tenant must also pay a reasonable late fee set out in a written lease. In an eviction, the court awards late charges only if a written lease specifies them, and other periodic charges (such as extra-person, pet, storage, signage or common-area fees) only if a written lease specifies them and they are collected periodically with rent; anything else must be sued for separately. A partial payment of rent or other charges keeps the landlord's eviction rights only with the tenant's contemporaneous signed agreement.",
    notes: "AZ: NEW 2026-09-30 (SOP 1.13 retro, rule 27). Controlling text: A.R.S. §33-1310(12) ('Rent' means payments to be made to the landlord in full consideration for the rented premises); §33-1369 ('as rent'); §33-1368(B); §33-1377(F) and §12-1178(A) (judgment for 'late charges stated in the rental agreement' / 'all charges stated in the rental agreement'); §33-1371(A); RPEA Rule 13(c)(2)(C)-(D). late-fee-az already says the late fee is not Rent. Court rules (SOP rule 21: not a state-code section): Arizona Rules of Procedure for Eviction Actions, read in full 2026-09-30 from govt.westlaw.com (official court-rules host; Westlaw 'current with amendments received through May 1, 2026'); Rules 4, 5, 8-11, 13-15, 17, 20 and Appendix A carry emergency amendments effective 2026-09-12, so a later permanent adoption may change them (legal-watch flag). Saved to the AZ retro source folder; not hash-verified (AZ retro log, sources). Statutes: Read section-open 2026-09-30 in Taylor's built-in browser from azleg.gov (official compilation; each section fetched twice, heading number checked); saved to the AZ retro source folder with a SHA-256 match to the browser text (AZ retro log, sources).",
