    topicKey: "landlord-self-cure",
    bodyText:
      "If a tenant's failure to keep up the unit materially affects health and safety and can be fixed by repair, replacing a damaged item or cleaning, an Arizona landlord may give written notice that describes the problem and asks the tenant to fix it within 14 days, or as promptly as an emergency requires. If the tenant does not, the landlord may enter, have the work done in a workmanlike manner, and bill the actual and reasonable cost, or the fair and reasonable value, as rent on the next rent due date, or for immediate payment if the lease has ended. This is one of the few entries the access statute allows without the tenant's consent. No lease clause is needed for this right.",
