      "Arizona prescribes few forms for residential landlords. The one lease form is the foreclosure notice: a lease signed after a foreclosure action has started must include a notice substantially in the statute's words, and the same notice goes to existing tenants within five business days after the owner receives a first notice of trustee's sale (not for buildings of four or more connected units). The pool safety notice is a Department of Health Services document, not statutory text. No form is required for eviction notices: courts and agencies may not require a mandatory or technical form, and a notice that meets the statute's content requirements is enough. In court, the eviction summons must include the Arizona Supreme Court's Residential Eviction Information Sheet on a separate page.",
