    topicKey: "statutory-forms",
    bodyText:
      "Georgia prescribes no form for a residential lease, and none for the three-day notice to vacate or pay or the demand for possession; the statute prescribes how those notices are delivered (posted in a sealed envelope on the door, plus any method the lease adds), not their wording. Two prescribed forms can reach a landlord: the written demand sent before suing on a dishonored check, which must be in substantially the statutory form (`edu-dishonored-payment-remedies-ga`), and, for a property covered by the federal CARES Act, the CARES Act affidavit form in the Uniform Magistrate Court Rules (`edu-eviction-process-ga`). Magistrate courts' own dispossessory filing forms were not reviewed.",
    notes: "GA: NEW 2026-10-01 (SOP 1.18 retro, rule 27). Verdict: PRESENT (two forms; no lease or eviction-notice form). Controlling text: O.C.G.A. § 13-6-15(c) (demand 'in substantially the form which follows'); O.C.G.A. § 44-7-50(d) (delivery, not wording); Uniform Magistrate Court Rule 46 (CARES affidavit; gasupreme.us PDF read in the browser). Official O.C.G.A. full-text search 2026-10-01 (GA retro battery B10c; nonsense control 0): ('form which follows' OR 'following form' OR 'form as follows' OR 'substantially the form' OR 'substantially as follows' OR 'in the following form' OR 'substantially the following') AND landlord or tenant words: 11 hits, known positive O.C.G.A. § 13-6-15 returned; others: O.C.G.A. § 10-1-393(b)(20) (foreclosure-rescue sale-leaseback form), § 44-7-21 (broker commission notice), § 44-7-113 (abandoned mobile homes, deprioritized), and non-landlord forms. Two earlier proximity patterns (B10, B10b) missed the known positive and were discarded (GA retro log). Model: `edu-statutory-forms-wy` (read, not tagged). Read section-open 2026-10-01 in the built-in browser from the official O.C.G.A. on advance.lexis.com (the General Assembly's free LexisNexis public access, 'Current through the 2026 Special Session of the General Assembly'); section text saved and SHA-256 matched to the browser copy (GA retro sources).",
