      "Minnesota has no statute restricting the use of algorithmic or software-assisted rent-setting, and no disclosure duty if you use one. Several states have begun legislating here, so treat this as a live watch item rather than a settled answer, and remember that using a shared pricing service with competitors can raise antitrust questions that have nothing to do with landlord-tenant law.",
