    topicKey: "late-fee",
    bodyText:
      "Iowa caps any late fee a lease provides by the size of the monthly rent. If rent is $700 a month or less, the fee may not exceed $12 per day or $60 in total for a month; if rent is more than $700, it may not exceed $20 per day or $100 in total for a month. Iowa requires no grace period. Accepting a late payment can cost you the right to end the lease for that late payment, so if you want to rely on strict deadlines later, say so in writing before the tenant relies on your leniency.",
    notes: "IA: Iowa Code § 562A.9(4) (2013 Iowa Acts ch. 97, § 3); waiver: Iowa Code § 562A.30(1)-(2). Late fees are 'rent' (Iowa Code § 562A.6(10)); in a HUD-assisted tenancy, a notice that demanded late fees barred by HUD rules was nullified (Seldin Co v Calabro, 702 N.W.2d 504 (Iowa Ct. App. 2005)). Clause: `late-fee-ia`. Rule 37: the cap is per month of rent, the same for every tenancy type. Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from legis.iowa.gov (Iowa Code 2026 chapter XML; the whole Code and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, IA log §1); no 2025 or 2026 act amends ch. 562A or ch. 648 (IA log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
