      "In Iowa, 'rent' means any payment the tenant must make to you under the rental agreement, so on the statute's plain reading pet rent, utility charges, late fees and other required fees are rent for the three-day nonpayment notice; no reported Iowa case read for this library decides that, and the library's default clause does not end a lease for unpaid late fees alone. Demand only amounts the lease and the law actually allow: an Iowa court threw out an eviction because the nonpayment notice demanded charges the landlord could not lawfully collect, and you must prove any amount you claim.",
