      "Iowa lets you charge up to $30 for a dishonored check, draft or order, but only if you clearly and conspicuously post a notice of the charge and its amount where rent is usually paid or put it in the tenant's billing statement. You may not charge it when the check bounced because the tenant stopped payment. The statute does not cover failed electronic payments.",
