      "If rent is unpaid, serve a written notice of nonpayment stating that the lease will terminate if the rent is not paid within three days. Serve it by delivery with a signed and dated acknowledgment from a resident at least 18, by personal service, or by posting it on the main entrance door and mailing it by both regular and certified mail; mailed notice is complete four days after mailing. If the rent is not paid, you may file for eviction without a separate notice to quit. The Iowa Supreme Court has held that the federal CARES Act's 30-day notice applies only to rent defaults that arose during the 2020 moratorium.",
