      "For a material lease violation, or a failure of the tenant's statutory upkeep duties that materially affects health and safety, serve a written notice that specifies the breach and says the lease will end on a stated date at least seven days after the tenant receives it unless the breach is remedied in seven days. If the breach can be fixed by repairs, paying damages or otherwise, and the tenant fixes it in time, the lease does not end. If substantially the same breach recurs within six months, you may end the lease on at least seven days' written notice without another chance to cure. You may also recover damages, and attorney fees only if the tenant's noncompliance was willful.",
    notes: "IA: Iowa Code § 562A.27(1), (3); service, Iowa Code § 562A.29A; tenant duties, Iowa Code § 562A.17. Fees only for willful noncompliance, Seldin Co v Calabro, 702 N.W.2d 504 (Iowa Ct. App. 2005) (read). Public housing: a municipal housing agency may give a 30-day notice citing a federal regulation without a right to cure (Iowa Code § 562A.27(5)). Clause: `default-by-tenant-ia`. Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from legis.iowa.gov (Iowa Code 2026 chapter XML; the whole Code and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, IA log §1); no 2025 or 2026 act amends ch. 562A or ch. 648 (IA log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
