    notes: "IA: CONFIRMED ABSENT (whole-Code battery; boundary: statutes and Constitution searched, administrative rules, case law and local codes not searched). Rule 41: verdict recorded under `for-cause-eviction`. IA battery 100: 23 hits, control 0; known positives passed (just cause or good cause: every hit outside landlord-tenant law); IA battery 101: 4 hits, control 0; known positives passed (everyday words, refuse to renew or nonrenewal: Iowa Code §§ 322F.3, 537A.10 (dealers, franchises), 562A.27B(1)(f), 562B.25B). Exceptions: Iowa Code § 562A.36 (retaliation), Iowa Code § 562A.27B (emergency assistance), Iowa Code § 29A.101 (servicemembers, nonpayment), Iowa Code § 562A.27(5) (public housing). No condominium-conversion tenant protection (`edu-conversion-ia`). Mobile home parks (ch. 562B) are out of scope. Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from legis.iowa.gov (Iowa Code 2026 chapter XML; the whole Code and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, IA log §1); no 2025 or 2026 act amends ch. 562A or ch. 648 (IA log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
