    topicKey: "termination-notice",
    bodyText:
      "Two Iowa statutes touch the end of a fixed term. A general statute says a written agreement fixing the date a tenancy ends terminates it on that date without notice. The landlord-tenant act also lets either party end a tenancy longer than month-to-month by written notice at least 30 days before the end of the term. Because no Iowa decision reconciling the two was found, serve a written notice at least 30 days before the last day of the term whenever you want the unit back, using a method the termination-notice statute allows. If the tenant stays after the term without your consent, give a three days' notice to quit before filing for eviction. If you accept rent and let the tenant stay, the tenancy becomes month-to-month.",
