    topicKey: "holdover",
    bodyText:
      "If a tenant stays without your consent after the lease ends, you may sue for possession. If the holdover is willful and not in good faith, you may also recover your actual damages and reasonable attorney fees. A separate Iowa statute makes a tenant who holds over after giving notice of intent to quit at a stated time, or who willfully holds over after the term and after a notice to quit, liable for double the rental value for the holdover period. If you consent to the tenant staying, the tenancy continues month to month.",
