    topicKey: "notice-delivery-methods",
    bodyText:
      "Most landlord notices may be served by hand delivery, delivery with a signed and dated acknowledgment from a resident at least 18, personal service, regular plus certified mail, posting on the main entrance door (dated, within the notice period), or any method that results in the tenant actually receiving it. Termination notices and notices to quit are stricter: only signed acknowledgment of delivery, personal service, or posting on the main entrance door plus regular and certified mail. Mailed notice is complete four days after mailing. E-mail is never enough for a termination notice or notice to quit, and works for other notices only if the tenant agreed to e-mail and actually receives it.",
