    topicKey: "landlord-maintenance",
    bodyText:
      "You must comply with building and housing codes materially affecting health and safety; make all repairs and do whatever is necessary to keep the premises fit and habitable; keep common areas clean and safe; keep supplied electrical, plumbing, sanitary, heating, ventilating, air-conditioning and other facilities and appliances, including elevators, in good and safe working order; provide and arrange removal from garbage receptacles; and supply running water, reasonable hot water at all times and reasonable heat (unless the tenant controls a unit-only system on a direct utility connection). A lease cannot waive these duties. In a single family residence you and the tenant may agree in writing, in good faith, that the tenant handles garbage, water and heat supply and specified repairs or tasks; for any other unit only by a separate signed writing with adequate consideration that does not affect other tenants. You are not liable for injuries caused by things a tenant put in the common areas.",
