      "A vehicle unlawfully parked on private property, or placed there without the owner's consent, for more than 24 hours is an 'abandoned vehicle'. Police may take it into custody, or you may hire a garagekeeper to take custody and dispose of it after the certified-mail notice to the owner and lienholders. Since July 1, 2026, that notice must go out within 10 days of custody, the owner has 20 days to reclaim the vehicle (and may retrieve listed personal items once during that time), the tower must post its storage and impound fees, and the statute preempts county and city ordinances on towing abandoned vehicles. Iowa gives no separate authority to tow a tenant's authorized vehicle for expired registration or because it does not run; handle that through your parking rules and the lease.",
