      "The Iowa Civil Rights Act bars housing discrimination because of race, color, creed, sex, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, disability or familial status, including in advertising and in the terms of a rental, and bars discrimination against a tenant because of the race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age or national origin of the tenant's guests. Gender identity was removed from the Act effective July 1, 2025. Exemptions include an owner-occupied building with two units, rental of fewer than four rooms in an owner-occupied dwelling, an owner-occupied building of up to four units where the owner qualifies for the homestead credit or exemption, housing for older persons, and shared living areas by sex; the small-building exemptions never cover advertising. Federal fair housing law applies separately.",
    notes: "IA: Iowa Code §§ 216.8(1)(a)-(d), 216.8A(1)-(3); exemptions Iowa Code § 216.12(1)(a)-(f), (2); Iowa Code § 216.12(1)(e) amended by 2026 Iowa Acts ch. 1115, § 126 (homestead 'tax credit or exemption under chapter 425, subchapter I', effective July 1, 2026, read as enrolled; the compiled Code 2026 text still cites Iowa Code § 425.1); gender identity removed by 2025 Iowa Acts ch. 1 (SF 418; compiled). Local ordinances: 2026 Iowa Acts ch. 1002 (SF 579, effective on enactment, signed Mar. 10, 2026) bars a city or local government from enacting an ordinance 'broader or has different categories of unfair or discriminatory practices' than ch. 216 and struck Iowa Code § 216.19(1)(c); 2026 Iowa Acts ch. 1200, § 40 (HF 2800, effective July 1, 2026) adds 'or enforce'. Both read as enrolled; pdf.js extraction lost underline and strike-through, so the amendments' wording was inferred from the enrolled text and the compiled section (IA log §1.2). Federal Fair Housing Act not read in this pass. IA battery 46: 2 hits, control 0; known positives passed. Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from legis.iowa.gov (Iowa Code 2026 chapter XML; the whole Code and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, IA log §1); no 2025 or 2026 act amends ch. 562A or ch. 648 (IA log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
