    bodyText:
      "A tenant with a disability and a disability-related need may ask to keep an assistance or service animal; evaluate and respond within a reasonable time, and give a written determination. If the disability or need is not readily apparent, you may ask for information that reasonably supports the need for that particular animal. Iowa sets out a written finding a listed licensed professional can provide, which must state, among other things, whether the provider has known the person for at least 30 days, and is valid for 12 months or the lease term, whichever is longer; other reliable proof is still allowed. An online registration or certificate is not enough. Do not ask for a diagnosis, severity or medical records. You may require proof of licensing and vaccination, and you may deny the request for undue financial and administrative hardship, a fundamental alteration of your operations, a direct threat or substantial damage that cannot be reduced by a reasonable accommodation, or because the accommodation is not otherwise reasonable. The tenant is liable for damage the animal causes.",
