      "In most Iowa rentals the lease may restrict firearms, but not in federally assisted housing: if you receive USDA rural rental assistance or HUD voucher or listed project-based payments, the lease may not prohibit or restrict lawful firearms, components or ammunition in the tenant's own unit, though you may reasonably restrict them in common areas and the tenant must store them with reasonable care. Where the law requires you to allow firearms, you are not liable for resulting harm except for willful, reckless or grossly negligent conduct. Merely keeping a firearm in the unit is never a clear and present danger. Iowa's constitutional right to keep and bear arms binds the government; whether it limits a private landlord was not decided in any case read for this library.",
