      "Iowa requires a landlord to waive lease restrictions on dogs for a blind or partially blind person with a guide dog and for a deaf or hard-of-hearing person with a hearing dog; the tenant is liable for damage the dog does. Denying or interfering with these rights is a simple misdemeanor. Separately, an owner or lessor of property that law requires to be accessible to a person using a service animal is not liable for injury or damage the animal causes if the owner believed in good faith it was a service animal and was not negligent, reckless or willful; whether a private dwelling unit is such property is not settled.",
