    bodyText:
      "Iowa prescribes no form of residential lease and no form for the ordinary notices to tenants; the 3-day nonpayment notice and the 7-day notice to remedy a breach must say what the statute requires, in your own words. One notice must quote the statute: a 3-day notice of termination and notice to quit for conduct creating a clear and present danger must state the specific activity and set out, in full, the subsection that exempts a tenant who acts against the person causing the danger. Small claims court forms exist for filing an eviction, but they are court forms, not lease or notice forms.",
    notes: "IA: Added 2026-10-02 at sync (SOP rule 27; the IA log §18.2 recorded this topic without a row: 'Iowa prescribes no lease or notice form ... the § 562A.27A notice must quote subsection 3'). Verdict: PRESENT for one prescribed text, otherwise absent. Iowa Code § 562A.27A(1) ('setting forth the language of subsection 3'), § 562A.27A(3); notice contents Iowa Code § 562A.27(1)-(2). Court forms: Iowa Court Rules ch. 3, Form 3.6 (IA log §17). Clause: edu-clear-present-danger-ia. Read 2026-10-02 by Claude Code at sync from the official Iowa Code 2026, ch. 562A (legis.iowa.gov/docs/code/562A.pdf, compiled Dec. 2025; the IA log §1.2 found no 2025 or 2026 act amending ch. 562A).",
