    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "quiet-possession",
    bodyText:
      "No North Carolina statute states a landlord's covenant of quiet enjoyment or quiet possession for residential leases. The closest statute is the policy statement behind the expedited criminal-activity eviction procedure, which recognizes residents' right to the peaceful, safe and quiet enjoyment of their homes and applies that procedure to every residential rental agreement. Possession is otherwise protected by the ban on self-help eviction: a residential tenant can be removed only through a court eviction. Whether a lease carries an implied covenant of quiet enjoyment is a question of case law that this library has not reviewed.",
    notes: "NC: NEW 2026-10-02 (SOP 1.21 retro, rule 27). Verdict: CONFIRMED ABSENT as a statutory covenant; case law NOT LOCATED (boundary stated in the body). Full-text search 2026-10-02 of the official General Statutes and the NC Constitution on ncleg.gov (all 396 chapters on the General Statutes table of contents plus the Constitution, 57,561,854 characters, loaded in the built-in browser; control term 'zqxvbnmwt' 0 hits; battery log battery_NC_retro_2026-10-02.md). B27quiet ('quiet enjoyment|quiet possession|peaceful ... enjoyment|peaceable possession|quietly enjoy'): 9 hits in 7 sections; landlord-tenant hits N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-59.1 (known positive: 'the right to the peaceful, safe, and quiet enjoyment of their homes'), N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-59(2), N.C. Gen. Stat. § 47A-36(a) ('other tenants' peaceful enjoyment') and N.C. Gen. Stat. § 157-29; the rest are secured transactions, title and adverse possession. Heading screen H27e: only N.C. Gen. Stat. § 41-10 (titles quieted). Self-help ban: N.C. Gen. Stat. §§ 42-25.6, 42-25.8 (`edu-self-help-eviction-nc`). Model: `edu-no-quiet-possession-statute-ga` (read, not tagged). Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from the official General Statutes on ncleg.gov (section pages, each fetched twice with the heading number checked; saved to the NC retro source folder with a SHA-256 match to the browser text).",
