    topicKey: "statutory-forms",
    bodyText:
      "North Carolina prescribes no form for a residential lease or for a landlord's demand for rent or notice to quit. The statutes do supply a few forms a landlord may meet. The small claims statute sets out a sufficient form of complaint in summary ejectment. A court form published by the Administrative Office of the Courts may not be modified in a way that keeps its official appearance, and anyone who modifies one must clearly note that it was modified and say what changed. A tenant who appeals an eviction may stay it with a bond and undertaking substantially in a statutory form. A landlord who sues on a knowingly bad check must first send demand letters substantially in the statutory forms. The notice to the State Bar about an attorney tenant's files has statutory contents but no set form.",
    notes: "NC: NEW 2026-10-02 (SOP 1.21 retro, rule 27). Verdict: PRESENT (court and collection forms; no lease or notice-to-quit form). Full-text search 2026-10-02 of the official General Statutes and the NC Constitution on ncleg.gov (all 396 chapters on the General Statutes table of contents plus the Constitution, 57,561,854 characters, loaded in the built-in browser; control term 'zqxvbnmwt' 0 hits; battery log battery_NC_retro_2026-10-02.md). B27form2 (statutory-form phrases including 'substantially in the following form', 'substantially as follows', 'following form', 'form which follows', 'substantially the form', 'in the following form' near landlord-tenant words): 213 hits in 167 sections; known positive N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-34 passed; landlord-tenant hits N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-34(d), N.C. Gen. Stat. § 6-21.3 and N.C. Gen. Stat. § 7A-232. Heading screen H27f: N.C. Gen. Stat. § 7A-216 (form of complaint) and N.C. Gen. Stat. § 7A-232 (forms). Controlling text, read section-open: N.C. Gen. Stat. § 7A-232 (Form 11, complaint in summary ejectment; 'Substantial conformity is sufficient'; marking rule for modified AOC forms added by S.L. 2025-54, s. 3(a)); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-34(d) (bond to stay execution on appeal, 'may be substantially in the following form'); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 6-21.3(a1)-(a2) (bad-check demand letters 'substantially in the following form'; read in the browser, browser hash only, a weaker method); N.C. Gen. Stat. § 42-14.4(a) (State Bar notice contents). AOC eviction forms themselves not reviewed. Model: `edu-statutory-forms-ga` (read, not tagged). Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from the official General Statutes on ncleg.gov (section pages, each fetched twice with the heading number checked; saved to the NC retro source folder with a SHA-256 match to the browser text).",
