      "Since June 20, 2025, a New Mexico landlord may charge an applicant (including a guarantor or cosigner) a screening fee of no more than $50, and no other fee to process an application. You must give written or digital notice of the fee, get the applicant's written agreement to pay it, and give a receipt. You may not charge it when you know the unit is not available, and you must hold card payments or wait to deposit cash or checks until earlier applicants have been screened and rejected or have declined. Return the fee within 30 days if an earlier applicant takes the unit or you do not actually screen the applicant. Do not charge the same applicant twice within 90 days for properties under the same ownership. An unauthorized screening fee costs $250 plus a refund of all fees paid.",
