      "New Mexico landlords must substantially comply with minimum housing codes materially affecting health and safety; make repairs and keep the premises safe; keep common areas safe; keep supplied electrical, plumbing, sanitary, heating, ventilating, air-conditioning and other facilities and appliances in good and safe working order; provide garbage receptacles and arrange removal; and supply running water, reasonable hot water and reasonable heat (unless the building is not required by law to be equipped for that purpose, or heat or hot water comes from an installation in the tenant's exclusive control supplied by a direct utility connection). A lease cannot waive these duties. Only for a single family residence may the lease itself shift garbage, water and heat duties and specified repairs to the tenant; for other units, specified repairs or maintenance tasks may be shifted only by a separate signed writing supported by consideration.",
