      "If you fail to meet your repair duties, the tenant must give you written notice. For a material breach of the lease, or a violation of the act materially affecting health and safety, the tenant may give notice that the lease ends in at least 7 days unless you make a reasonable attempt to fix it. Or, if you do not fix a covered condition within 7 days of written notice, the tenant may withhold one-third of the daily rent from the notice date until it is fixed, or all of the rent if the home is uninhabitable and the tenant does not live there. The tenant may also sue for damages. These remedies do not apply to conditions the tenant or the tenant's household or guests caused, or to amenities. New Mexico does not let tenants repair and deduct.",
    notes: "NM: NMSA 1978, § 47-8-27.1(A)-(E) (written notice; seven-day termination notice; abatement; (B) no rights for conditions caused by the resident, family or persons with consent, and only termination or abatement for circumstances beyond the owner's control; (C) damages and injunctive relief; (D) one remedy per rental period for the same violation; (E) weekend or federal holiday extension). NMSA 1978, § 47-8-27.2(A)-(E) (one-third of the pro-rata daily rent, or one hundred percent if uninhabitable and not inhabited; subsidized rent; no abatement for an amenity, defined in NMSA 1978, § 47-8-3(C)). A tenant who gave no written notice was not entitled to abate (Cheng v. Rabey, 2023-NMCA-013, as summarized in the compilation's annotation to NMSA 1978, § 47-8-27.2; opinion not read, NM log §1.4). Resident's form: Form 4-902A NMRA. No repair-and-deduct remedy (NM battery 112 (tenant right to repair and deduct / withhold rent for repairs): 7 hits, control 0; known positives passed: all hits are art. 8 sections already read). Retaliation for abating is barred (NMSA 1978, § 47-8-39(A)(7)). Stale cross-reference: NMSA 1978, § 47-8-27.2(C) refers to an 'abatement limitation of one month's rent' that the section does not contain (NM log §10). Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from nmonesource.com (NMSA 1978 annotated chapter PDFs, 2026 compilation; the whole NMSA 1978 and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, NM log §1); 2025 N.M. Laws ch. 122 read as enrolled (NM log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
