    topicKey: "tenant-death",
    bodyText:
      "If a tenant who is the sole occupant dies, you must turn the property in the home over to the tenant's named contact person, or another person lawfully entitled, if they ask before it is discarded, and refund the deposit less lawful deductions (including removal and storage costs). You may remove and store the property, require an inventory signature, and discard it only after a certified-mail request to the contact person and 30 days without removal or any claim. If you asked in writing for a contact person and the tenant gave none, you have no responsibility for the property. The death does not end the lease by statute. A lease may set a different procedure, but the library uses the statutory one; take advice before changing it.",
    notes: "NM: NMSA 1978, § 47-8-34.2(A)-(G) (contact person; owner duties on a sole occupant's death; (E) a different procedure may be agreed in a written rental agreement; (F) no responsibility after a written request goes unanswered; (G) liability to the estate for actual damages). No New Mexico statute terminates a residential lease on a tenant's death (NM battery 26 (tenant death / deceased resident or lessee): 53 hits, control 0; known positives passed: hits are probate, insurance and trust sections and NMSA 1978, §§ 47-8-21, 47-8-34.2). Rule 54: the (E) alternative procedure is lawful but not offered (education per WY retro 6). Clause: `deceased-resident-contact-nm`. Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from nmonesource.com (NMSA 1978 annotated chapter PDFs, 2026 compilation; the whole NMSA 1978 and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, NM log §1); 2025 N.M. Laws ch. 122 read as enrolled (NM log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
