      "A New Mexico lease may not make the tenant (or the landlord) waive or give up rights or remedies under the law, so 'landlord is not liable' clauses, waivers of notice and similar terms are void. A landlord who deliberately uses a lease containing terms known to be prohibited owes the tenant the resulting damages and reasonable attorney fees. A confession-of-judgment clause signed before a claim arises is void, there is no landlord's lien on a tenant's belongings, and a court may limit any term it finds was inequitable when made.",
    notes: "NM: NMSA 1978, § 47-8-16 ('No rental agreement may provide that the resident or owner agrees to waive or to forego rights or remedies under the law'); NMSA 1978, § 47-8-17 ('If an owner deliberately uses a rental agreement containing provisions known by him to be prohibited by law, the resident may recover damages sustained by him resulting from application of the illegal provision and reasonable attorney's fees'); NMSA 1978, § 39-1-16 (confession-of-judgment provisions before a cause of action accrues are unlawful and void); NMSA 1978, § 47-8-36.1(A); NMSA 1978, § 47-8-12. Exculpation variants used (rule 52): `parking-ks-oh-ca`, `storage-space-ks-oh-ca`, `tenants-property-insurance-ks-oh-ca`, `services-utilities-provided-ks-oh`. New Mexico does not bar attorney-fee clauses; the act itself awards fees to the prevailing party (`edu-attorney-fees-nm`). Rule 47: New Mexico has no debt-collection statute reaching a landlord collecting its own rent (Fair Debt Collection Practices Act not read); the Unfair Practices Act reaches collecting fees not in the rental agreement (NMSA 1978, § 57-12-27(C)). NM battery 68 (confession of judgment / jury waiver / waiver of rights in leases): 17 hits, control 0; known positives passed. Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from nmonesource.com (NMSA 1978 annotated chapter PDFs, 2026 compilation; the whole NMSA 1978 and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, NM log §1); 2025 N.M. Laws ch. 122 read as enrolled (NM log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
