    notes: "NM: Rule 51, asked as two questions: (1) enumerated list: NMSA 1978, § 57-12-2(D) defines 'unfair or deceptive trade practice' with a list that now includes (20) 'charging an applicant a fee in violation of the [act]' (2025 N.M. Laws ch. 122, § 8), and NMSA 1978, § 57-12-27(B)-(C) adds the rental fee practices; the list has no blank-space or copy-at-signing item for leases (NM battery 79 (lease blanks / copy at signing / unfair practices list items): 13 hits, control 0; known positives passed); (2) general standard: false or misleading statements 'in connection with the sale, lease, rental or loan of goods or services' (NMSA 1978, § 57-12-2(D)) and unconscionable practices in connection with a lease or rental (NMSA 1978, § 57-12-2(E)); 'trade' or 'commerce' includes 'any property' (NMSA 1978, § 57-12-2(C)), so the general standards reach residential leasing (Claude's reading; a federal decision applied the act alongside the Owner-Resident Relations Act against an apartment owner, Fallen v. GREP Southwest, LLC, 247 F. Supp. 3d 1165 (D.N.M. 2017), as summarized in the compilation's annotation to NMSA 1978, § 47-8-48; opinion not read). Remedies: NMSA 1978, § 57-12-10. NM battery 35 (Unfair Practices Act reach: real property, lease, rent): 6 hits, control 0; known positives passed (hits: NMSA 1978, §§ 57-12-2, 57-12-8, 57-12-21, 57-12-22, 57-12-23, 57-12-27). Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from nmonesource.com (NMSA 1978 annotated chapter PDFs, 2026 compilation; the whole NMSA 1978 and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, NM log §1); 2025 N.M. Laws ch. 122 read as enrolled (NM log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
