      "The Uniform Owner-Resident Relations Act governs rental agreements for dwelling units in New Mexico, wherever the agreement was made. It does not apply, unless an arrangement was created to avoid it, to residence at an institution incidental to detention or medical, geriatric, counseling, religious or educational services; occupancy under a contract of sale by the purchaser; fraternal or social organization housing; transient occupancy in a hotel or motel; employee housing under a written agreement conditioning occupancy on employment; or agricultural rentals. Mobile home park lots follow the Mobile Home Park Act where it directly conflicts.",
    notes: "NM: NMSA 1978, §§ 47-8-8, 47-8-9(A)-(F), 47-8-3(G), (X) ('transient occupancy'), 47-8-49, 47-8-51, 47-8-52. Mobile home parks are out of scope (kickoff lead 1). Real-lease caveat: the New Mexico Tech license agreement used for the real-lease comparison may fall within the educational-institution exemption (NM log §15). Read section-open 2026-10-02 in the built-in browser from nmonesource.com (NMSA 1978 annotated chapter PDFs, 2026 compilation; the whole NMSA 1978 and the Constitution loaded, saved and hash-matched, NM log §1); 2025 N.M. Laws ch. 122 read as enrolled (NM log §1.2). Rule 15: written section-open.",
