      "The New Mexico Human Rights Act bars refusing to rent, discriminating in rental terms, conditions, privileges or services, and advertising or inquiring in a way that shows a preference, because of race, religion, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, pregnancy, childbirth or a related condition, spousal affiliation, physical or mental disability, or military status. The Act does not list familial status or age for housing; the federal Fair Housing Act protects families with children. Narrow exemptions cover some single-family homes rented by an owner of no more than three without discriminatory advertising, owner-occupied buildings of up to four units, and some religious organizations.",
