      "If rent is unpaid when due, give the tenant written notice of the nonpayment and of your intention to terminate the lease if the rent isn't paid within 3 days. If the tenant doesn't pay within 3 days after the notice, you may terminate and the tenant must vacate. Rent is due without demand or notice, and in Montana 'rent' includes agreed late fees and charges. Deliver the notice by a method Montana allows: in hand, by mail with a certificate of mailing or by certified mail (treated as served 3 days after mailing), or by e-mail only if the tenant elected e-mail notice in the lease. Accepting full payment of the rent due waives the nonpayment; accepting a partial payment waives nothing.",
