      "Montana has no just-cause or good-cause eviction statute. A month-to-month or week-to-week tenancy can be ended by the required written notice without a reason, and a fixed-term lease ends at the end of its term if either party gives 30 days' written notice before that date. Limits still apply: you may not retaliate against a tenant within the protections of the retaliation statute, ending a lease early without cause carries a damages cap, and terminations for breach must follow the statutory notices.",
