      "If a tenant abandons the unit, you must make reasonable efforts to re-rent it at a fair rental. If you re-rent for a term starting before the lease ends, the old lease terminates when the new tenancy begins. If you don't make reasonable efforts, or you accept the abandonment as a surrender, the lease is treated as terminated by you on the date you had notice of the abandonment. You may enter during an absence of more than 7 days at reasonably necessary times, and if the lease requires notice of an extended absence and the tenant doesn't give it, you may recover actual damages. Every party has a duty to mitigate damages.",
