      "You may not retaliate by raising rent, decreasing services, or bringing or threatening a possession action after a tenant has complained to a government agency about a code violation materially affecting health and safety, complained to you in writing about a maintenance violation, or organized or joined a tenants' union. A complaint within 6 months before your action creates a rebuttable presumption of retaliation (not if the complaint came after notice of the rent increase or service cut). The tenant may recover possession or terminate and recover up to the greater of three months' periodic rent or treble damages. You may still bring a possession action if the tenant caused the code violation, is in default in rent, or compliance requires work that would effectively deprive the tenant of the unit.",
