    topicKey: "eviction-process",
    bodyText:
      "After a lawful termination, file an action for possession in district court or in a justice's, city or municipal court (small claims court hears only money and personal-property claims). The tenant has 5 business days after service of the summons and complaint to answer. The court must hear the case within 10 business days after the tenant's appearance or answer date (5 business days for dangerous-activity terminations) and rule within 5 days after the hearing; a damages hearing must be held within 45 days after possession and rent are decided. If you win possession, the court issues writs of possession and assistance immediately, and the sheriff executes the writ within 5 business days. Either side may demand a jury.",
