      "A person who can't produce authorization to occupy (a written rental agreement, or written or verified verbal permission from you, or from a tenant for a guest) is an unauthorized person or trespasser and may be removed immediately by law enforcement at your request; law enforcement may stand by while you change locks and remove the occupant's belongings. Since October 1, 2025, knowingly entering and residing on another's premises without consent is the crime of unlawful squatting. A tenant who lets unauthorized persons live in the unit can be given a 3-day curable notice. Never use this route against a tenant: a tenant is removed only through the court process.",
