    id: "edu-statutory-forms-nv",
    title: "Statutory Forms",
    group: "Notices & General",
    states: ["NV"],
    ruleTypes: ["RECOMMENDED"],
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "statutory-forms",
    bodyText:
      "Nevada prescribes few forms for residential landlords. A tenant ending the lease because of domestic violence may use an affidavit from a qualified third party in substantially the statute's form. A single-family lease not signed by a licensed property manager must carry the statutory disclosure about occupancy presumptions at the top of the first page, in type at least twice the size of any other text. Summary-eviction notices must contain the statements the eviction statute lists (the court with jurisdiction, how to contest, what happens if the court rules against the tenant, and the lockout remedies), but no statewide form is prescribed; the Las Vegas Justice Court requires its court-approved notice and complaint forms. A lender collecting rents after an assignment may notify tenants on a statutory form, and a trustee's or execution sale of an occupied home requires a separate notice posted and mailed to the tenants.",
    notes: "NV: NEW 2026-10-02 (SOP 1.27 retro, rule 27). PRESENT: NRS 118A.347 (affidavit, 'substantially the following form'; edu-dv-termination-documentation-nv); 118A.200(4) (sfr-occupancy-disclosure-nv); 40.253(3); LVJCLR 6.2(f)(1)(A), (3) (edu-eviction-court-rules-nv); 107A.290; 107.087(3); 21.130(3). Battery (rule 19 form patterns: substantially (in) the following form, substantially as follows, in substantially the following, statutory form, form prescribed, following form, 'as follows:', form which follows, substantially the form) within 250 characters of landlord/tenant/lease terms: 44 sections; the landlord-tenant ones are 118A.345, 118A.347, 107A.290, 107.087 and 21.130 (118B manufactured-home park forms out of scope). Read section-open 2026-10-02 in Taylor's built-in browser from leg.state.nv.us (Nevada Revised Statutes 2025/2026 R1; the relied-on chapter pages print Rev. 4/15/2026 and the 36th Special Session (2025) amended none of the sections relied on; whole NRS loaded, 835 chapter pages, 49,746 sections, parser checked complete against every chapter's table of contents); each relied-on section saved with a SHA-256 match to the browser text (NV retro sources). Court rules (SOP rule 21: not state-code sections): Justice Court Rules of Civil Procedure (JCRCP, 'Including Amendments Through October 31, 2025'), the Nevada Rules for Sealing and Redacting Court Records (SRCR), the Policy for Handling Filed, Lodged and Presumptively Confidential Documents, and the local rules of the Las Vegas, Las Vegas Township, Henderson, North Las Vegas, Pahrump, Reno and rural justice courts, read whole 2026-10-02 from leg.state.nv.us/CourtRules in Taylor's built-in browser and saved with a SHA-256 match (NV retro sources).",
