    bodyText:
      "Nevada has no statute barring a landlord from having a tenant sign a residential lease with blank spaces, or requiring the lease to be complete at signing. The landlord-tenant act lists what a written lease must contain, and you must give the tenant a free copy of the signed lease when it is signed. Fill in every blank before anyone signs: a blank filled later invites a dispute over what was agreed.",
