    topicKey: "statutory-forms",
    bodyText:
      "Texas prescribes only a few forms a residential landlord uses. The floodplain notice, and the prior-flooding notice where you know of flood damage in the last five years, must be substantially in the statute's words, with its check boxes, and signed by you and the tenant (the library's flood disclosure clause). The lease must contain language substantially equivalent to the statute's statement on the tenant's special rights to end the lease early for family violence, certain sex offenses or stalking, or military service, or you lose the right to collect unpaid rent from a tenant who leaves under those rights (the library's statement clause). A homeowner removing an unauthorized occupant uses the complaint the statute sets out. Other notices (the electricity termination notice, the smoke-alarm notice, the repair-remedies statement) have required content and print, not a fixed text.",
    notes: "TX: NEW 2026-10-03 (SOP 1.29 retro, rule 27 topic `statutory-forms`). PRESENT. Battery 'substantially (as follows|the following|equivalent to the following|in the following form|the form)|in the following form|following form|form which follows|as follows:|prescribed form|form prescribed|form adopted' over the Property Code: hits in the landlord-tenant chapters are §24B.002 (complaint form), §92.0135(b), (d) (flood notices), §§92.016(f), 92.0161(g), 92.017(g) (early-termination statement); the many hits elsewhere (e.g., §§5.014, 5.019, 5.0206) are the positives. Rows: `flood-disclosure-tx`, `early-termination-rights-statement-tx`, `edu-unauthorized-occupant-removal-tx`; content-and-print rules: §92.008(h)(3)-(4), §92.2611(d), §92.056(g) (`electric-submeter-interruption-tx`, `smoke-alarm-tx`, `habitability-timeline-tx`). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the official Texas statutes (chapter HTML served by tcss.legis.texas.gov behind statutes.capitol.texas.gov; site current through the 89th Legislature, 2nd Called Session, 2025); the whole Property, Business & Commerce, Civil Practice & Remedies and Finance Codes and the Constitution were loaded, proved complete against the site's chapter lists, saved and hash-matched (TX log, 'Retro checks (SOP 1.29)').",
