    bodyText:
      "Texas statutes do not address tenant-installed security cameras or video doorbells. The lease's alteration and installation terms govern, subject to the tenant's statutory rights to rekey and to have security devices installed. A separate statute stops a homeowners' association from barring an owner's security camera on the owner's own property; it protects owners, not tenants. Laws on recording and surveillance were not reviewed.",
