    notes: "WI: Wis. Stat. § 704.085(1)(a): 'a landlord may require a prospective tenant to pay the landlord’s actual cost, up to $25, to obtain a consumer credit report on the prospective tenant from a consumer credit reporting agency that compiles and maintains files on consumers on a nationwide basis. The landlord shall notify the prospective tenant of the charge before requesting the consumer credit report, and shall provide the prospective tenant with a copy of the report.' § 704.085(1)(b): not if the applicant provides a report 'that is less than 30 days old'. § 704.085(2): nonresident background check, 'actual cost, up to $25'. The credit report rule is repeated in Wis. Admin. Code ATCP § 134.05(4); the nonresident background-check charge rests on § 704.085(2) alone. Earnest money: 'the total of any payments or deposits, however denominated or described, given by a prospective tenant to a landlord in return for the option of entering into a rental agreement in the future, or for having a rental agreement considered by a landlord', excluding the credit check fee (ATCP § 134.02(3)); refund rules in ATCP § 134.05(2)-(3) (`edu-holding-deposit-wi`). No other application-fee authorization found (WI battery 7 (application / screening fee): 193 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic)). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Wisconsin Statutes (2023-24, updated through 2025 Wis. Act 247), the Wisconsin Administrative Code (current through Register September 2026, No. 849) and the Wisconsin Constitution, loaded in the built-in browser from docs.legis.wisconsin.gov, saved and hash-matched (WI log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
