      "Before taking earnest money or a deposit from an applicant, identify the unit or units they are being considered for. Return the full earnest money by the end of the next business day if you reject the applicant, the applicant withdraws before you accept, or you have not approved the application within 3 business days (or a later date the applicant agrees to in writing, no more than 21 days out). If you sign a lease, apply it to rent or the security deposit, or return it. If an approved applicant backs out (and you have not significantly altered the rental terms you disclosed), you may keep only your actual costs and damages, and lost rent only after reasonable efforts to rerent.",
    notes: "WI: Wis. Admin. Code ATCP § 134.05(1): no earnest money or security deposit 'until the landlord identifies to the applicant the dwelling unit or units for which that applicant is being considered for tenancy.' ATCP § 134.05(2)(a)1.-3.: refund 'by the end of the next business day' after rejection, withdrawal before acceptance, or failure to approve 'by the end of the third business day after the landlord accepts the applicant’s earnest money deposit, or by a later date to which the tenant agrees in writing. The later date may not be more than 21 calendar days after the landlord accepts the earnest money deposit.' ATCP § 134.05(2)(b): apply as rent or security deposit, or return it. ATCP § 134.05(3)(a)-(b): withholding if the approved applicant fails to enter into the agreement, 'unless the landlord has significantly altered the rental terms previously disclosed', limited to 'actual costs and damages', and no lost rent without mitigation under Wis. Stat. § 704.29. Local ordinances may not add deposit requirements (Wis. Stat. § 66.0104(2)(b)) (WI battery 28 (holding / earnest money deposit): 14 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic)). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Wisconsin Statutes (2023-24, updated through 2025 Wis. Act 247), the Wisconsin Administrative Code (current through Register September 2026, No. 849) and the Wisconsin Constitution, loaded in the built-in browser from docs.legis.wisconsin.gov, saved and hash-matched (WI log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
