    notes: "WI: Wis. Stat. § 704.28(1)-(3); Wis. Admin. Code ATCP § 134.06(3) (`security-deposit-use-wi`, `nrp-deposit-withholding-wi`). DATCP note: 'a landlord may not withhold from tenant’s security deposit for routine painting or carpet cleaning, where there is no unusual damage caused by tenant abuse' (ATCP § 134.06 note). A separate DATCP note says a lease term requiring professional carpet cleaning 'in the absence of negligence or improper use by the tenant, does not render a rental agreement void under sub. (7)' (ATCP § 134.08 note); DATCP's ATCP § 134.06 note adds: 'Even if the lease includes the permitted provision, a landlord may not deduct the cost of routine carpet cleaning from the security deposit, which cannot be withheld for normal wear and tear under sub. (3).' Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Wisconsin Statutes (2023-24, updated through 2025 Wis. Act 247), the Wisconsin Administrative Code (current through Register September 2026, No. 849) and the Wisconsin Constitution, loaded in the built-in browser from docs.legis.wisconsin.gov, saved and hash-matched (WI log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
