      "Wisconsin tenants may not make physical changes, including decorating, without your consent, may not use the unit for an unlawful purpose or unreasonably interfere with other occupants, and must comply with any local housing code. If the tenant damages the unit, including through a pest infestation the tenant caused, you may let the tenant repair it or do the work yourself and bill the tenant; your cost is presumed reasonable and may include your own time at a reasonable hourly rate. Where no local housing code applies, the tenant also makes minor repairs to furnished equipment when the cost is small relative to rent.",
