    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "utility-landlord-account",
    bodyText:
      "If gas, electric or water service is measured jointly for 2 or more rental units, the account must be in your name or your managing agent's name. When a tenant ends service, the utility may hold you responsible unless you name the responsible party, or ask for shutoff within 15 days of its notice and confirm that shutoff will not endanger health or property. A utility may not require proof of eviction to start service in your name, and a gas or electric utility may not knowingly help a landlord remove a tenant. Cutting off heat, water or electricity to force a tenant out is an unlawful constructive eviction.",
    notes: "WI: Wis. Stat. § 196.643(1) (15 days after the notice is mailed), (2) (joint metering: 'the owner shall maintain the account ... in the name of the owner or in the name of the agent'), (4) (no proof of eviction). Wis. Admin. Code PSC §§ 113.0301(8)(g) (electric), 134.062(6)(g) (gas) (a utility may not disconnect or refuse service in order 'to knowingly assist a landlord in the removal or eviction of a tenant from rental property'). Constructive eviction barred: Wis. Admin. Code ATCP § 134.09(5), (7) (WI battery 55 (utility shutoff where landlord holds account / joint metering): 12 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic)) (WI battery 92 (lockout / self-help eviction / utility shutoff): 867 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic)). Owner notice of pending electric disconnection needs the tenant's authorization 'in a separate written document' (Wis. Stat. § 196.643(3)(b); `utility-notice-authorization-wi`). Also answers `utility-shutoff-statute` (WI log §18). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Wisconsin Statutes (2023-24, updated through 2025 Wis. Act 247), the Wisconsin Administrative Code (current through Register September 2026, No. 849) and the Wisconsin Constitution, loaded in the built-in browser from docs.legis.wisconsin.gov, saved and hash-matched (WI log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
