      "Wisconsin requires you to keep the parts of the property you control in reasonable repair, maintain equipment for services you agreed to provide, make structural repairs, repair furnished plumbing, wiring and equipment (where no local housing code applies), and comply with any local housing code. These duties cannot be waived, and a lease that waives your duty to deliver or maintain a habitable unit is void in its entirety. One tenant's damage does not excuse repairs owed to other tenants.",
