    topicKey: "alarm-duties",
    bodyText:
      "One- and two-unit buildings: you must install a working smoke detector in the basement and on each floor level of each unit (not the attic or storage area), and a carbon monoxide detector in the same places (not the garage) unless the building has no attached garage, no fireplace and no fuel-burning appliance; the tenant maintains the detectors in the unit, but you must fix one within 5 days after a tenant or inspector gives you written notice that it does not work. Buildings with 3 or more units: you must install and maintain smoke detectors in the basement and at the head of each stairway on each floor, plus one in or within 6 feet of each sleeping area of each unit (not in a kitchen); you maintain common-area detectors and tenants maintain those in their units, subject to the same 5-day repair rule, with forfeitures of up to $50 a day. Carbon monoxide detectors are required near the sleeping areas of units that contain a fuel-burning appliance; of other units in a building that contains one, such as a central boiler or water heater, unless there is no opening between the appliance and the unit or a detector is installed between them or on the ceiling of the appliance room; of units served by a fuel-burning forced-air furnace; and of units near an attached garage (with listed exceptions, and none at all if every fuel-burning appliance in the building is a warrantied sealed-combustion unit), and you must maintain them and repair or replace one within 5 days after a tenant's written notice.",
    notes: "WI: One- and two-unit 'dwellings' (Wis. Stat. § 101.61(1)): Wis. Stat. § 101.645(3); Wis. Stat. § 101.647(2), (3)(a) ('This paragraph does not apply to the owner of a dwelling that has no attached garage, no fireplace, and no fuel-burning appliance'), (3)(am), (3)(b) (WI battery 44 (smoke detectors): 53 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic)) (WI battery 45 (carbon monoxide detectors): 26 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic)). Buildings of 3 or more units are public buildings (a structure used 'by the public or by 3 or more tenants', Wis. Stat. § 101.01(12)) and residential buildings, which include 'any apartment house' (Wis. Stat. § 101.145(1)(a)): smoke detectors, § 101.145(3)(a)-(c), (4) ('in the basement and at the head of any stairway on each floor level of the building and ... either in each sleeping area of each unit or elsewhere in the unit within 6 feet of each sleeping area and not in a kitchen'), (5) ('not more than $50 for each day of violation'); carbon monoxide detectors, Wis. Stat. § 101.149(2)(ac)-(ax) (including (ap): 'Carbon monoxide detectors shall be provided in units located in residential buildings that contain fuel-burning appliances', with the (ap)1.-2. exceptions), (3)(a) ('The owner of a residential building shall reasonably maintain every carbon monoxide detector'), (3)(b) (5 days after an occupant's written notice), (5) (sealed combustion units). `alarm-maintenance-wi`. Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Wisconsin Statutes (2023-24, updated through 2025 Wis. Act 247), the Wisconsin Administrative Code (current through Register September 2026, No. 849) and the Wisconsin Constitution, loaded in the built-in browser from docs.legis.wisconsin.gov, saved and hash-matched (WI log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
