      "Before signing and before taking any deposit: give the lease and written rules to review; disclose known uncorrected code violations and listed habitability conditions; disclose if water, heat or electricity is not included in rent and how shared charges are split; tell an applicant about any credit-report or background-check charge before ordering it; disclose non-rent charges with any rent quote; and give the check-in notice before taking a deposit. At or before signing: name the manager and owner with a Wisconsin service address (not required for an owner-occupied building of 4 or fewer units), and identify any NONSTANDARD RENTAL PROVISIONS document. In the lease or an addendum: the Notice of Domestic Abuse Protections. At move-in: the check-in sheet. If you will not store property left behind: written notice at signing and renewal. Federal lead disclosure for pre-1978 housing.",
