    topicKey: "termination-notice",
    bodyText:
      "Unless you both agreed on another method or the tenant surrenders the unit, either side can end a month-to-month or other periodic tenancy only by written notice, at the end of a rental period, given at least 28 days before (or one full rental period if rent is paid more often than monthly). The notice must state the intent to end the tenancy and the termination date. A notice with a wrong date is generally effective on the first date that would have been proper. If a periodic tenant moves out without notice and stops paying, the tenancy ends as if notice had been given on the day you learn they left.",
    notes: "WI: Wis. Stat. § 704.19(2)(a)-(b), (3) ('At least 28 days’ notice must be given except ... If rent is payable on a basis less than monthly, notice at least equal to the rent-paying period is sufficient'), (4), (5), (6). When notice is given: § 704.19(7) (registered or certified mail within Wisconsin: the 2nd day after mailing; leave-and-mail or post-and-mail: the later of leaving or mailing; personal delivery: that day). Day counting: 'Notice is given on the day specified below, which is counted as the first day of the notice period' (§ 704.19(7)); on that specific rule, Wis. Stat. § 990.001(4) does not govern these notices (Claude's reading; no case searched). Manufactured home community terminations also follow Wis. Stat. § 710.15(5m), which applies 'Notwithstanding ss. 704.17 and 704.19'. Other agreed method or surrender: § 704.19(2)(a) (WI battery 96 (termination notice periodic tenancy): 6 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic)). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Wisconsin Statutes (2023-24, updated through 2025 Wis. Act 247), the Wisconsin Administrative Code (current through Register September 2026, No. 849) and the Wisconsin Constitution, loaded in the built-in browser from docs.legis.wisconsin.gov, saved and hash-matched (WI log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
