    notes: "WI: Wis. Stat. § 758.20(2)(a)-(b) ('a period of at least 10 years'; 'a period of at least 2 years'). Retention: SCR 72.01(8)(a), (c)-(d), (9), (10) (Wisconsin's citation form for its Supreme Court Rules), created by In re amendment to SCR 72.01(8), 72.01(9), and 72.01(10), 2024 WI 24 (No. 22-03, amended order filed July 31, 2024), 'effective July 1, 2025' (court rules read from the saved court-rules file, WI log §1.1, rule 39). No sealing statute: CONFIRMED ABSENT (whole-code battery; boundary: the Wisconsin Statutes, the Wisconsin Administrative Code and the Wisconsin Constitution searched; case law and local ordinances not searched). (WI battery 83 (eviction record sealing / removal from court website): 1 hit, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic)) (WI battery 84 (eviction record everyday rerun (court website / CCAP)): 4 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic)). Screening: Wis. Stat. § 66.0104(2)(a)1.e. Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Wisconsin Statutes (2023-24, updated through 2025 Wis. Act 247), the Wisconsin Administrative Code (current through Register September 2026, No. 849) and the Wisconsin Constitution, loaded in the built-in browser from docs.legis.wisconsin.gov, saved and hash-matched (WI log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
