    bodyText:
      "You may not raise rent, cut services, sue for possession, refuse to renew, or threaten any of these because a tenant complained in good faith to an elected official or a local housing code agency (DATCP's rule covers reports to any government agency), complained to you about repairs or code violations, or exercised a legal right; DATCP also protects tenants who join or organize a tenants' union. You may still evict for unpaid rent, the protection does not cover complaints about defects the tenant caused, and the tenant must show the action would not have happened but for the protected conduct. A lease that lets you take these steps because a tenant called police, health or safety services is void.",
