      "A Wisconsin lease may not require the tenant to pay your attorney fees or costs for any dispute; a lease that does is void in its entirety. Fees that pass your collection or notice-service costs on to the tenant are risky because they may be treated the same way, so the clause library does not include them. You can recover only the costs and fees a court awards by statute, which in an eviction is $10 plus the statutory amount on any damages recovered. When suing over a worthless check, a separate statute allows exemplary damages and reasonable attorney fees, together capped at $500 per check.",
