      "In a Wisconsin eviction either side may demand a jury, by filing a written demand and paying the fee at or before joinder of issue; otherwise the right is waived. Wisconsin's constitution lets a jury be waived 'in the manner prescribed by law', which the state supreme court has said is not limited to statutes. No Wisconsin statute addresses a lease jury waiver and its enforceability is unsettled, so the clause library does not include one.",
