      "Besides the federal Servicemembers Civil Relief Act, Wisconsin protects members of the Wisconsin National Guard or state defense force ordered to state active duty for 30 days or more. A member who signed a lease before entering state active duty may end it by written notice delivered personally or by first-class mail; for monthly rent, termination is effective 30 days after the next rent due date. Evicting the family of a member on state active duty from a dwelling whose rent does not exceed the federal limit requires a court order, and on the member's application the court must stay the case for up to 90 days unless the member's ability to pay is not materially affected.",
