    bodyText:
      "You may not charge a late fee for rent paid within five days after its due date; once rent is more than five days late, the fee may run from the first day after the due date. For these tenancies Washington sets no cap on the late fee itself (mobile home lot agreements have percentage caps), but in an eviction for nonpayment the court's judgment, and the amount the tenant pays to be reinstated, may include late fees only up to $75 in total. A lease term charging a late fee within the five days is void, and knowingly using a lease with that term exposes you to actual damages plus statutory damages of up to twice the monthly rent, costs and attorneys' fees. You may still serve a 14-day pay-or-vacate notice any time after rent is due.",
    notes: "WA: 'The landlord may not charge a late fee for rent that is paid within five days following its due date' (RCW 59.18.170(2)); 'Nothing in this subsection prohibits a landlord from serving a notice to pay or vacate at any time after the rent becomes due'. Void term and penalty: RCW 59.18.230(2)(i), (3). Judgment and reinstatement: 'late fees if such fees are due under the lease and do not exceed $75 in total' (RCW 59.18.410(1)) (same words in RCW 59.18.410(2)). No cap on the fee for chapter 59.18 tenancies: CONFIRMED ABSENT (whole-corpus battery; boundary: the Revised Code of Washington, the Washington Administrative Code and the Washington Constitution searched; case law and local ordinances not searched); mobile home lot agreements entered into or renewed on or after May 7, 2025 cap late fees by percentage of total rent (RCW 59.20.060(2)(j)) (WA battery 2 (late fee cap / limit (amount or percent)): 7 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic)) (WA battery 3 (late fee cap everyday rerun (charge for late payment; penalty for late rent)): 5 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 2 synthetic)) (WA battery 1 (late fee (any)): 211 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic)). The penalty doctrine as applied to late fees was not read (unread). Late fees on rent that came due during the COVID-19 period are separately barred (RCW 59.18.625; historical). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Revised Code of Washington and the whole Washington Administrative Code (app.leg.wa.gov, every chapter page loaded in the built-in browser) and the Washington Constitution, saved and hash-matched (WA log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
