    bodyText:
      "In Washington, rent means the recurring and periodic charges in the lease for use and occupancy, which can include utilities, pet rent or parking. Late fees, damages, deposits, legal costs and other one-time fees are not rent, and a tenant's right to stay cannot be conditioned on paying them (except the court costs, late fees up to $75 and awarded attorneys' fees a tenant pays to be reinstated in a nonpayment eviction): put only rent in a 14-day pay-or-vacate notice, and collect other charges by other lawful means. The exception: if you gave an installment plan for deposits or nonrefundable fees at the start of the tenancy and the tenant defaults, the missed installment may be treated as rent owing. A fee in lieu of a deposit is never rent. Do not roll a balance from an earlier lease or unit into rent.",
    notes: "WA: 'these terms do not include nonrecurring charges for costs incurred due to late payment, damages, deposits, legal costs, or other fees, including attorneys' fees' (RCW 59.18.030); possession: RCW 59.18.283(2), which opens 'Except as provided in RCW 59.18.410' (reinstatement amounts, RCW 59.18.410(2)); installments: 'the landlord may treat the default in payment as rent owing' (RCW 59.18.283(3)); fee in lieu: RCW 59.18.670(2)(b). The last sentence answers the real lease's prior-balance clause (WA log §15): a balance from another tenancy is not a charge 'identified in the rental agreement for the use and occupancy of the premises' (Claude's reading of RCW 59.18.030). (WA battery 209 (amounts other than rent / prior balances as condition of tenancy): 3 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic)) (WA battery 226 (rent concession and recurring charges as rent (definition of rent)): 5 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic)). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Revised Code of Washington and the whole Washington Administrative Code (app.leg.wa.gov, every chapter page loaded in the built-in browser) and the Washington Constitution, saved and hash-matched (WA log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
