    bodyText:
      "After a tenant's personal check to you is returned for nonsufficient funds or a closed account, you may refuse personal checks from that tenant for nine months, but you must still accept a cashier's check or money order. Washington's dishonored-check law lets the payee collect a reasonable handling fee for each returned check; if the check is still unpaid 15 days after you send the statutory notice of dishonor, interest at 12% and collection costs of up to $40 (or the check amount, if less) may be added, and in a court action on the check further damages and fees apply. Keep your fee reasonable and state it in the lease.",
