    topicKey: "holding-deposit",
    bodyText:
      "After you offer a unit, you may take a fee or deposit to hold it, up to 25% of the first month's rent. Immediately on payment, give a receipt and a written statement of any conditions under which you may keep it. If the applicant moves in, credit it to the first month's rent or the security deposit; if not, you may keep it only as the written statement allows. You may not keep any of it if the unit fails a tenant-based rental assistance inspection; if that inspection doesn't happen within 10 days (or an agreed longer time), you may tell the applicant the unit is no longer held and must then promptly return the money. A screening charge is separate and is not a holding fee.",
