    notes: "WA: Confidentiality: no rental agreement may provide that the tenant 'Sign a nondisclosure agreement relating to the lease agreement or details of the offer, including rent amount, security deposits or fees, rent concessions, move-in gifts, or lease specials or terms' (RCW 59.18.230(2)(c)) (Laws of 2025, ch. 206, § 1, which applies to leases entered into or renewed on or after July 27, 2025 (Laws of 2025, ch. 206, § 2); WA log §1.2). First-year and mid-term bars: RCW 59.18.700(1)(a)(i), 59.18.140(3)(a). Increase rules: RCW 59.18.700(1), 59.18.140(3), and the 'rent' definition in RCW 59.18.030. Whether ending a recurring concession is an 'increase' is not addressed by any section found; no case was searched (rule 21); the advice is Claude's conservative reading. Concession texts of AZ, IL and WI rest on their own statutes and are not tagged (WA log §2.3). (WA battery 200 (rent concession): 41 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic)) (WA battery 201 (rent concession everyday rerun (free rent, discount, move-in special)): 8 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 2 synthetic)). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Revised Code of Washington and the whole Washington Administrative Code (app.leg.wa.gov, every chapter page loaded in the built-in browser) and the Washington Constitution, saved and hash-matched (WA log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
