    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "nonpayment-notice",
    bodyText:
      "For unpaid rent, serve a 14-day notice to pay or vacate in substantially the statutory form, which lists monthly rent, utilities and other recurring charges due (no late fees or other one-time charges), tells the tenant about the Attorney General's translated notices and rental assistance, the right to a lawyer and an interpreter, and mediation, and states where to pay. You may serve it any time after rent is due. Accept payment as the lease allows or by nonelectronic means, including (but not limited to) cashier's check, money order or other certified funds; any payment must go first to the amount on the notice. Serve it the way RCW 59.12.040 requires (personal delivery, or the substitute methods, which include mailing a copy); when a copy is mailed, allow five additional days before filing. State in the notice the date by which the tenant must pay or vacate, which the service statute now requires of every termination notice. You must accept a rental assistance pledge that covers the full rent before the notice expires.",
    notes: "WA: 'Every 14-day notice served pursuant to RCW 59.12.030(3) must be in substantially the following form' (RCW 59.18.057(1)); period RCW 59.12.030(3); timing RCW 59.18.650(2)(a); the form's payment note: 'payment must be made pursuant to the terms of the rental agreement or by nonelectronic means including, but not limited to, cashier's check, money order, or other certified funds'; 'The form required in this section does not abrogate any additional notice requirements to tenants as required by federal, state, or local law' (RCW 59.18.057(2)). No late fees or one-time charges: rent excludes nonrecurring charges (RCW 59.18.030, applied by RCW 59.12.030(3)). Service and five days: RCW 59.12.040, which also requires a termination notice to specify the date to vacate or comply (Laws of 2026, ch. 144, § 1); the RCW 59.18.057 form has no date field, so add one. Translations: RCW 59.18.058 (Attorney General). Pledges: RCW 59.18.410(2). The federal CARES Act 30-day notice for covered properties is federal law, not searched here (rule 39; WA log §7). (WA battery 81 (unlawful detainer notices (pay or vacate, comply or vacate)): 30 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic)) (WA battery 184 (formatting: prescribed forms (substantially the following form)): 190 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic)). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Revised Code of Washington and the whole Washington Administrative Code (app.leg.wa.gov, every chapter page loaded in the built-in browser) and the Washington Constitution, saved and hash-matched (WA log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
