    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "cure-and-eviction-grounds",
    bodyText:
      "For a breach other than unpaid rent or money damages, give a written 10-day notice to comply or vacate that specifies the acts or omissions; the tenant (or a subtenant or mortgagee) may cure within the 10 days and save the tenancy. A breach must be substantial and of a material lease term, a material subsidized-housing requirement, or a tenant duty imposed by law. No cure applies to waste, nuisance, unlawful activity affecting others' use and enjoyment, or other substantial or repeated and unreasonable interference: a 3-day notice to quit. Repeated cured violations can support a 60-day end-of-term notice only after four separate violations in 12 months, each with a written warning containing the statutory statements. For unpaid rent the tenant can still pay and be reinstated up to five court days after judgment.",
    notes: "WA: Cure: 'after the landlord has served written notice specifying the acts or omissions constituting the breach and requiring, in the alternative, that the breach be remedied or the rental agreement will end' (RCW 59.18.650(2)(b)); RCW 59.12.030(4) (10 days; cure saves the lease). No cure: RCW 59.18.650(2)(c), 59.12.030(5). Warnings: RCW 59.18.650(2)(n)(ii)(A)-(D). Reinstatement: RCW 59.18.410(2). Whether a lease clause declaring every term material is effective was not settled by any section read; RCW 59.18.650(2)(b) itself requires a 'substantial breach of a material program requirement of subsidized housing, material term subscribed to by the tenant within the lease or rental agreement' (the real lease's blanket materiality clause, WA log §15; case law not searched, rule 21). (WA battery 81 (unlawful detainer notices (pay or vacate, comply or vacate)): 30 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic)) (WA battery 204 (material term / material noncompliance): 14 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic)). Read section-open 2026-10-03 from the whole Revised Code of Washington and the whole Washington Administrative Code (app.leg.wa.gov, every chapter page loaded in the built-in browser) and the Washington Constitution, saved and hash-matched (WA log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
