      "Washington abolished the landlord's right of distress for rent. A lease clause creating a lien on the tenant's personal property, or authorizing you to seize it for rent, is void. You may take a tenant's property only with the tenant's specific written consent to that taking, after an abandonment, after a writ of restitution, or after a sole tenant's death, each under its own procedure.",
