    bodyText:
      "You may ask a tenant to designate, in a writing separate from the lease, a person to act on the tenant's death if the tenant lives alone. When a sole occupant dies, promptly mail or hand-deliver (and email if you know an address) a notice to any known personal representative, designated person, emergency contact and likely successor, and to the tenant at the unit, stating the death, rent paid-through date, and that the tenancy ends 15 days after the notice or at the paid-through date, whichever is later, unless a representative arranges to prepay rent for up to 60 days from the death. Release property to a representative who asks in writing, takes an inventory and signs a possession-only acknowledgment. Refund unearned rent and account for the deposit within 30 days after removal. Before selling or disposing of unclaimed property, send a second notice and wait at least 45 days; property worth over $1,000 must be sold in a commercially reasonable manner, and personal papers and photographs may not be sold.",
