      "You may not end, refuse to renew, or refuse to rent because a tenant, applicant or household member is a victim of domestic violence, sexual assault or stalking, or because they ended a lease under the victim-protection statute; doing so is a defense to eviction. Lawful factors unrelated to victim status may still be considered. The tenant-duty rule against assaults and weapon threats leading to arrest does not authorize evicting the victim.",
