      "Washington's statute already makes these tenant duties: no drug-related activity at the premises (and not allowing it with the tenant's knowledge or consent); no imminently hazardous activity involving an assault or unlawful use of a firearm or deadly weapon that leads to an arrest; and no gang-related activity endangering two or more households. Waste, nuisance or unlawful activity affecting others' use and enjoyment lets you serve a 3-day notice to quit with no cure. Neighbors in the same building or complex, or within a one-block radius, whose safety or property is endangered by a tenant's gang activity may serve you a 10-day demand to file an eviction, and may petition the court if you don't investigate, if you investigate and find no gang activity, or if your steps don't stop it. The library offers no separate crime-free clause: the statute covers the ground, a broader lease definition could reach conduct the statute protects (victims), and city crime-free programs may not bar renting to someone solely for criminal history.",
