    topicKey: "term-change-notice",
    bodyText:
      "To change a month-to-month tenancy's terms: new rules take effect after 30 days' written notice to each affected tenant and at the end of the rental period's term (or sooner if the tenant agrees); any increase in rent, including a new or higher recurring fee, needs 90 days' written notice on the state form (30 days and no state form for income-based subsidized tenancies), and, unless an RCW 59.18.710 exemption applies, can't take effect in the first 12 months of the tenancy and must stay within the increase limit. Making month-to-month terms more burdensome than fixed-term terms, or the reverse, is barred, and rents for different lease types on the same unit may differ by no more than 5%.",
