    topicKey: "pool-safety",
    bodyText:
      "Washington's landlord-tenant act has no pool or spa safety rule for rentals, but the state's water recreation facility rules treat a pool or spa at an apartment, condominium or rental housing unit for residents and their guests as a 'limited use pool' subject to the health rules. They don't apply to a pool or spa used only by the residents and invited guests of a single-family home, or of a duplex owned by its residents. A pool only for residents of an apartment complex, or of a group of fewer than 15 rental units (or a mobile home park), is excused from preconstruction design review, routine inspection, and permit or fee requirements; local health departments may read the size limit differently. Check with the local health department.",
