    topicKey: "term-change-notice",
    bodyText:
      "A fixed term lease can't be changed by either party alone during the term. In a periodic tenancy, Oregon sets specific notice periods for some changes: rent increases (seven days week-to-week; 90 days otherwise, and none in the first year); the type or amount of a late charge (30 days); adding a renter's liability insurance requirement to an existing month-to-month tenancy (30 days, with the exceptions summary); requiring a public service charge adopted by a provider or local government within the previous six months, in a month-to-month tenancy (60 days); and a new or increased security deposit (none in the first year except with an agreed change such as a pet; after the first year, at least three months to pay). A new house rule that substantially modifies the bargain needs the tenant's written consent. From January 1, 2027, a landlord may adopt a smoking ban inside units or interior common areas without that consent only under the 2026 act's conditions, including 180 days' written notice.",
