    bodyText:
      "Oregon treats an increase or decrease in the regular rent based on whether the tenant pays by a certain date as a late charge, so an early-payment discount has to meet the late-charge rules. No statute addresses move-in concessions such as a free month; if you offer one, state in the lease whether the stated rent is the rent before or after the concession, since the rent-increase limit is measured from the rent.",
    notes: "OR: ORS 90.260(7). Concessions: present or absent (rule 27): no Oregon statute on move-in concessions was found (OR battery 79 (rent concessions and discounts): 37 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CONST 383, OAR 40864, ORS 39614, SL2026 142); the drafting advice is Claude's. Clawback of a concession on early termination would be liquidated damages unless within ORS 90.302(2)(e) (ORS 90.302(5); Claude's reading). Read section-open 2026-10-04 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole Oregon Revised Statutes (oregonlegislature.gov, 2025 edition, every chapter page with history lines and Notes), the Oregon Constitution, the 2026 session laws as enrolled and the Oregon Administrative Rules (secure.sos.state.or.us). Rule 15: written section-open.",
