    bodyText:
      "Apart from a screening charge, you may take money from an applicant only as a deposit to secure the execution of a rental agreement, after you approve the application and before you both sign, and only after giving a written statement of the rent, fees and deposits, the terms of the agreement to sign and the conditions for refunding or keeping the deposit. When the agreement is signed, you must apply the deposit to the money due under it or refund it immediately. If the applicant fails to sign as agreed, you may keep the deposit, unless the applicant rejected the agreement because of material habitability defects. If you fail to sign, or the applicant rejects for habitability, you must return the deposit within five business days; the applicant can recover the deposit, and late return (unless caused by an act of God) adds a penalty equal to the greater of the deposit or an amount you agreed on.",
