      "A last month's rent deposit is a security deposit in Oregon. You must apply it to the rent for the last month of the tenancy when either of you gives a termination notice (other than a nonpayment notice), when you agree to end the tenancy, or when a fixed term ends under the written agreement, and account for and refund any part you don't apply. Unless you both agree otherwise, the tenant can't make you apply it to any other month, and it does not cap the rent you may charge unless the written agreement says so. Accepting one collected at the beginning of the tenancy is not acceptance of rent that waives a violation.",
