    bodyText:
      "A tenant who is a victim of domestic violence, sexual assault, bias crime or stalking may give you at least 14 days' written notice asking to be released from the rental agreement, naming the release date and any immediate family members to be released, with verification: a protective order, a police report, a conviction, or a statement signed by the tenant and a qualified third party (law enforcement officer, attorney, licensed health professional, Department of Justice victim-services employee or victim's advocate) in the statute's form, showing an incident within the previous 90 days (not counting time the perpetrator was incarcerated or lived more than 100 miles away) or a valid protective order. You must release them. They owe no rent or damages incurred after the release date and no fee solely for the termination, and you may not charge an early termination fee. Other tenants remain bound. You may not disclose the information provided except with the tenant's written consent, for an eviction proceeding, to a qualified third party or as the law requires.",
    notes: "OR: ORS 90.453(1)-(7) ('If a tenant gives a landlord at least 14 days’ written notice, and the notice so requests, the landlord shall release the tenant and any immediate family member of the tenant from the rental agreement' (ORS 90.453(2)(a)); verification form ORS 90.453(3), verbatim form not reproduced here (`edu-statutory-forms-or`)); fee bar ORS 90.302(2)(e); remaining tenants and deposits ORS 90.456. (OR battery 123 (domestic violence, sexual assault, bias crime, stalking (victims)): 39 hits, control 0; known positives passed (3 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CONST 383, OAR 40864, ORS 39614, SL2026 142) Read section-open 2026-10-04 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole Oregon Revised Statutes (oregonlegislature.gov, 2025 edition, every chapter page with history lines and Notes), the Oregon Constitution, the 2026 session laws as enrolled and the Oregon Administrative Rules (secure.sos.state.or.us). Rule 15: written section-open.",
