      "A tenant may end a rental agreement on written notice with proof of official orders if enlisting in the Armed Forces, ordered to active service outside the area for more than 90 days as a member of the National Guard, a reserve component or an active component, ending active service, or on qualifying Public Health Service or NOAA commissioned-corps duty; the termination takes effect on the earlier of any date federal law sets or the latest of 30 days after the notice, 30 days before the reporting date, the date in the notice, or (for ending service) 90 days before the orders take effect. A member of the Oregon organized militia called into state active service for 90 or more consecutive days may end the agreement on written notice with orders, effective the earlier of 30 days after the next rent is due or the last day of the month after the notice month. Neither owes a penalty, fee, charge or loss of deposit for the termination, or rent after the effective date. A court may stay for up to 90 days the eviction of a member of the organized militia called into state active service for 30 or more consecutive days, if the rent is $1,200 a month or less, the dwelling is occupied chiefly by the member's spouse, children or other dependents, and the service materially affects the member's ability to pay.",
