    topicKey: "statutory-early-termination",
    bodyText:
      "Besides the victim and servicemember rights, an Oregon tenant may end the tenancy: on written notice ending the tenancy at least 30 days later (7 for week-to-week) if you materially fail to comply with the lease, or fail to comply with the habitability duty, and don't remedy it (within 7 days for an essential service, 30 days otherwise); on 48 hours' notice if a failure to supply an essential service poses an imminent and serious threat; immediately if the unit is posted unsafe for conditions the tenant didn't cause, or if conditions existing at the start that the tenant didn't cause pose an imminent and serious threat within six months; on 72 hours' notice (or immediately before move-in) if a utility the tenant must pay can't be obtained because of a prior tenant's or the owner's debt, or a landlord-paid utility is shut off for nonpayment; after an unlawful lockout or a willful utility shutoff; after an unlawful or unreasonable entry, or repeated harassing demands for entry, through the 30-day notice-and-remedy procedure for landlord noncompliance; during a fixed term, on 30 days' notice after you give a qualifying-reason notice for the end of the term; and during a fixed term after a foreclosure notice, on 60 days' notice unless within 30 days you give written evidence from a lender or trustee that the property is no longer in foreclosure, or written evidence that a court has appointed a receiver. A tenancy in a unit destroyed in a natural disaster (including a disaster resulting in a state of emergency declared under ORS 401.165 or 401.309 for wildfires, floods, tsunamis, earthquakes or similar events) ends immediately unless the parties agree otherwise after the disaster (not for facility space rentals). The lease can't waive these rights.",
    notes: "OR: ORS 90.360(1); ORS 90.365(2); ORS 90.380(5)(a), (7); ORS 90.315(5)-(7); ORS 90.375; ORS 90.322(8); ORS 90.372; ORS 90.367 (read: foreclosure). Waiver bar: 'Agrees to waive or forgo rights or remedies under this chapter' (ORS 90.245(1)(a)); Or. Laws 2026, ch. 108, § 21(1), (4) (added to ORS 90.100 to 90.465 by § 20; effective June 5, 2026, § 31; 'natural disaster' as defined in ORS 197A.440); ORS 90.367(6)(a)-(b); ORS 90.360(1)(a). Present (rule 27). Read section-open 2026-10-04 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole Oregon Revised Statutes (oregonlegislature.gov, 2025 edition, every chapter page with history lines and Notes), the Oregon Constitution, the 2026 session laws as enrolled and the Oregon Administrative Rules (secure.sos.state.or.us). Rule 15: written section-open.",
