      "Oregon has no special termination rule for a tenant's death; the tenancy and the estate's obligations follow the rental agreement and general law. When a sole tenant dies and leaves property, the abandoned property statute applies with changes: an heir, devisee, personal representative or a person the tenant designated in writing to be contacted on death has the tenant's rights to the property, and your notice must go by first class mail to the tenant at the premises, to any of those people you actually know of, and to an estate administrator of the State Treasurer.",
