      "On a former tenant's motion, the court must set aside the judgment and seal the records of an eviction case that ended in the tenant's favor or in dismissal, a stipulated judgment the tenant complied with (with any money award satisfied), or a judgment of restitution (with any money award satisfied) entered at least five years earlier or, until January 2, 2028, based on claims arising between April 1, 2020 and March 1, 2022. Each court also sets aside and seals, once a year, judgments with no unexpired or unsatisfied money award: restitution judgments at least five years old and dismissals or judgments for the tenant at least 12 months old. A set-aside judgment is treated as never entered. When screening you may not consider dismissed actions, judgments for the applicant or judgments five or more years old, and, until January 2, 2028, judgments on claims arising between April 1, 2020 and March 1, 2022.",
