      "You may take possession only after an abandonment or relinquishment or through the court process. Removing or excluding a tenant, or seriously attempting or threatening to, or willfully cutting heat, running water, hot water, electricity or another essential service, lets the tenant get a court order restoring possession or end the tenancy and recover up to two months' rent or twice actual damages, whichever is greater; the tenant can also recover damages without ending the tenancy. Distraint for rent is abolished, and a lien on the tenant's household goods is unenforceable unless perfected before October 5, 1973.",
