      "Oregon prescribes several forms landlords use: the notice that must appear in an e-mail service addendum ('THIS IS AN IMPORTANT NOTICE ABOUT YOUR RIGHTS REGARDING RECEIPT OF WRITTEN NOTICES'); the qualified third-party verification a victim may use to end a tenancy; the eviction complaint and summons forms; the notice of rental assistance from the Oregon Judicial Department that goes with nonpayment notices and summonses; the foreclosure purchaser's notice to residential tenants; and agency forms for affordability-restriction notices and (from 2027) well-water test results. Use the current versions; the court forms are on the Oregon Judicial Department's website.",
