      "An agreement to lease real property for longer than one year is void unless it, or a note or memorandum of it expressing the consideration, is in writing and signed by the party to be charged or that party's authorized agent. A rental agreement may otherwise be oral, but a late charge, fees, a renter's insurance requirement, utility billing and several other terms are enforceable in Oregon only if they are in a written rental agreement, and a week-to-week tenancy needs a written agreement.",
