    topicKey: "scope",
    bodyText:
      "Oregon's Residential Landlord and Tenant Act (ORS chapter 90) covers most residential rentals. It does not cover: residence at an institution incidental to detention or to medical, geriatric, educational, counseling, religious or similar services (off-campus non-dormitory housing is covered); a buyer's or seller's occupancy of up to 90 days around a sale; fraternal or social organization housing; transient occupancy in a hotel or motel; squatters; vacation occupancies (up to 45 days and not a principal residence, or up to 90 days for a recreational vehicle park space on the statute's conditions); an employee's occupancy conditioned on employment on the premises; condominium owners and cooperative proprietary lessees; agricultural rentals; and licensed treatment and care programs. Rentals of spaces in manufactured dwelling parks and floating home marinas (ORS 90.505 to 90.850) follow special rules that the library's lease does not cover. A tenant may be a minor in the circumstances the minors' housing statute allows. Arrangements created to avoid the act are covered anyway.",
    notes: "OR: ORS 90.110(1)-(9) ('Unless created to avoid the application of this chapter, the following arrangements are not governed by this chapter' (ORS 90.110)); ORS 90.113; ORS 90.100 ('Vacation occupancy', 'Tenant'); ORS 90.505-90.850 (facility series, ORS 90.120(3); read whole; flagged, not covered; kickoff lead 12); ORS 90.860-90.875 (notices on the sale of a manufactured dwelling or floating home with a lien, read; not rules for ordinary tenancies); ORS 90.120 (general statutes displaced). Employee occupancy ends under ORS 91.120 (ORS 90.110(7)); ORS 91.122 covers employees of a resident. ORS 90.100(55)(a)-(b) (vacation occupancy; (54) in the 2025 edition, renumbered when Or. Laws 2026, ch. 23, § 4 added 'tenant portal', effective June 5, 2026). Group recovery homes: ORS 90.440. Read section-open 2026-10-04 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole Oregon Revised Statutes (oregonlegislature.gov, 2025 edition, every chapter page with history lines and Notes), the Oregon Constitution, the 2026 session laws as enrolled and the Oregon Administrative Rules (secure.sos.state.or.us). Rule 15: written section-open.",
