      "A rental agreement may not provide that the tenant waives rights or remedies under the landlord-tenant act, authorizes a confession of judgment, agrees to excuse or limit your liability for your own willful misconduct or negligence (or to indemnify you for it), or agrees to pay liquidated damages other than the capped early-termination fee; such a term is unenforceable. Other provisions Oregon voids or bars in leases: fees not on the statute's list, including any move-in fee for an expected expense; waivers of the abandoned-property procedure; renter's insurance terms outside the statute; requiring payment by electronic means; a lien on household goods; and receiving rent free of the habitability duty. A lease may include an informal dispute resolution provision despite the waiver ban.",
