      "If you deliberately use a rental agreement containing a provision you know is prohibited and try to enforce it, the tenant may recover actual damages plus up to three months' periodic rent. Charging a fee the fee statute doesn't allow costs twice the tenant's actual damages or $300, whichever is greater, and collecting a charge that neither the agreement nor the law authorizes can also be an unlawful collection practice.",
