    topicKey: "fair-housing",
    bodyText:
      "Oregon bars housing discrimination because of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, marital status, familial status, source of income (including Section 8 and other housing assistance) and disability, in renting, terms, advertising, and coercion or interference. A facially neutral policy with a disparate adverse impact on a protected class can violate the law, considering its business purpose and less discriminatory alternatives. Exemptions are narrow: familial status for qualifying housing for older persons; sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and familial status for renting space in an owner-occupied single-family home with shared common space (but not for advertising a preference); and sex where the property requires shared bath or bedroom facilities by unrelated persons of the opposite sex. Except as a federal rent-subsidy or affordable-rent program requires, Oregon's landlord-tenant act also bars discrimination against an applicant, tenant or household member based on actual or perceived immigration or citizenship status, and asking about that status. Local ordinances may add classes.",
    notes: "OR: ORS 659A.421(1)-(9) ('A person may not, because of the race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, marital status, familial status or source of income of any person' (ORS 659A.421(2))); ORS 659A.145 (disability); ORS 659A.425 ('“Facially neutral housing policy” means a guideline, practice, rule or screening or admission criterion, regarding a real property transaction, that applies equally to all persons' (ORS 659A.425(1)(a))); Owner-occupied exemption: ORS 659A.421(8) (does not reach (2)(e), advertising); opposite-sex shared facilities ORS 659A.421(6). Remedies ORS 659A.885 (named, read for scope; amended by Or. Laws 2026, ch. 57, effective June 5, 2026, not relied on); ORS 90.306(1), (3); ORS 90.388(2). (OR battery 102 (source of income and housing assistance): 213 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CONST 383, OAR 40864, ORS 39614, SL2026 142) (OR battery 117 (occupancy by children / familial status): 100 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CONST 383, OAR 40864, ORS 39614, SL2026 142) Read section-open 2026-10-04 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole Oregon Revised Statutes (oregonlegislature.gov, 2025 edition, every chapter page with history lines and Notes), the Oregon Constitution, the 2026 session laws as enrolled and the Oregon Administrative Rules (secure.sos.state.or.us). Rule 15: written section-open.",
