    topicKey: "source-of-income",
    bodyText:
      "You may not refuse to rent, set different terms, discourage, advertise a preference or otherwise discriminate because of source of income, which includes federal rent subsidies (Section 8) and any other local, state or federal housing assistance; it doesn't include income from a particular occupation or illegal income. You may still refuse based on an applicant's inability to pay rent, but only after taking the value of the applicant's housing assistance into account, and only consistently with fair housing laws.",
    notes: "OR: ORS 659A.421(1)(d), (2)(a)(B) ('Source of income” includes federal rent subsidy payments under 42 U.S.C. 1437f and any other local, state or federal housing assistance' (ORS 659A.421(1)(d)(A))). (OR battery 102 (source of income and housing assistance): 213 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CONST 383, OAR 40864, ORS 39614, SL2026 142) Read section-open 2026-10-04 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole Oregon Revised Statutes (oregonlegislature.gov, 2025 edition, every chapter page with history lines and Notes), the Oregon Constitution, the 2026 session laws as enrolled and the Oregon Administrative Rules (secure.sos.state.or.us). Rule 15: written section-open.",
