      "You may not ask about the immigration or citizenship status of an applicant, tenant or household member (except where a federal housing program requires it), and you may not reject an applicant for lacking a Social Security number or proof of lawful presence if the applicant offers the identification the statute lists, which includes an individual taxpayer identification number, a passport, a driver license or any government identification regardless of expiration, and certain non-government combinations. You may not discriminate based on actual or perceived immigration status, or disclose or threaten to disclose immigration status to harass, retaliate or intimidate; violations are treated like other discrimination and are unlawful practices under the civil rights law.",
