      "A rule about the tenant's use and occupancy is enforceable only if it promotes tenants' convenience, safety or welfare, protects your property from abusive use or fairly distributes services and facilities; is reasonably related to that purpose; applies fairly to all tenants; is explicit enough to tell tenants what to do; isn't meant to evade your obligations; and the tenant had written notice of it on signing or when it was adopted. A rule adopted later that substantially modifies the bargain needs the tenant's written consent; from January 1, 2027, an indoor smoking ban adopted under the 2026 act's conditions is an exception. Rules become part of the rental agreement. Fees for repeated rule violations are limited to the statute's list.",
