    topicKey: "smoking-policy",
    bodyText:
      "Every Oregon rental agreement (other than for a space in a manufactured dwelling or floating home facility) must disclose the smoking policy: prohibited on the premises, allowed on the entire premises, or allowed in limited areas (identified). From January 1, 2027, the statute defines smoking as inhaling or possessing a lit tobacco product, and you may change the policy during a tenancy to ban smoking inside units or interior common areas without the tenant's written consent only if the unit shares a wall with another unit or was developed under a development agreement, it isn't an accessible unit, the change doesn't apply to a fixed term until the term ends, you provide at least one posted designated smoking area on the premises, and you give 180 days' written notice. A fee for smoking in a clearly designated nonsmoking area is allowed only under the rule-violation fee statute (up to $250, 24 hours after a warning). Statewide indoor clean air rules may reach staffed or public common areas.",
