    bodyText:
      "You may have a vehicle removed only as the landlord towing statute and the private-property towing statutes allow. Without notice, only if it blocks emergency access or entry, violates a prominently posted prohibition, is in a disabled space or a non-parking area, is in a reserved but unassigned tenant space without a tag (and only if you provide tags and have the written agreements the statute requires), or is in a space assigned to a tenant with that tenant's agreement at the time of the tow (you may not require tenants to agree in advance). An inoperable vehicle parked under your agreement may be removed after a prominent notice affixed at least 72 hours before. You may not tow because a registration has expired or is invalid. Posted guest spaces need readable signs, and parking facilities need tow signs under the general towing law. You may not require a nonremovable tag that reveals where the tenant lives. No Oregon statute authorizes a landlord to boot a vehicle.",
