      "Whether association rules bind a tenant depends on the association's governing documents; no Oregon statute binds tenants to them generally. You may pass association assessments through to the tenant only if the written rental agreement sets out that requirement at the start of the tenancy and you give the tenant a copy of the assessment before or when you charge it. The statute's conditions read together cover move-in and move-out charges most clearly; for a fine caused by the tenant's rule violation, the safer route is to recover it as damages for the tenant's breach of the lease. You may prohibit a family child care use that the association's governing documents don't allow, even though a landlord otherwise can't bar a certified or registered family child care home the tenant has told you about.",
