    topicKey: "utility-shutoff-statute",
    bodyText:
      "When the account holder isn't the occupant, regulated utilities must warn the tenants before shutting off service: an energy utility gives occupants a five-day notice addressed to 'tenant' or 'occupant' and, for a master-metered multifamily building, notifies the Public Utility Commission at least five business days ahead; a regulated water utility sends a duplicate notice to the service address and, for a master-metered building, a seven-day notice to each unit. If you are responsible for a utility under the lease and it is shut off for nonpayment, the tenant may pay it and deduct the amount from rent, or end the tenancy on 72 hours' notice unless you restore service within the 72 hours. A regulated water utility must also tell the Public Utility Commission seven days before shutting off a master-metered building.",
    notes: "OR: OAR 860-021-0326(1)-(2) ('the utility must provide a five-day disconnect notice to the occupants of the premises' (OAR 860-021-0326(1))); OAR 860-021-0405(6); OAR 860-036-1550(1)-(3) ('The water utility must notify the Consumer Services Section at least seven calendar days before disconnecting service to a master-metered, multi-dwelling premise' (OAR 860-036-1550(3))); OAR 860-037-0230 (wastewater). These rules bind utilities the Public Utility Commission regulates; ORS 91.255 sets no pre-shutoff tenant notice for municipal utilities: it limits transferring a tenant's claim to the owner (ORS 91.255(2)-(3)), bars shutting off a later tenant over a previous tenant's debt without the owner notice (ORS 91.255(4)) and requires the same disconnection policy for tenant- and owner-occupied single-family homes (ORS 91.255(6)). ORS 90.315(7)(a)-(b). (OR battery 59 (utility disconnection rules reaching landlords and tenants): 10 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CONST 383, OAR 40864, ORS 39614, SL2026 142) (OR battery 230 (interruption or failure of utilities and essential services (rerun of 212)): 39 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CONST 383, OAR 40864, ORS 39614, SL2026 142) `edu-utility-landlord-account-or`. Read section-open 2026-10-04 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole Oregon Revised Statutes (oregonlegislature.gov, 2025 edition, every chapter page with history lines and Notes), the Oregon Constitution, the 2026 session laws as enrolled and the Oregon Administrative Rules (secure.sos.state.or.us). Rule 15: written section-open.",
