    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "landlord-maintenance",
    bodyText:
      "For residential property, you must deliver the dwelling unit and surrounding premises in fit and habitable condition at the start of the tenancy and keep them that way; keep the property in line with applicable health, safety, fire and housing codes; make all repairs needed to keep it fit and habitable; and keep in good and safe working order the electrical, plumbing, sanitary, heating, ventilating, air-conditioning and other facilities and appliances, including elevators, that you supply or must supply by written or oral agreement or by law. In a building with more than one living unit, you must also keep common areas under your control clean, safe and in repair and provide appropriate facilities for removing ashes, garbage, rubbish and other waste. The code and repair duties do not cover a code violation caused by the fault of the tenant, the tenant's family or someone on the premises with the tenant's consent, or repairs needed primarily because of that person's lack of reasonable care. You are not required to make repairs while the tenant is behind on rent, but if your lease gives you a greater duty than the statute, the lease controls; the Landlord Maintenance clause this library uses for West Virginia promises repairs without an exception for unpaid rent, so if you use it, do not rely on the unpaid-rent excuse. The statute sets no repair deadline and no reporting procedure, so say in the lease how tenants should report problems.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 37-6-30(a)(1)-(6) ('With respect to residential property'; (a)(2) code duty 'unless the failure to meet those requirements is the fault of the tenant, a member of his family or other person on the premises with his consent'; (a)(4) repairs 'unless said repairs were necessitated primarily by a lack of reasonable care by the tenant, a member of his family or other person on the premises with his consent'; (a)(5) facilities and appliances 'supplied or required to be supplied by him by written or oral agreement or by law'), (b) (a greater lease duty controls: 'that portion of the rental agreement imposing a greater duty shall control'), (c) ('None of the provisions of this section shall be deemed to require the landlord to make repairs when the tenant is in arrears in payment of rent'), (d) ('multiple housing unit' defined). Heat and water: `edu-heating-wv`. No repair deadline statute (WV battery a-repair-timeline (deadlines for a landlord to make repairs after notice): 4 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery a-repair-timeline-nc (deadlines for a landlord to make repairs after notice (no context limb)): 12 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (hits are mine safety, deed correction, goods leases and other non-tenancy sections). Other habitability statutes (WV battery a-habitability-r2 (fit and habitable condition or warranty of habitability (scan for other habitability duties)): 9 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery a-habitability-r2-nc (fit and habitable condition or warranty of habitability (scan for other habitability duties) (no context limb)): 11 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205): code enforcement only (`edu-receivership-wv`). Because § 37-6-30(b) makes a greater lease duty control, the shared `landlord-maintenance` clause's wording (no arrears exception; its fault exception reaches only improper use by Tenant or a guest) may bind the landlord beyond the statute (Claude's reading; the clause is tagged, see its WV tag note and `edu-condemned-premises-wv`). Topics `other-landlord-facilities`, `stove-refrigerator`, `promises-to-repair` and `habitability-materiality` answered here (oral promises of facilities count under (a)(5); the statute has no materiality threshold). Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
