    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute says whether a lease may shift your statutory repair and habitability duties to the tenant or have the tenant waive them, and none sets a procedure, such as a separate signed agreement, for doing so. The habitability statute excuses you only where the tenant, the tenant's family or someone on the premises with the tenant's consent caused the code violation or the need for repair, and it says a lease that gives you a greater duty controls; it does not say a lease may reduce your duties. Whether a court would enforce a reduction or waiver is a question of case law, which was not searched, so keep tenant maintenance terms to routine tasks and do not use them to take away the statutory duties. A tenant's promise to leave the premises in good repair means returning them in good and substantial repair, reasonable wear and tear excepted, and does not oblige the tenant to rebuild or pay for buildings destroyed by fire or otherwise without the tenant's fault or negligence unless other words in the lease show that intent.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 37-6-30(a)(2), (a)(4) (fault exceptions), (b) (greater lease duty controls). A lessee's covenant 'that he will leave the premises in good repair' means surrender 'in good and substantial repair and condition, reasonable wear and tear excepted' (W. Va. Code § 36-4-12); no rebuilding duty after destruction 'without fault or negligence on his part' 'unless there be other words showing it to be the intent of the parties that he should be so bound' (W. Va. Code § 36-4-13). No delegation, separate-writing or waiver statute (WV battery a-tenant-repair-agree-r3 (agreements that the tenant will make repairs or perform the landlord's maintenance duties (rerun)): 5 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery a-tenant-repair-agree-r3-nc (agreements that the tenant will make repairs or perform the landlord's maintenance duties (rerun) (no context limb)): 5 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (hits: §§ 36-4-12, -13; UCC goods leases §§ 46-2A-309, -310; a watershed compact) (WV battery habitability-waiver (waiving habitability or repair duties): 11 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery habitability-waiver-nc (waiving habitability or repair duties (no context limb)): 15 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (hits are tax exemptions, energy-savings contracts and other non-tenancy sections). Shared `tenant-maintenance`, `landscaping-irrigation` and `snow-removal` are tagged. Topics `habitability-waiver`, `habitability-modifiable`, `maintenance-duty-shift` and `part5-nonwaivable` answered here. Case law on waiver of the warranty of habitability not searched. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
