      "West Virginia's habitability statute requires you to keep a rental in line with applicable health, safety, fire and housing codes, but the codes themselves are not in the statutes. The State Fire Code, a legislative rule of the State Fire Commission, has the force of law statewide as a minimum standard; a stricter local fire ordinance governs only if the Fire Commission has approved it. The State Building Code applies only in counties and cities that adopt it, and only prospectively. Counties may adopt building and housing codes, cities may regulate construction and unsafe buildings, and local boards of health administer housing sanitation and may adopt local health rules with county or city approval. The State Fire Marshal may order an owner to repair or demolish a hazardous building within 30 days, and the cost can become a lien. Check with your city or county; none of these codes or rules was read here.",
