    topicKey: "portfolio-thresholds",
    bodyText:
      "West Virginia's landlord-tenant statutes do not change your duties based on how many units you own. Some rules turn on the building instead: common-area and garbage duties apply in buildings with more than one living unit, and the statutory smoke detector rule covers one- and two-family dwellings. Fair housing law applies to all dwellings, but the state discrimination rules largely do not reach renting rooms in a rooming house where you live with no more than four rooms rented. For familial status only, there are two exemptions: a single-family house rented by a private individual owner who owns no more than three such houses, without a broker or anyone in the business of renting and without discriminatory advertising; and units in a building for no more than four families where you live in one of them. Federal fair housing law was not read.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 16B-18-4(a) (all dwellings; owner-occupied rooming house 'containing no more than four rented rooms or rooms to be rented'; 'Solely for the purposes of familial status'; (a)(1) 'does not own more than three such single-family houses at any one time', (A)-(B); (a)(2) 'no more than four families living independently of each other, if the owner actually maintains and occupies one of such living quarters as his residence'), (b) (in the business: three or more rentals as principal in 12 months, or owner of a dwelling for five or more families). The rooming-house sentence excepts 'subsection (b) of this section', apparently meant to be the advertising rule in § 16B-18-5(c) (Claude's reading; flagged as a cross-reference error). W. Va. Code § 37-6-30(a)(3), (6), (d); W. Va. Code § 15A-10-12(a); W. Va. Code § 37-6A-6(a) (deposit article: all residential units). Accessible design applies to 'covered multifamily dwellings' of four or more units (W. Va. Code § 16B-18-5(f)(7)). Searched (WV battery a-portfolio (duties keyed to how many units or houses an owner owns): 2 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery a-portfolio-nc (duties keyed to how many units or houses an owner owns (no context limb)): 4 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (other hits: home-loan settlement rules, consumer-credit exclusions). Topic `repair-escrow-exemption-notice` (OH) has no West Virginia counterpart. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
