    ruleTypes: ["CONSTRAINED"],
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "abandoned-property",
    bodyText:
      "If a tenant who owes rent abandons the property, West Virginia law sets the steps. First post a written notice in a conspicuous place on the property requiring the tenant to pay the rent within one month; if it is not paid, you are entitled to possession and may enter, the tenant's right to the property ends, and you may recover the rent owed up to that time. To dispose of belongings left behind, give a second written notice, posted on the property and sent by first-class mail with a certificate of mailing, in an envelope marked \"Please Forward\", to the rental, to any post office box of the tenant you know of, and to any forwarding address you have. It must say the property is considered abandoned and that belongings must be removed from the property (or from where you stored them) by a stated date at least 30 days after mailing, or at least 60 days if the tenant has told you they are on active duty in the U.S. Armed Forces, or the tenant forfeits them and they become yours. If belongings worth more than $300 are not removed by that date and the tenant or a secured creditor tells you they intend to remove them, you must store them for up to 30 more days, provided they pay your reasonable storage and removal costs. The statute covers only a tenant who abandons while owing rent; no statute sets a procedure for belongings left by a tenant who owed nothing, so following the same notice steps is the safe course. Belongings left after a court-ordered eviction follow separate rules.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 37-6-6(a) (posted notice 'requiring the tenant to pay the rent within one month'; possession, entry and end of the tenant's right if unpaid; rent 'up to the time when he or she became entitled to possession'), (c)(1)-(2) (posting; 'first-class mail with a certificate of mailing'; envelope endorsed Please Forward; leased property, known post office box, forwarding address), (d)(1)-(3) (contents; not less than thirty days, or sixty days if the tenant has given notice of active duty; forfeiture to the landlord), (e) (worth more than $300; up to thirty additional days on notice of intent to remove and payment of reasonable storage and removal costs). The landlord may dispose 'without incurring any liability to the tenant or any other person' (W. Va. Code § 37-6-6(c)). Housing authority variant where rent is not a condition of the lease: § 37-6-6(b). Scope: subsection (a) reaches 'any tenant from whom rent is in arrears and unpaid' (W. Va. Code § 37-6-6(a)); no statute governs belongings left by a tenant who owed no rent (Claude's reading of § 37-6-6, read whole) (WV battery abandoned-property (belongings left behind by a tenant): 23 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery abandoned-property-nc (belongings left behind by a tenant (no context limb)): 53 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery b-left-property-ev (property left behind or remaining on rented premises (everyday rerun)): 6 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery b-left-property-ev-nc (property left behind or remaining on rented premises (everyday rerun) (no context limb)): 11 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205); hits other than §§ 37-6-6 and 55-3A-3 concern tax sales, foreclosure purchasers (§ 38-1-17 reaches only the previous owner), self-storage liens, vehicles, squatter removal and lot rentals (§ 55-3B-6, out of scope). Shared `surrender-end-of-term` hedges its disposal sentence to the extent permitted by applicable law, which fits. After an order for possession: `edu-post-eviction-property-wv`. Rent and reletting after abandonment: `edu-abandonment-mitigation-wv`. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
