      "No West Virginia statute requires a pay-or-quit notice, or any other notice, before you file to evict for unpaid rent; a summary eviction petition may be filed once the tenant is in arrears. The exceptions: if the tenant has abandoned the property, you use the posted notice requiring payment within one month; the federal CARES Act may require 30 days' notice to vacate for some properties (see that row); and you should honor any notice or waiting period your own lease promises. A tenant may defend by showing that you breached a material covenant on which the duty to pay rent depends. This library does not offer a clause waiving a nonpayment notice, because there is no statutory notice to waive.",
    notes: "WV: Confirmed absent: (WV battery nonpayment-notice (notice before suing for unpaid rent (pay or quit)): 0 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 2 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery nonpayment-notice-nc (notice before suing for unpaid rent (pay or quit) (no context limb)): 0 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 2 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery b-nonpayment-ev (notice or demand to pay rent (everyday rerun)): 1 hit, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery b-nonpayment-ev-nc (notice or demand to pay rent (everyday rerun) (no context limb)): 1 hit, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (the everyday rerun's only hit is the abandonment notice, W. Va. Code § 37-6-6(a)). Petition ground: 'in arrears in the payment of rent' (W. Va. Code § 55-3A-1(a)(3)). Defense: 'breach by the landlord of a material covenant upon which the duty to pay rent depends' (W. Va. Code § 55-3A-3(b)). Lease-fixed time before reentry: W. Va. Code § 37-6-19. Tender before trial in ejectment or unlawful detainer: `edu-redemption-wv`. Federal: `edu-cares-act-notice`. Lease: `default-by-tenant-wv` (no nonpayment notice). Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
