      "West Virginia has no separate expedited eviction or no-notice termination for criminal or drug activity by a tenant. The ordinary summary procedure is already quick, with a hearing 5 to 10 judicial days after filing, and is available when a tenant breaches a lease covenant, so a lease term against criminal activity lets you act on it promptly. Know your exposure as an owner: real property used to commit or facilitate a drug offense punishable by more than a year in prison can be forfeited to the state, unless the owner shows the act or omission happened without the owner's knowledge or consent, so act promptly once you learn of drug activity. Nuisance laws that can close a property or require evictions are in the nuisance row.",
