    title: "Tenants' Statutory Rights to End a Lease Early",
    group: "Default & Termination",
    states: ["WV"],
    ruleTypes: ["CONSTRAINED"],
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "statutory-early-termination",
    bodyText:
      "West Virginia statutes give a residential tenant, or the tenant's estate, these rights to end a lease early: when a tenant dies, an heir, personal representative, devisee or assignee may end the lease by written notice (see the tenant-death row); if the buildings are destroyed or damaged by fire or otherwise without the tenant's fault or negligence and you do not rebuild as soon as you reasonably can, the tenant may surrender possession after that reasonable time and owe no further rent; and if the whole property is taken by eminent domain, the tenant's liability for rent ends unless the lease expressly provides otherwise. Federal law adds servicemember rights, which West Virginia extends to Guard members on state active duty for 30 days or more. No West Virginia statute gives tenants an early-termination right for domestic violence, illness, disability or a move to a care facility. The lease's Early Termination terms keep these rights.",
    notes: "WV: Death: W. Va. Code § 37-6-11(b) (`edu-tenant-death-wv`). Casualty: W. Va. Code § 37-6-28 (`casualty-wv`). Eminent domain: W. Va. Code § 37-6-29 (whole taking ends rent 'unless the lease expressly provide otherwise'; partial taking reduces rent proportionally; `edu-eminent-domain-wv`, lead). Guard: W. Va. Code § 15-1F-11(b) (`edu-servicemember-rights-wv`). Absent: (WV battery b-dv-terminate (lease termination by a victim of domestic violence, stalking or sexual assault): 0 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery b-dv-terminate-nc (lease termination by a victim of domestic violence, stalking or sexual assault (no context limb)): 3 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery dv (domestic violence, protective orders and tenancy): 4 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (domestic violence; hits are confidentiality and data sections and § 48-27-503); (WV battery b-infirmity (tenant lease termination for disability, illness, age or care-facility admission): 1 hit, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery b-infirmity-nc (tenant lease termination for disability, illness, age or care-facility admission (no context limb)): 2 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery medical-termination (tenant early termination for health or nursing home admission): 31 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (illness, disability, care facility; hits are smoke detectors, licensing and unrelated sections). Domestic violence: `edu-no-dv-lease-termination-wv`. Shared `early-termination-ks` saves rights under applicable law. Federal SCRA not read. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
