    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "termination-notice",
    bodyText:
      "To end a year-to-year tenancy, either side must give the other written notice at least three months before the end of a year of the tenancy. A periodic tenancy with a period shorter than a year, such as month-to-month or week-to-week, may be ended by the same notice or by notice of at least one full rental period before the end of a rental period: for month-to-month, at least a full rental month before the last day of a rental month; for week-to-week, at least a full week before the end of a rental week. No notice is needed from either side to end a lease whose term ends on a set date. Notice to the tenant may be served on the tenant or on anyone holding the property under the tenant; notice from the tenant may be served on any owner or the owner's agent. These rules do not apply where the lease, by special agreement, fixes a different notice period or provides that no notice is to be given, so check your lease. This library offers an optional clause, as that special agreement, letting either party end a periodic tenancy on a stated number of days' written notice before the end of a rental period; it does not offer a no-notice term, because that would let either side end the tenancy without warning. Give every notice in writing and keep proof of delivery.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 37-6-5 ('at least three months prior to the end of any year'; 'A periodic tenancy, in which the period is less than one year, may be terminated by like notice, or by notice for one full period before the end of any period.'; service on the tenant or 'anyone holding under him'; by the tenant on an owner, the owner's agent 'or according to the common law'; 'This section shall not apply where, by special agreement, some other period of notice is fixed, or no notice is to be given; nor shall notice be necessary from or to a tenant whose term is to end at a certain time.'). Whether the one-full-period notice must be written is not stated (the three-month notice is 'in writing'); the body advises writing (Claude's reading). The month-to-month and week-to-week illustrations are Claude's reading of 'one full period'. Rule 37: year-to-year, shorter periodic and fixed-term rules stated separately. Optional clause `termination-notice-wv` (offered as the § 37-6-5 special agreement; a no-notice term is declined); topic `notice-to-quit-waiver` (PA) answered here and in WV log §6.1. Periodic screens: (WV battery periodic-notice (notice to end a periodic or month-to-month tenancy): 11 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery periodic-notice-nc (notice to end a periodic or month-to-month tenancy (no context limb)): 56 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205). Tenancy at will: `edu-tenancy-at-will-wv`. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
