    topicKey: "tenancy-at-will",
    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute defines a tenancy at will or says how much notice ends one. The notice statute covers year-to-year tenancies (written notice at least three months before the end of a year) and periodic tenancies shorter than a year (that notice, or notice of one full rental period before the end of a period), and requires no notice for a term that ends on a set date. Whether an arrangement with no set term or rent period is a tenancy at will, and what notice ends it, is a question of case law; if rent is paid by the week or month, treat it as a periodic tenancy and give at least one full period's written notice.",
