    topicKey: "minor-tenant-filing",
    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute bars naming a minor (a person under 18) as a defendant in an eviction or unlawful detainer case. A magistrate may not enter a default judgment against a minor unless the minor is represented in the case by a guardian ad litem, guardian or similar fiduciary, so name the adults who signed the lease or hold the tenancy, and name a minor only if the minor is a party to it. Whether a minor's own lease can be enforced against the minor is a question of case law; a promise made after turning 18 to pay a debt incurred as a minor can be enforced only if it is in writing and signed.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 50-4-10(a)(2)(A) ('No judgment by default shall be rendered against a person who is an infant, incompetent person or incarcerated convict unless such person is represented in the action by a guardian ad litem, guardian, committee, curator or other like fiduciary.'); Magistrate Court Civil Rule 10(d) (saved rules). 'Minor' means persons under the age of 18 years (W. Va. Code § 2-2-10(a)(7)); reading 'infant' as a minor is Claude's reading. Writing: W. Va. Code § 55-1-1(b). Confirmed absent (bar on naming minors): (WV battery b-minor (minors as tenants or as defendants in possession cases): 12 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery b-minor-nc (minors as tenants or as defendants in possession cases (no context limb)): 37 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (hits include § 37-1-1 on fiduciaries renewing leases for persons under disability and § 48-27-503; none bars minors as defendants). Case law not searched. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
