      "No West Virginia statute requires a landlord to disclose bed bugs or a past infestation to a tenant, or sets bed bug treatment duties for rental housing. The state's only bed bug statute applies to hotels with ten or more bed chambers. Your general duties still apply: you must deliver and keep a residential unit fit and habitable, meet applicable health and housing codes, and make the repairs needed to keep it habitable, except where the problem is the fault of, or caused by a lack of reasonable care by, the tenant, a member of the tenant's family or another person on the premises with the tenant's consent.",
