      "Under the West Virginia Fair Housing Act you must make reasonable accommodations in your rules, policies, practices and services when they may be necessary to give a person with a disability equal opportunity to use and enjoy a home, and you must permit reasonable modifications of the premises, at the tenant's expense, that may be necessary for full enjoyment of the premises. Where reasonable, you may condition permission for a modification on the tenant agreeing to restore the interior at move-out, reasonable wear and tear excepted. For an assistance animal you may ask for documentation from a professional treatment provider of the disability-related need, but not for medical records or detailed information about the impairment; you may not unreasonably deny it, condition it on a fee, a deposit or the terms you apply to pets, or unreasonably delay your response, and you may deny it if there is credible evidence, based on an individualized assessment of the specific animal's actual conduct, that it poses a direct threat to others' health or safety, or would cause substantial physical damage to others' property, that no other reasonable accommodation can eliminate or reduce. You need not rent to someone whose tenancy would be a direct threat to others' health or safety or would cause substantial physical damage to others' property, but you bear the burden of proving it. Buildings of four or more units first occupied after the Act's design deadline must meet accessible design rules (every unit if the building has an elevator, otherwise the ground-floor units).",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 16B-18-5(f)(3)(A) ('the landlord may where it is reasonable to do so condition permission for a modification on the renter agreeing to restore the interior of the premises to the condition that existed before the modification, reasonable wear and tear excepted'), (B), (C), (7) (covered multifamily dwellings, first occupancy after the thirty-month date), (9) ('The burden of proving such threat to health or safety or the likelihood of such damage is upon the respondent'), (10)(A)-(D) (assistance animals: 'may not be unreasonably denied, conditioned on payment of a fee or deposit or other terms and conditions applied to applicants or residents with pets'). 'Assistance animal' weighs 'less than 150 pounds' (W. Va. Code § 16B-18-3(p)); 'Disability' excludes current illegal use of a controlled substance (W. Va. Code § 16B-18-3(g)). Exemptions as in `edu-fair-housing-wv` (the familial-status-only exemptions do not reach disability). Restoration condition need not be in the lease (Claude's reading). Shared `assistance-animal-accommodation` and `no-alterations` tagged. Federal law not read. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
