    topicKey: "property-tax-rent-disclosure",
    bodyText:
      "West Virginia gives property tax relief to residents aged 65 or older, including renters, whose gross household income in the prior year was not more than $5,000, counting 12 percent of the rent they pay as rent constituting property taxes. If a tenant claiming that relief asks, you must sign a statement of the gross rent the tenant paid for the calendar year (rent for occupancy only, excluding charges for utilities, services, furniture or appliances you provide). Willfully giving a false statement, or willfully failing to give one in time for the tenant to file a timely claim, is a misdemeanor with a fine of up to $50 for each violation. Claims are filed with the State Tax Commissioner between July 1 and September 30 for the prior year. No West Virginia statute otherwise requires you to tell tenants how much of their rent goes to property taxes.",
    notes: "WV: The landlord shall, at the claimant's request, 'sign a statement setting forth the gross rent paid by the claimant for the particular calendar year' (W. Va. Code § 11-25-5); misdemeanor, fine 'not exceeding $50' (same). Claimant: 65 or older, domiciled in the state, gross household income of not more than $5,000 (W. Va. Code § 11-25-2(1)); 'Gross rent' (4); 'Rent constituting property taxes' means 'twelve percent of the gross rent' (8); purpose W. Va. Code § 11-25-1; filing July 1 to September 30 (W. Va. Code § 11-25-6). No general property-tax share disclosure: (WV battery c-proptax-rent (property tax and rent or tenants): 12 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (hits are art. 11-25, tax credits, family-court support and parking sections). Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
