      "No West Virginia statute protects residential tenants who organize or join a tenants' organization, or bars retaliation for it, in ordinary residential tenancies; the only such statute covers factory-built home site rentals, which this library does not cover. The eviction statute and the court's answer form treat retaliatory eviction as something a tenant can raise, but its scope is case law not checked here. The constitutional right of peaceable assembly limits government, not private landlords.",
