    ruleTypes: ["CONSTRAINED"],
    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "foreign-ownership",
    bodyText:
      "A 2025 West Virginia law, in effect since July 10, 2025, bars a prohibited foreign-party-controlled business from acquiring or owning, directly or indirectly, any interest in West Virginia real estate, and bars anyone from holding such an interest as its agent, trustee or fiduciary; the Attorney General can force a judicial sale. A prohibited foreign party includes a citizen or resident of the People's Republic of China who is not a U.S. citizen or resident alien, that government, entities they significantly control, and any government, entity or person a majority of six named state officials identifies as hostile; a business is covered if such a party owns or operates, even in part, a controlling interest (50 percent or more). The law does not say whether leasing a home to such a business gives it an interest in real estate, and it does not restrict individual foreign tenants. A person not subject to the law need not investigate whether another party is. Otherwise any alien may own land in West Virginia as if a citizen.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 37-3A-3(a)-(c) ('may not acquire or own, directly or indirectly, any interest in any real estate in this state, including mineral rights'); § 37-3A-2 (definitions; 'Controlling interest' means 'an ownership interest of 50 percent or more in the aggregate'); § 37-3A-4 (divest within six months; Attorney General action; judicial sale); § 37-3A-5(b) ('is not required to investigate'); § 37-3A-1; § 36-1-21. Effective date: Enr. Com. Sub. for H.B. 2961 (2025) (2025 W. Va. Acts ch. 120) adds §§ 37-3A-1 to 37-3A-5; the enrolled act's heading says it passed April 12, 2025, in effect 90 days from passage (July 10, 2025), while the Legislature's bill-status page says effective ninety days from passage (July 11, 2025) and its code-affected list names only §§ 37-3A-1 and -2 (enrolled act and status page read and saved 2026-10-08, WV log §1.2); the body uses July 10, 2025, the enrolled act's own date (Taylor's decision 2026-10-08, WV log §6.2); the status page's July 11 date is recorded here and flagged for the legal watch (WV log §7). Whether a leasehold is an 'interest in any real estate': Claude's reading (probably yes for a lease to a covered business), case law not searched. (WV battery foreign-own (foreign adversary ownership or leasing restrictions): 40 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (40 hits read: § 37-3A-2 on point; banking, insurance, emergency and agriculture provisions otherwise) (WV battery d-immigration-rn (immigration status or citizenship near housing or land words): 14 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205). Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
