    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "statute-of-frauds-lease-term",
    bodyText:
      "A lease of land for more than one year is not enforceable unless it, or a note or memorandum of it, is in writing and signed by the party to be charged or that party's agent, and no action may be brought on any agreement that is not to be performed within a year unless it is in a signed writing. A lease for a term of more than five years must be created by deed, and once recorded (or a memorandum of it is recorded) it is valid against the landlord's creditors and buyers. Oral leases are still rental agreements under the deposit law, and without a written lease a landlord can still recover reasonable payment for the use and occupation of the property. Electronic records and signatures satisfy these rules when both sides agreed to deal electronically.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 36-1-3 ('No contract for the sale of land, or the lease thereof for more than one year, shall be enforceable unless the contract or some note or memorandum thereof be in writing and signed by the party to be charged thereby, or by his agent'); W. Va. Code § 55-1-1(f); W. Va. Code § 36-1-1 ('for a term of more than five years'); W. Va. Code § 40-1-8 (recording; memorandum of lease); W. Va. Code § 37-6A-1(12) (rental agreement includes written or oral agreements); W. Va. Code § 37-6-9 ('recover a reasonable satisfaction for the use and occupation of lands'); § 39A-1-7(c)-(d). A one-year lease agreed long before it starts may fall under § 55-1-1(f): Claude's reading. No maximum residential lease term (WV battery d-lease-max (maximum or long lease terms (years)): 129 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (129 hits read: public leases, bonds and criminal penalties; § 36-1-1 and § 40-1-8 as above); topic `lease-term-limitation` answered here. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
