    bodyText:
      "Several West Virginia rules apply only if, or unless, the lease says so. You may take late charges from the security deposit only if they are reasonable and specified in the rental agreement, and other damages or charges only as the rental agreement provides. A pet fee or application fee is outside the deposit rules only if you and the tenant expressly agree in writing that it is nonrefundable. The deposit law's definitions say you may use submetering, energy allocation equipment or a ratio utility billing system if the rental agreement so provides, so put any such arrangement in the lease. Rent is reasonably reduced after a fire or other casualty unless the lease otherwise provides, and rent ends or is reduced when land is taken by eminent domain unless the lease expressly provides otherwise. The statutory notice periods for ending a periodic tenancy do not apply where a special agreement fixes another notice period or none. A lease that gives you greater repair duties than the habitability statute controls. Terms waiving deposit rights or a deceased tenant's estate's right to end the lease are unenforceable or void (see Lease Terms West Virginia Voids).",
