      "West Virginia has no statewide landlord or rental registration or licensing requirement. Cities may by ordinance set up a registration, with fees, for buildings found uninhabitable under the local building code and a registration and maintenance program for vacant buildings. A statute in the Municipal Home Rule Program section also says municipalities may not prohibit or effectively limit the rental of a property, or regulate the duration, frequency or location of rentals, and may regulate activities that arise from rental use only if the regulation applies uniformly to all properties, rented or not. Whether that reaches every city, and whether it rules out a registration or inspection ordinance that applies only to rentals, is unsettled (court decisions were not checked). Local rental registration or licensing ordinances were not checked; ask the city or county where the property is located.",
    notes: "WV: Confirmed absent: (WV battery d-registration (rental registration, licensing or landlord registry): 5 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (5 hits read: § 8-12-16a uninhabitable property, § 8-12-16c vacant buildings, § 16B-5-6 facility licensing, §§ 30-40-26 and 30-27-19 professional licensing). W. Va. Code § 8-12-16a(a); § 8-12-16c(a). W. Va. Code § 8-1-5a(k) ('Municipalities may not prohibit or effectively limit the rental of a property, in whole or in part, or regulate the duration, frequency, or location of such rental, in whole or in part'; 'A municipality may regulate activities that arise when a property is used as a rental: Provided, That such regulation applies uniformly to all properties, without regard to whether such properties are used as a rental'); § 8-1-5a(b) (Home Rule participants must update their ordinances to comply with subsection (k)). Whether (k) binds every municipality or only Home Rule participants, and whether a rental-only registration or inspection ordinance 'effectively' limits rental or fails the uniformity proviso: Claude's reading (unsettled), case law not searched. Lead's `rental-registration` battery failed its positive and is not cited. Local ordinances not searched (rule 3). Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
