    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute regulates automatic renewal clauses in residential leases. Without one, a lease for a fixed term ends on its end date with no notice needed; a year-to-year tenancy ends on written notice at least three months before the end of a year; and a shorter periodic tenancy ends on like notice or on notice of one full period before the end of a period (give it in writing). A special agreement in the lease can fix another notice period or none. Some rules turn on when a lease is entered into or renewed (for example, a deceased tenant's estate may end a lease entered into or renewed on or after July 1, 2012), so treat each renewal as a new lease date. West Virginia's subscription-cancellation statute covers correspondence courses, occupational courses and magazine subscriptions, not leases.",
