    topicKey: "hoa",
    bodyText:
      "If the unit is in a condominium, cooperative or planned community under West Virginia's Uniform Common Interest Ownership Act, the declaration, bylaws and association rules govern leasing, and no provision found sets a fee for leasing a unit or lets the association collect rent from your tenant. An amendment changing the uses to which a unit is restricted needs the unanimous consent of the unit owners unless the Act expressly permits otherwise; whether a new leasing restriction is such a change is not settled by the text. The association may levy reasonable fines for violations of the declaration, bylaws and rules after notice and an opportunity to be heard; the Act does not say whether it may fine a tenant directly. The declaration may give lessees the vote on specified matters. For a community created before the Act took effect, generally only listed parts of the Act apply, and the unanimous-consent rule is not among them; but an older community may amend its declaration under the Act, and an older condominium is also governed by the earlier condominium law (not reviewed here), so check how its declaration may be amended. Read the declaration, bylaws and rules before leasing a unit.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 36B-2-117(d) ('or the uses to which any unit is restricted, in the absence of unanimous consent of the unit owners'); § 36B-3-102(a)(1), (11) ('after notice and an opportunity to be heard, levy reasonable fines'); § 36B-3-110(c); conversion buildings § 36B-4-112 (`edu-sale-or-management-change-wv`); preexisting communities § 36B-1-204(a), (d) and amendments under the Act § 36B-1-206(a) (older condominiums under chapter 36A, not read in full). (WV battery d-hoa-lease (association, declaration or bylaw provisions on leasing or tenants (common interest ownership chapters)): 16 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic); scope NARROW: chapters 36A, 36B, 36C only) (narrow: chapters 36A to 36C; 16 hits read: declarations, voting, assessments and liens; no unit-leasing fee or rent collection). Leasing limits as use restrictions: Claude's reading, case law not searched. Shared `hoa-compliance` tagged. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
