    topicKey: "cannabis",
    bodyText:
      "West Virginia allows only medical cannabis, for certified patients and caregivers with a valid identification card, and only in forms such as pills, oils, topicals, tinctures, liquids, dermal patches and forms for vaporization or nebulization. Smoking medical cannabis is unlawful, and so is growing it without a permit; other marijuana possession remains a crime. The Medical Cannabis Act protects patients from arrest, prosecution or penalty, or denial of any right or privilege, solely for lawful use, but says nothing about rental housing. A lease may prohibit smoking and growing; whether you may bar a patient's lawful non-smoked use, or refuse to rent to a patient, is not settled by the text (court decisions were not checked).",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 16A-3-2(a)(1)-(3); § 16A-3-3(b)(1), (3) ('Smoke medical cannabis'; 'Grow medical cannabis unless the grower/processor has received a permit'); § 16A-15-4(a) ('denied any right or privilege, including civil penalty or disciplinary action by a state licensing board or commission, solely for lawful use of medical cannabis'), (b) (employment only); § 16A-15-1; marihuana is Schedule I (W. Va. Code § 60A-2-204) and possession is unlawful (W. Va. Code § 60A-4-401(c)). (WV battery cannabis (cannabis or marijuana): 96 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (96 hits read: chapter 16A, chapter 60A, hemp and banking; no rental housing provision). Reach of § 16A-15-4(a) to landlords: Claude's reading, case law not searched. Shared `smoking-policy` tagged. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
