      "No West Virginia statute requires a landlord who holds tenants' deposits personally to keep them in a separate or escrow account, at any particular bank, or to pay interest on them. A licensed real estate broker (including a broker acting as your property manager) who holds deposits for you rather than passing them to you at once must keep them in a federally insured trust fund account, not mixed with the broker's own money, that does not earn interest unless a Real Estate Commission rule allows it. You must keep itemized records of every deduction you make from a tenant's deposit because the tenant did not comply with the lease, for one year after the tenancy ends. Within 72 hours after a written request, during normal business hours, you must either let the tenant (or the tenant's authorized agent or attorney) inspect that tenant's record of deductions or, at your option, give them a copy.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 37-6A-3(1)-(2) (records of deductions 'which the landlord has made by reason of a tenant's noncompliance with the rental agreement'). No account or bank rule for a landlord holding its own deposits (WV battery deposit-account (separate, escrow or trust account for deposits): 15 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery deposit-account-nc (separate, escrow or trust account for deposits (no context limb)): 71 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205): the one hit on point is the broker trust-account statute. A broker who does not immediately deliver funds 'shall maintain and reconcile one or more trust fund accounts in a recognized financial institution and shall place all funds therein' (W. Va. Code § 30-40-18(a)), including 'security deposits, rental receipts' (§ 30-40-18(b)); federally insured (§ 30-40-18(c)); 'No trust fund account may earn interest or any other form of income, unless specifically authorized by commission rule' (§ 30-40-18(e)); no commingling (§ 30-40-18(f)). 'Property management' includes 'collecting or holding security deposits on behalf of the property owner' (W. Va. Code § 30-40-4); the licensing article does not apply to 'Any person acting on his or her own behalf as owner or lessor of real estate' or to some employees and single-owner agents (W. Va. Code § 30-40-5(c)(1), (2), (8)). Real Estate Commission rules not read (round 1 independent check). No interest rule (WV battery deposit-interest (interest on security deposits): 22 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery deposit-interest-nc (interest on security deposits (no context limb)): 184 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (topic `security-deposit-interest` answered in `edu-no-deposit-interest-wv`). Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
