      "Whoever holds the landlord's interest in the property when a tenancy ends is bound by West Virginia's deposit rules and must return any deposit the original landlord received that is owed to the tenant. That is true however the interest was acquired or transferred, whether or not the deposit was handed over, and whatever the seller and buyer agreed between themselves. A buyer should therefore account for tenants' deposits at closing. If a tenant has an assignee or subtenant, you may hold a deposit from only one of them.",
