      "West Virginia does not cap pet deposits, pet fees or pet rent. A refundable pet deposit is a security deposit, held and returned under the deposit rules. A pet fee is outside those rules only if you and the tenant expressly agree in writing that it is nonrefundable; use the lease's Nonrefundable Fees terms to do that. Monthly pet rent is rent (this library's reading). You may not charge a pet fee, deposit or other pet charge for an assistance animal a tenant needs because of a disability.",
