    topicKey: "guest-rights",
    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute gives tenants or their guests rights that limit a lease's guest terms, apart from fair housing law. Under the Stop Squatters Act, police removal is only for an unauthorized person unlawfully occupying the property, and not for a member of the tenant's immediate family, so a guest the tenant has authorized, or a member of the tenant's immediate family, cannot be removed under that process; whether a former guest whose permission has ended can be is not settled. A guest problem is handled under the lease and, if necessary, the court eviction process against the tenant.",
