    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute regulates smoking or vaping in private rental housing or limits a lease's no-smoking terms, so the lease governs; local board of health rules and ordinances, which were not read, may add limits. West Virginia's cannabis law is a medical program: use of medical cannabis is lawful only as that act allows, and the act makes it unlawful to smoke medical cannabis. Medical cannabis may be dispensed as pills, oils, topical forms, tinctures, liquids, dermal patches and forms for vaporization or nebulization, but not in dry leaf or plant form unless the state bureau's rules allow it. The act says a patient or caregiver may not be denied any right or privilege solely for lawful use, but it says nothing about leases or landlords, so whether a lease may bar lawful medical use other than smoking, such as vaping, is unsettled; a ban on smoking cannabis matches state law.",
