      "West Virginia has no statute giving a tenant rights because of domestic violence, sexual assault or stalking, such as a right to end the lease early, to have the locks changed or to avoid eviction, so there is no statutory list of documents a tenant must give you. Court orders can still affect a tenancy: a family court protective order may grant the victim possession of the residence the parties shared and order the abuser to stay away from the victim's residence, though it cannot affect title to real property, and a magistrate's personal safety order may order a person not to enter the petitioner's residence. Follow any such order you are shown. Federal housing program rules were not reviewed.",
