    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "rent-escalation",
    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute addresses a lease term that lets you raise rent during a fixed term, and none forbids one. Without such a term, the rent stated in a fixed-term lease applies for the whole term. If you want the right to raise rent mid-lease, the lease must say so, including when an increase can take effect, how much notice you will give and how the new rent is set. This library offers an optional Mid-Term Rent Increase clause: you give at least 30 days' written notice of the new rent, and the tenant may instead end the lease without a fee before the increase takes effect.",
    notes: "WV: Confirmed absent: (WV battery f-rent-midterm (rent or term changes during a fixed-term lease): 13 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (13 hits, run without a tenancy limb: public-land and campus leases, municipal charter procedures, sign permits, contract modification under the Uniform Trust Code, salaries during a term of office, the escalation-of-interest bar for mortgage loans in W. Va. Code § 47-6-5(c), and the factory-built home site written-agreement rule § 37-15-3 (out of scope); none governs residential rent) (WV battery f-rent-increase (rent increases (notice, limits, frequency)): 5 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205). That a fixed-term lease's rent binds both sides unless the lease provides otherwise is Claude's reading of contract law, not a statute; case law not searched. Optional clause `rent-increase-midterm-wv` (30 days' written notice, tenant may leave without a fee instead; WV log §6.1). Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
