    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "algorithmic-rent-setting",
    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute specifically regulates using software or an algorithm to set rent. West Virginia's antitrust act does apply to renting homes: it makes unlawful any contract, combination or conspiracy in restraint of trade, including an agreement between two or more persons for the purpose or with the effect of fixing, controlling or maintaining a market price, rate or fee. Anyone injured in their business or property may sue for three times their damages plus attorney's fees and costs. Set your rents independently and don't share nonpublic rent data with competitors; federal antitrust law also applies but was not read here.",
    notes: "WV: Confirmed absent (algorithm-specific rule): (WV battery f-algorithm (algorithmic or software rent pricing): 0 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 2 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery f-algorithm-nc (algorithmic or software rent pricing (no context limb)): 8 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 2 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (8 hits: tax confidentiality, school computer-science courses, blockchain consensus algorithms, electronic-transaction and funds-transfer definitions; none on rent) (WV battery f-algorithm-ev (coordinated or recommended rent levels (everyday rerun)): 3 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 2 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery f-algorithm-ev-nc (coordinated or recommended rent levels (everyday rerun) (no context limb)): 3 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 2 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (3 hits: leasehold common interest communities, rent payable in kind, trust powers; none on point). Antitrust: 'Every contract, combination in the form of trust or otherwise, or conspiracy in restraint of trade or commerce in this state shall be unlawful.' (W. Va. Code § 47-18-3(a)); per se list: 'for the purpose or with the effect of fixing, controlling, or maintaining the market price, rate or fee of any commodity or service' (W. Va. Code § 47-18-3(b)(1)(A)). Reach: commodity means 'any kind of real or personal property' (W. Va. Code § 47-18-2(c)); service includes 'sale, rental, leasing or licensing for use' (W. Va. Code § 47-18-2(d)). Treble damages, attorney fees, filing fees and costs: W. Va. Code § 47-18-9. Whether a shared pricing tool is a 'contract, combination or conspiracy' is case law, not searched. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
