    topicKey: "required-fees",
    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute requires a residential lease to list every fee or sets a notice period for adding one; the rule that a landlord may not collect a fee not listed in the rental agreement applies only to factory-built home sites. Several West Virginia rules still turn on the lease's words: you may apply the deposit to late charges only if they are specified in the rental agreement, and to other charges only as the rental agreement provides; a pet or application fee is outside the deposit only if the tenant expressly agrees in writing that it is nonrefundable; and, if the consumer debt-collection law applies, a fee added because of a default or for collection, such as a late fee, returned-check fee or collection cost, can be collected only if both the agreement and a statute or regulation expressly authorize it. Rent, reimbursement of an actual cost the lease makes the tenant's, and the price of an option the tenant chooses, such as an early-termination fee, are part of what the tenant agreed to pay. List every fee in the lease and add one mid-term only with the tenant's written agreement. You may not charge any fee or deposit for an assistance animal.",
    notes: "WV: Lot-rent rule (out of scope): a factory-built home site landlord may not demand or collect 'Any fee which is not listed in the rental agreement' (W. Va. Code § 37-15-5(a)(1)). Residential tenancies: no counterpart (WV battery f-required-fees (fees that must be listed in a lease or disclosed before signing): 11 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery f-required-fees-nc (fees that must be listed in a lease or disclosed before signing (no context limb)): 19 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (hits: art. 37-15 lot rentals, rent-to-own goods § 46B-3-8, self-storage insurance § 33-12-38, insurance, mineral and pore-space leases, mortgage-loan fees, prize promotions, and art. 37-6A itself; none requires a residential lease to list fees). Deposit: W. Va. Code § 37-6A-2(b)(1) ('specified in the rental agreement'), (5) ('To other damages or charges as provided in the rental agreement'); W. Va. Code § 37-6A-1(14) ('Provided, That the parties expressly agree, in writing, that a pet fee or application fee is nonrefundable'). Debt collection: W. Va. Code § 46A-2-128(d) (reach: Claude's reading, see `edu-collection-fee-wv`); the split between charges that are the tenant's contractual obligation and 'incidental' charges added because of default or for collection is the library-wide reading of (d) (Claude's reading, case law not searched); statutory authority exists for a late fee (W. Va. Code § 37-6A-2(b)(1)) and a returned-check fee up to $25 (W. Va. Code § 61-3-39e). Assistance animals: a request may not be 'conditioned on payment of a fee or deposit' (W. Va. Code § 16B-18-5(f)(10)(D)); § 16B-18-5 does not reach an owner-occupied rooming house with no more than four rooms for rent (W. Va. Code § 16B-18-4(a)), a carve-out too narrow for the body. The mid-term consent advice is Claude's reading of contract law. Fee disclosure and plain language: `edu-no-fee-transparency-wv`; `nonrefundable-fees-wv`. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
