    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "rent-receipts",
    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute requires a residential landlord to give a receipt for each rent payment, even rent paid in cash. One narrow exception: if a tenant aged 65 or older, with household income of no more than $5,000, claims West Virginia's senior citizens' homestead tax relief and asks, you must sign a statement of the gross rent the tenant paid for the year; willfully failing to do so, or willfully giving a false or fraudulent statement, is a misdemeanor with a fine of up to $50. The state's consumer-credit receipt rule covers consumer credit sales, consumer loans and consumer leases of goods, not leases of homes. Giving a written receipt for every cash payment and keeping a rent ledger is still good practice, and helps if the amount owed is disputed in court.",
    notes: "WV: Confirmed absent: (WV battery f-rent-receipt (receipts for rent or other payments): 15 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery f-rent-receipt-nc (receipts for rent or other payments (no context limb)): 199 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery rent-receipt (receipts for rent or cash payments): 4 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (15 hits with the tenancy limb: tax, banking and trust sections, and two receipt rules that do not reach home rentals: W. Va. Code § 46A-2-114(1) ('a written receipt for each payment by coin or currency on an obligation pursuant to a consumer credit sale, consumer lease or consumer loan'), where a consumer lease is defined as a lease of goods (W. Va. Code § 46A-1-102(14)(a)), and the rent-to-own dealer rule § 46B-5-2(a)). The receipt batteries look for the word receipt; the senior-renter statement duty was found by the independent check: 'The claimant's landlord shall at the claimant's request sign a statement setting forth the gross rent paid by the claimant for the particular calendar year.' (W. Va. Code § 11-25-5), with a fine 'not exceeding $50' for a willfully false statement or a willful failure (same section); a claimant is a person 'sixty-five years of age or older' with gross household income of not more than $5,000 (W. Va. Code § 11-25-2(1)); the relief is for low-income citizens aged 65 or over (W. Va. Code § 11-25-1). Also cited in `edu-no-payment-method-rule-wv`. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
