    bodyText:
      "In an action for rent, West Virginia allows interest as on other contracts. The court may award prejudgment interest on special or liquidated damages; if the obligation is based on a written agreement, it bears interest until judgment at the rate the agreement sets, and otherwise at a statutory rate of two percentage points above the Fifth Federal Reserve District secondary discount rate in effect on January 2 of the year the claim arose, but not less than 4% or more than 9% a year. A judgment then bears simple interest at the rate figured the same way for the year it is entered. The general legal rate of interest is 6% a year. This library's lease sets no contract interest rate.",
    notes: "WV: 'In any action for rent, or for such use and occupation, interest shall be allowed as on other contracts.' (W. Va. Code § 37-6-9). Prejudgment: W. Va. Code § 56-6-31(b) ('If an obligation is based upon a written agreement, the obligation bears prejudgment interest at the rate and terms set forth in the written agreement until the date the judgment or decree is entered'), (b)(1) (two points above the Fifth Federal Reserve District secondary discount rate on January 2 of the accrual year; 'may not exceed nine percent per annum or be less than four percent per annum'; the Supreme Court's administrative office publishes the rate). Post-judgment: § 56-6-31(a), (c). Legal rate: W. Va. Code § 47-6-5(a) ($6 upon $100 a year); written contracts 'for the loan or forbearance of money' capped at $8 upon $100 (§ 47-6-5(b)); whether overdue rent is a forbearance is Claude's reading, case law not searched. If the debt-collection rules reach rent, interest is 'incidental' and needs authority in the agreement and a statute (W. Va. Code § 46A-2-128(d)); § 37-6-9 supplies it for interest as on other contracts, while interest beyond that is the incidental charge without statutory authority under the library-wide reading of (d) (Claude's reading, case law not searched; whether § 56-6-31(b) itself authorizes a contract rate is unsettled). (WV battery f-unpaid-interest (interest on unpaid rent or damages): 31 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (31 hits; the landlord-tenant hits either add interest to rent arrears in recovery, relief or redemption (§§ 37-6-9, 37-6-17, 37-6-20, 37-6-21, 37-6-23, 37-6-26) or use interest for an estate in land (§§ 37-6-11, 37-6-29); none sets another rate). No interest clause offered: WV log §6.1. Case law not searched. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
