    topicKey: "holding-deposit",
    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute specifically regulates a holding deposit taken before a lease is signed. The deposit law treats money, however labeled, paid to be considered as a tenant as an application fee, and any refundable money given to secure performance of a rental agreement as a security deposit; prepaid rent is neither. Unless you and the applicant expressly agree in writing that a payment is a nonrefundable application fee, treat a holding deposit as a refundable security deposit, applied and returned under the deposit rules. Put in writing what the payment is for, whether it will be credited to the deposit or first month's rent, and when and how it will be refunded if no lease is signed.",
    notes: "WV: Confirmed absent (holding-deposit rule): (WV battery f-holding-deposit (holding deposit or money paid before a lease is signed): 3 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery f-holding-deposit-nc (holding deposit or money paid before a lease is signed (no context limb)): 9 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (hits: art. 37-6A, renewal of leases for persons under disability § 37-1-1, a military-training definition, and ejectment and unlawful detainer procedure; none regulates pre-lease deposits). Application fee: 'any deposit of money, however denominated, which is paid by a tenant to a landlord, lessor or agent of a landlord for the purpose of being considered as a tenant for a dwelling unit' (W. Va. Code § 37-6A-1(2)). Security deposit: 'any refundable deposit of money that is furnished by a tenant to a landlord to secure the performance of the terms and conditions of a rental agreement' and 'A security deposit does not include prepaid rent' (W. Va. Code § 37-6A-1(14)); a rental agreement may be 'written (including an electronic record as defined by paragraph (7), section two, article one, chapter thirty-nine-a of the code) or oral, express or implied' (W. Va. Code § 37-6A-1(12)). Which label fits a particular holding deposit is Claude's reading. `edu-application-fees-wv`; `nonrefundable-fees-wv`. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
