      "No West Virginia statute authorizes or regulates a fee or insurance product offered in place of a security deposit. Under the deposit law, any refundable money a tenant gives to secure performance or cover damage is a security deposit, while a nonrefundable fee is neither a deposit nor rent, so a genuinely nonrefundable fee in lieu of a deposit falls outside the deposit rules. If you offer one, say in writing that it is nonrefundable and whether it limits the tenant's liability for damage. Deposit insurance and surety products are governed by insurance law, not read here. This library offers no fee-in-lieu clause.",
