    topicKey: "assistance-animal-accommodation",
    bodyText:
      "Under West Virginia's Fair Housing Act, an assistance animal is any service, therapy or support animal weighing less than 150 pounds, with or without specific training or certification, that works, provides assistance or performs tasks for a person with a disability, or provides emotional support that alleviates one or more identified symptoms or effects of the disability. A request for one is a request for a reasonable accommodation to your animal rules: it may not be unreasonably denied or delayed, or conditioned on a fee, deposit or other terms that apply to pets. These rules reach small landlords too; the exemptions are narrow (see the fair housing row). An animal of 150 pounds or more is outside the state definition, but the general duty to make reasonable accommodations, and federal law (not read here), may still require you to consider the request.",
    notes: "WV: Definition: 'any service, therapy or support animal, weighing less than 150 pounds, with or without specific training or certification, that works, provides assistance, or performs tasks for the benefit of a person with a disability, or provides emotional support that alleviate one or more identified symptoms or effects of a person's disability' (W. Va. Code § 16B-18-3(p)). Animal rules 'are subject to the reasonable accommodation requirements' (W. Va. Code § 16B-18-5(f)(10)); 'A request for a reasonable accommodation may not be unreasonably denied, conditioned on payment of a fee or deposit or other terms and conditions applied to applicants or residents with pets, and a response may not be unreasonably delayed.' (W. Va. Code § 16B-18-5(f)(10)(D)). Coverage: the familial-status exemptions in § 16B-18-4(a)(1)-(2) apply 'Solely for the purposes of familial status'; an owner-occupied rooming house with no more than four rooms for rent is outside § 16B-18-5 (W. Va. Code § 16B-18-4(a)). That a 150-pound or heavier animal may still need consideration under § 16B-18-5(f)(3)(B) is Claude's reading. Documentation, denial grounds and modifications: `edu-disability-accommodation-wv`; exemptions: `edu-fair-housing-wv`. Shared `assistance-animal-accommodation` (tagged) is more generous than the state definition (no weight limit), which is lawful. Federal law not read. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
