    topicKey: "service-animal-misrepresentation",
    bodyText:
      "In West Virginia it is a misdemeanor to falsely claim that an animal is a service animal, or that you are blind or have a disability, to obtain the rights the state's White Cane law gives in public places, public transportation, hotels, lodging places and other places of public accommodation. The penalty is a fine of up to $200, up to 10 days in jail, or both, rising to $1,000, 30 days, or both for a repeat offense. That law does not by its terms reach a request to keep an assistance animal in a rental home, and no West Virginia statute penalizes a false assistance-animal request in housing. Handle housing requests under the fair housing rules, which let you ask for documentation from a professional treatment provider of the disability-related need.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 5-15-9(a)-(c) ('Any person who falsely represents that an animal is a service animal in order to obtain any right or privilege protected by the provisions of §5-15-4 of this code is guilty of a misdemeanor'); penalty 'fined not more than $200 or confined in jail for not more than 10 days, or both fined and confined' (W. Va. Code § 5-15-9), repeat $1,000 or 30 days, or both (c); the rights are in W. Va. Code § 5-15-4(a) (highways, streets, public buildings, public facilities and other public places) and (b)-(c) (public conveyances, 'hotels, lodging places', places of public accommodation and other places to which the general public is invited); service animal: W. Va. Code § 5-15-3(c) (individually trained). Whether a rental dwelling is a place 'to which the general public is invited' is Claude's reading (it reads as not); whether a rooming house that takes in members of the public is a 'lodging places' establishment under § 5-15-4(b) is unsettled (Claude's reading, case law not searched). Housing: no penalty (WV battery f-misrep-animal (misrepresenting a service or assistance animal or a disability): 1 hit, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (1 hit: § 5-15-9) (WV battery f-misrep-animal-housing (false assistance-animal request in housing): 0 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery f-misrep-animal-housing-nc (false assistance-animal request in housing (no context limb)): 2 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (0 hits with housing context; without it § 5-15-9 and an insurance-policy provision). Documentation: 'a person with a disability may be required to submit documentation, from a professional treatment provider, of the disability related need for the assistance animal' (W. Va. Code § 16B-18-5(f)(10)(A)); `edu-disability-accommodation-wv`. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
