    topicKey: "ev-charging",
    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute gives tenants a right to install an electric vehicle charger or requires landlords to provide charging. A tenant who wants a charger needs your consent under the lease's alterations terms; if you agree, put the installation, electricity cost, insurance and removal at move-out in writing.",
