    verificationStatus: "VERIFIED",
    topicKey: "storage-space",
    bodyText:
      "West Virginia's Self-Service Storage Lien Act gives operators of self-service storage facilities a lien on stored property and a sale procedure, but it works through a storage rental agreement that must contain the statements the Act requires. Unlike the state's storage-insurance statute, the lien Act does not expressly exclude storage rented with a home, so whether it reaches a storage unit you rent to a tenant with an apartment is not settled by statute. This library's storage clause does not invoke the Act. Treat belongings a tenant leaves in a storage space like other property left behind at the end of a tenancy.",
    notes: "WV: Lien Act scope: a self-service storage facility is 'any real property used for renting or leasing individual storage spaces in which the occupants themselves customarily store and remove their own personal property' (W. Va. Code § 38-14-2(8)); 'An occupant may not use a self-service storage facility for residential purposes.' (W. Va. Code § 38-14-7(c)); lien and required statements (W. Va. Code § 38-14-3(a), (c)); late fee (§ 38-14-4); sale after 60 days in default with notice (§ 38-14-5). Insurance statute excludes 'other than storage spaces which are leased or rented as an incident to the lease or rental of residential property or dwelling units' (W. Va. Code § 33-12-38(a)(7)); the lien Act has no such words (WV battery f-storage (storage spaces rented with a dwelling): 6 hits, control 0; known positives passed (2 real sections, 0 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (6 hits: § 33-12-38 and art. 38-14). Whether the Act reaches a landlord's tenant storage is Claude's reading, case law not searched. Left-behind property: `edu-abandoned-property-wv`, `edu-post-eviction-property-wv`. Shared `storage-space-ks-oh-ca` tagged. Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
