    bodyText:
      "No West Virginia statute requires an out-of-state landlord to appoint an agent in West Virginia. But a nonresident who has an interest in, uses or possesses real property in West Virginia is treated as having appointed the Secretary of State to receive process in a circuit court case arising from it; the Secretary of State mails the papers to your out-of-state address by registered or certified mail, and a default judgment may be entered if you don't appear and defend within 30 days. Keep your address current and consider naming a local manager to receive notices. Under the deposit law, a managing agent who does not disclose the owner's name is treated as the landlord.",
    notes: "WV: W. Va. Code § 56-3-33(a)(6) ('Having an interest in, using, or possessing real property in this state'), (a) (Secretary of State as attorney 'in any action or proceeding against him or her, in any circuit court in this state'), (b) (cause of action must arise from the act), (c) (service; 'If any defendant served with summons and complaint fails to appear and defend within 30 days of service, judgment by default may be rendered against him or her at any time thereafter'), (f) (cumulative). By its words the section covers circuit court actions; deposit suits may also be brought in magistrate court (W. Va. Code § 37-6A-5(b)) (Claude's reading). Landlord includes 'a managing agent of the premises who fails to disclose the name of such owner or lessor' (W. Va. Code § 37-6A-1(5)). Confirmed absent (agent requirement): (WV battery f-nonresident-landlord (nonresident landlord or owner agent for service or notices): 0 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery f-nonresident-landlord-nc (nonresident landlord or owner agent for service or notices (no context limb)): 0 hits, control 0; known positives passed (0 real sections, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (0 hits) (WV battery f-nonresident-landlord-ev (agent named in a lease for notices or process (everyday rerun)): 34 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (WV battery f-nonresident-landlord-ev-nc (agent named in a lease for notices or process (everyday rerun) (no context limb)): 84 hits, control 0; known positives passed (1 real section, 1 synthetic); scope CODE 31329, CONST 205) (hits: license applications naming owners, demolition notices, art. 37-6A; none requires a landlord's agent). Boundary: the West Virginia Code and Constitution were searched; legislative rules, case law and local ordinances were not. Read section-open 2026-10-05 from the saved, hash-matched corpus of the whole West Virginia Code (code.wvlegislature.gov, every article's official text with section pages for the sections the article view did not head; currency from each section page's Bill History and the 2024-2026 signed-bill \"code affected\" lists) and the West Virginia Constitution (WV log §1). Rule 15: written section-open.",
