    topicKey: "rent-tax",
    bodyText:
      "Counties and cities may impose a hotel occupancy tax on hotel rooms, which include boarding houses, condominiums, cabins, lodges and tourist homes where the public can rent sleeping accommodations. The tax does not apply to sleeping accommodations rented month-to-month or for 30 days or longer from the start at a boarding house, condominium, cabin, tourist home, apartment or home. Where it applies, the operator collects it from the guest, states it separately on bills and may not advertise that it will absorb it; if you rent through a booking platform that meets the statute's sales thresholds, the platform must collect and remit it for you. No West Virginia statute expressly taxes ordinary long-term residential rent. If you rent short-term, ask your county or city and the State Tax Department whether occupancy tax or consumers sales tax applies.",
